elevant fields; don''t dump raw rows verbatim.\n- Do not show the SQL you ran unless the user explicitly asks for it.\n- If a query returns nothing, say so plainly and suggest what to check.\n- For follow-up questions that reference a customer, vehicle, or result from earlier in the conversation, run a SQL query to fetch that entity''s full details (especially their id) if you need them to answer precisely. Use names or other identifiers visible in the conversation history to look them up.\n- When looking for matching inventory, search broadly: by vehicle segment (SUV, sedan, truck, etc.), price range, or a group of similar makes \u2014 not only by the exact brand the customer currently drives. A customer with a Hyundai Tucson likely fits any compact/mid-size SUV.\n- For complex questions, run multiple queries in sequence: gather context first, then query the target table with the details you found.\n- When an inventory query returns nothing for a narrow filter, widen the search (drop a constraint, try adjacent segments or a price range) before concluding nothing is available."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Hi! Ask me anything about your CRM data.\n\nExamples:\n\u2022 \"How many customers haven''t been contacted in 60 days?\"\n\u2022 \"Which leases end in the next 3 months?\"\n\u2022 \"What Toyotas do we have in stock under $30k?\""}, {"role": "user", "content": "any customer''s lease or finance ending soon?"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Yes \u2014 1 customer has a lease/finance ending in the next 90 days.\n\n- Priya Sharma\n  - Vehicle: 2020 Hyundai Tucson\n  - Type: lease\n  - End date: 2026-06-30\n  - Email: priya.sharma@hotmail.com\n  - Phone: 604-555-0104\n\nIf you want, I can also check a wider window like 6 months or break it out by lease vs finance."}, {"role": "user", "content": "which inventory car might fit her?"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I\u2019m not seeing any available inventory that\u2019s an obvious fit for Priya right now.\n\n- No available Hyundai/Kia matches\n- I also don\u2019t see any broader mainstream-brand options in stock from the set I checked\n\nYou may want to check:\n- whether current inventory has been updated\n- whether sold/reserved units should also be considered\n- whether she\u2019d be open to a different body style or price range\n\nIf you want, I can next:\n- search all available inventory regardless of brand\n- look for similar SUVs specifically\n- include reserved inventory too"}, {"role": "user", "content": "search inventory regardless of brand"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Available inventory across all brands is very limited right now \u2014 9 cars, all Volkswagen.\n\nBest potential fits for Priya if she wants to stay in a similar practical daily-driver category:\n- 2025 Volkswagen Taos S\n  - $24,995\n  - Compact SUV\n- 2025 Volkswagen Tiguan S\n  - $29,495\n  - Larger SUV\n- 2025 Volkswagen ID.4 Standard\n  - $38,995\n  - Electric SUV\n\nOther available options:\n- 2025 Volkswagen Jetta S \u2014 $21,990\n- 2025 Volkswagen Golf Base \u2014 $25,990\n- 2025 Volkswagen GTI S \u2014 $32,895\n- 2025 Volkswagen Atlas S \u2014 $36,995\n- 2025 Volkswagen Golf R Base \u2014 $45,640\n- 2025 Volkswagen Arteon 2.0T \u2014 $45,995\n\nFor someone coming out of a Hyundai Tucson lease, the Taos or Tiguan are probably the closest fit.\n\nIf you want, I can narrow this to:\n- SUVs only\n- under a target monthly/payment price\n- closest match specifically to a Tucson"}, {"role": "user", "content": "write an email to remind her in Inbox"}], "tools": [{"type": "function", "function": {"name": "query_db", "description": "Run a single read-only SQL SELECT statement against the CRM database and get the matching rows back. Use this whenever the user asks about their customers, cars, interactions, inventory, outreach rules, or email drafts.", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"sql": {"type": "string", "description": "One SELECT statement in PostgreSQL dialect. No INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE/DDL."}}, "required": ["sql"]}}}], "tool_choice": "auto"}', '{"choices": [{"finish_reason": "stop", "index": 0, "message": {"content": "I can help draft the message, but I can\u2019t create or save it in Inbox from here.\n\nPlease use the Add Customer/Edit Customer or the email workflow agent to place it in Inbox.\n\nSuggested email:\n\nSubject: Your Hyundai Tucson lease is ending soon\n\nHi Priya,\n\nI wanted to reach out because your Hyundai Tucson lease is coming up soon on June 30.\n\nIf you\u2019re starting to think about next steps, I\u2019d be happy to help you review your options. We currently have a few vehicles that could be a good fit if you\u2019d like to stay in a similar SUV, including the Volkswagen Taos, Tiguan, and ID.4.\n\nIf you\u2019d like, I can help you compare:\n- lease renewal or replacement options\n- compact vs. mid-size SUV choices\n- pricing and availability based on your preferences\n\nLet me know what you\u2019re hoping for in your next vehicle, and I can put together a few options for you.\n\nBest,\n[Your Name]\n\nIf you want, I can also make this:\n- shorter and more casual\n- more sales-focused\n- personalized with the assigned rep\u2019s name", "role": "assistant"}}], "created": 1781182412, "id": "chatcmpl-32f8654d-f4c9-4562-8b9b-ae8a9", "model": "gpt-5.4", "object": "chat.completion", "usage": {"completion_tokens": 231, "prompt_tokens": 1311, "total_tokens": 1542}}', '2026-06-11 12:53:32.871432+00');
INSERT INTO public.llm_request_logs (id, url, model, input, output, created_at) VALUES (11, 'https://www.baicai.chat/v1/chat/completions', '[Azure]gpt-5.4', '{"model": "[Azure]gpt-5.4", "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are the data assistant for a car dealership CRM, chatting with Admin.\nToday''s date is 2026-06-11.\n\nYou answer questions about CRM data by calling the query_db tool with read-only SQL.\nYou can also compose email drafts by calling the compose_email_draft tool.\n\nTables you can query (PostgreSQL):\n\ncustomers(id, assigned_sales_id, full_name, email, phone, note, last_contacted_at, created_at, updated_at)\ncustomer_car(id, customer_id, make, model, year, ownership_type, lease_end_date, is_primary, created_at, updated_at)\n  - ownership_type is one of: ''own'', ''lease'', ''finance''\ninteractions(id, customer_id, sales_id, channel, summary, contacted_at, created_at)\n  - channel is one of: ''call'', ''text'', ''email'', ''in-person''\ninventory(id, make, model, year, trim, mileage, price, vin, status, features, notes, added_at)\n  - status is one of: ''available'', ''sold'', ''reserved''\noutreach_rules(id, sales_id, name, rule_text, compiled_filter, cadence_days, active, email_type, custom_template, created_at)\nemail_drafts(id, sales_id, customer_id, rule_id, subject, body, status, created_at, approved_at)\n  - status is one of: ''pending'', ''approved'', ''dismissed''\nsample_messages(id, sales_id, channel, raw_content, label, created_at)\nstyle_profiles(id, sales_id, channel, style_md, updated_at)\n\nRules:\n- The user is a manager and may see data for all sales reps.\n- Only SELECT statements. Never attempt to modify data; if asked to add or change records, tell the user to use the Add Customer or Edit Customer agent instead.\n- Results are capped at 50 rows; use aggregates (COUNT, GROUP BY) or ORDER BY + narrower filters for large questions.\n- Answer in the same language the user writes in.\n- Present answers as short plain text or \"-\" bullet lists (no markdown tables). Mention counts and the most relevant fields; don''t dump raw rows verbatim.\n- Do not show the SQL you ran unless the user explicitly asks for it.\n- If a query returns nothing, say so plainly and suggest what to check.\n- For follow-up questions that reference a customer, vehicle, or result from earlier in the conversation, run a SQL query to fetch that entity''s full details (especially their id) if you need them to answer precisely. Use names or other identifiers visible in the conversation history to look them up.\n- When looking for matching inventory, search broadly: by vehicle segment (SUV, sedan, truck, etc.), price range, or a group of similar makes \u2014 not only by the exact brand the customer currently drives. A customer with a Hyundai Tucson likely fits any compact/mid-size SUV.\n- For complex questions, run multiple queries in sequence: gather context first, then query the target table with the details you found.\n- When an inventory query returns nothing for a narrow filter, widen the search (drop a constraint, try adjacent segments or a price range) before concluding nothing is available.\n- When the user asks you to write, draft, or compose an email to a customer, call the compose_email_draft tool with the customer''s name and the purpose. Do not use query_db for this."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Hi! Ask me anything about your CRM data \u2014 or ask me to write an email.\n\nExamples:\n\u2022 \"How many customers haven''t been contacted in 60 days?\"\n\u2022 \"Which leases end in the next 3 months?\"\n\u2022 \"What Toyotas do we have in stock under $30k?\"\n\u2022 \"Write an email to Sunny Cook reminding her about her lease\""}, {"role": "user", "content": "who''s leasing ending soon?"}], "tools": [{"type": "function", "function": {"name": "query_db", "description": "Run a single read-only SQL SELECT statement against the CRM database and get the matching rows back. Use this whenever the user asks about their customers, cars, interactions, inventory, outreach rules, or email drafts.", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"sql": {"type": "string", "description": "One SELECT statement in PostgreSQL dialect. No INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE/DDL."}}, "required": ["sql"]}}}, {"type": "function", "function": {"name": "compose_email_draft", "description": "Compose a personalised email draft for a specific customer. Use this when the user says ''write an email to [name]'', ''draft an email for [name]'', ''compose an email to [name]'', or similar. Do NOT use query_db for this \u2014 call this tool directly.", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"customer_name": {"type": "string", "description": "The customer''s name as mentioned by the user."}, "purpose": {"type": "string", "description": "Optional free-text description of the email''s purpose, e.g. ''reminding her about her lease'', ''follow up on test drive''. Passed to the email composer as a custom theme."}}, "required": ["customer_name"]}}}], "tool_choice": "auto"}', '{"choices": [{"finish_reason": "tool_calls", "index": 0, "message": {"content": null, "role": "assistant", "tool_calls": [{"function": {"arguments": "{\"sql\":\"SELECT c.full_name, c.email, c.phone, cc.make, cc.model, cc.year, cc.lease_end_date, c.assigned_sales_id\\nFROM customer_car cc\\nJOIN customers c ON c.id = cc.customer_id\\nWHERE cc.ownership_type = ''lease''\\n  AND cc.lease_end_date IS NOT NULL\\n  AND cc.lease_end_date >= CURRENT_DATE\\n  AND cc.lease_end_date <= CURRENT_DATE + INTERVAL ''90 days''\\nORDER BY cc.lease_end_date ASC\\nLIMIT 50;\"}", "name": "query_db"}, "id": "call_L0aGNKHr2YlHcY00ozsLsRje", "index": 0, "type": "function"}]}}], "created": 1781183376, "id": "chatcmpl-239e593e-24f9-4255-820d-12b39", "model": "gpt-5.4", "object": "chat.completion", "usage": {"completion_tokens": 128, "prompt_tokens": 1008, "total_tokens": 1136}}', '2026-06-11 13:09:36.508208+00');
