le.\n    *   *Customer:*\n        *   Name: Briana C.\n        *   Phone: (Not visible)\n        *   Email: (Not visible)\n\n3.  **Refining the Extraction & Applying Rules:**\n\n    *   `deal_type`: \"lease\" (Rule 1)\n    *   `contract_date`: \"2022-08-06\" (Rule 2)\n    *   `trim_base`: \"Comfortline\"\n    *   `trim_package`: null (Rule 4 - no package listed)\n    *   `make`: \"Volkswagen\"\n    *   `model`: \"Tiguan\"\n    *   `model_year`: 2022\n    *   `selling_price`: 44400\n    *   `discount`: -1800 (Rule 3 & 6)\n    *   `fees_total`: 3800\n    *   `tax_total`: 4400\n    *   `capital_cost`: 44400\n    *   `total_with_tax`: 48800\n    *   `cash_down`: 10000\n    *   `drive_off_total`: 38800\n    *   `payment_amount`: 899.00\n    *   `num_payments`: 36\n    *   `line_items`:\n        *   Discount: {\"item_name\": \"Discount\", \"category\": \"discount\", \"amount\": -1800.00}\n        *   Fees: Since the $3,800 is a lump sum and I cannot categorize it, I will list it as a single line item under ''other'' if I must list all fees, or just rely on the total. Given the instruction to copy *every* fee line verbatim, and only a total is present, I will list the total fees as a single line item.\n        *   {\"item_name\": \"Fees Total\", \"category\": \"other\", \"amount\": 3800.00}\n    *   `customer`: {\"name\": \"Briana C.\", \"phone\": null, \"email\": null}\n    *   `confidence`: 0.9 (High confidence in the numbers, low confidence in missing VIN/specific fee breakdown).\n\n4.  **Final JSON Construction (Self-Correction/Review):** Ensure all fields are present, types are correct (numbers vs strings), and the structure matches the required output exactly. (The final JSON structure looks correct based on the derived data.)"}}], "created": 1781279324, "model": "gemma-4-E4B_q4_0-it.gguf", "system_fingerprint": "b9590-d2462f8f7", "object": "chat.completion", "usage": {"completion_tokens": 2175, "prompt_tokens": 1479, "total_tokens": 3654, "prompt_tokens_details": {"