ate\" -> rate_pct (NOT Residual %). Rate is usually 0\u201310, not hundreds.\n- \"KM Allowed\" / \"KPY Allowed\" -> km_per_year (e.g. 20000). \"Residual 47%\" -> residual_pct as 47.\n- \"Res. MSRP\" -> residual_msrp. \"Cash Down / Cap Reduction\" -> both cash_down and cap_reduction.\n"}, {"role": "user", "content": [{"type": "image_url", "image_url": {"url": "<image omitted, 305415 chars>"}}, {"type": "text", "text": "Read ONLY the Lease or Finance table. Return ONLY the JSON object. Term and Number of Payments are separate rows."}]}], "max_tokens": 2048, "temperature": 0.0}', '{"choices": [{"finish_reason": "stop", "index": 0, "message": {"role": "assistant", "content": "{\n  \"deal_type\": \"lease\",\n  \"lender\": \"VW Credit Canada Inc.\",\n  \"rate_pct\": 5.99,\n  \"term\": 48,\n  \"payment_frequency\": \"biweekly\",\n  \"num_payments\": 104,\n  \"base_payment\": 220.25,\n  \"payment_amount\": 253.29,\n  \"capital_cost\": 44119.45,\n  \"cash_down\": 8781.75,\n  \"cap_reduction\": 8781.75,\n  \"drive_off_total\": 11000.00,\n  \"residual_msrp\": 40390.00,\n  \"residual_pct\": 47,\n  \"residual_value\": 18983.30,\n  \"buy_option_price\": 18983.30,\n  \"km_per_year\": 20000,\n  \"excess_km_rate\": 0.12,\n  \"security_deposit\": 550.00\n}"}}], "created": 1781366112, "model": "Qwen3VL-4B-Instruct-Q4_K_M.gguf", "system_fingerprint": "b9590-d2462f8f7", "object": "chat.completion", "usage": {"completion_tokens": 245, "prompt_tokens": 2625, "total_tokens": 2870, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 2624}}, "id": "chatcmpl-Kds5H9z789BXgDCpqaK1wiRo8d1TYQYn", "timings": {"cache_n": 2624, "prompt_n": 1, "prompt_ms": 32.854, "prompt_per_token_ms": 32.854, "prompt_per_second": 30.437694040299508, "predicted_n": 245, "predicted_ms": 6319.413, "predicted_per_token_ms": 25.79352244897959, "predicted_per_second": 38.7694236790664}}', '2026-06-13 15:55:12.548539+00');
INSERT INTO public.llm_request_logs (id, url, model, input, output, created_at) VALUES (57, 'http://host.docker.internal:8080/v1/chat/completions', 'Qwen3VL-4B-Instruct-Q4_K_M.ggu', '{"model": "Qwen3VL-4B-Instruct-Q4_K_M.ggu", "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are an AI email-writing assistant for a car dealership sales representative.\nYour task is to compose a personalised outreach email to a specific customer.\n\nYou will receive:\n1. Email purpose (the reason for reaching out)\n2. Customer profile (name, note, vehicles they own/lease)\n3. Matching inventory vehicles that may be relevant to this customer\n4. The sales representative''s writing style guide (in Markdown)\n5. Customer''s full contact log (channel, date, summary of each prior interaction)\n\nRules:\n- Match the representative''s voice and style exactly as described in the style guide\n- Make the email feel personal and relevant to this specific customer''s situation\n- Use the contact log to avoid repeating topics already covered, acknowledge the relationship naturally, and pick up where the last conversation left off\n- Reference their vehicle(s) naturally (e.g., lease end dates, age, type)\n- Mention 1-2 inventory options at most; do not list every car\n- Follow the word count and paragraph count specified in the style guide; if unspecified, target 180\u2013260 words\n- Always include a warm closing paragraph thanking the customer, a soft CTA (reply or call), and a professional sign-off with name and title\n- Do NOT include a subject line in the body\n- Respond ONLY with a JSON object in the exact format:\n  {\"subject\": \"...\", \"body\": \"...\"}"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Email purpose: The customer''s lease or financing is ending soon. Write an email about upgrade options and next steps.\n\nCustomer: Priya Sharma\n\nNote: leased a 2020 Hyundai Tucson, new immigrant family with 2 kids. commit with work 30 mins everyday\n happy but open to lease.\n\nCustomer vehicles:\n  \u2022 2020 Hyundai Tucson (lease) lease ends 2026-06-30\n\nRelevant inventory:\n  \u2022 2025 Volkswagen Jetta S $21,990\n  \u2022 2025 Volkswagen Golf Base $25,990\n  \u2022 2025 Volkswagen Tiguan S $29,495\n\nContact history (newest first):\n  (no prior contact logged)\n\nStyle guide:\n## Lease Expiration\n\n### Subject Line\nWhile not provided, the subject line would likely follow a direct and helpful pattern, focusing on the recipient''s current status or the vehicle they own (e.g., \"Update regarding your 2022 VW Tiguan\"). The tone would be informative and professional, clearly signaling that the email is about an important upcoming deadline.\n\n### Format\nThe message is structured with a formal, polite greeting followed by a clear opening paragraph establishing the context (lease maturity date). The body uses a numbered list to present the \"End-of-Lease Options,\" which acts as a structured, digestible summary of choices. The closing features a dedicated call-to-action (CTA) that directs the customer to reply or call, followed by a warm, appreciative sign-off. Paragraph spacing is clear to separate the context, the options, and the invitation.\n\n### Style\nThe tone is professional, consultative, and warm. The writer adopts the persona of a helpful guide, emphasizing a \"seamless\" transition. They use full vehicle descriptions (Year/Make/Model) to ensure the customer is addressed correctly. The language is sophisticated but accessible, avoiding aggressive sales pressure. The closing signature is comprehensive, including the name, title, and company affiliation.\n\n## Test Drive Follow-Up\n\n### Subject Line\nThe subject line would likely be friendly and highly relevant to the specific vehicle, possibly referencing the test drive (e.g., \"Following up on the Jetta Comfortline\"). The tone should be warm and casual, focused on continuing the conversation rather than pushing for an immediate sale.\n\n### Format\nThe message opens with a brief thank-you and a personalized reference to the test drive experience. It uses a conversational structure: gratitude $\\rightarrow$ empathy (acknowledging market research) $\\rightarrow$ value proposition (the incentive) $\\rightarrow$ soft CTA. The overall length is short to medium, maintaining a conversational pace. There are no lists or heavy formatting; the message relies on smooth transitions between paragraphs.\n\n### Style\nThe style is highly empathetic and casually professional. The writer actively validates the customer\u2019s process, acknowledging their need to \"invest\" and \"research,\" which reduces perceived sales pressure. The tone is encouraging and informative, using specific, strong data points (e.g., \"0.99% special finance rate,\" \"60 months\") to demonstrate expertise. The language is friendly and conversational, ending with a gentle wish for safe driving and a look forward to connecting."}]}', '{"choices": [{"finish_reason": "stop", "index": 0, "message": {"role": "assistant", "content": "{\n  \"subject\": \"Update: Your 2020 Hyundai Tucson Lease Ends June 30 \u2014 Upgrade Options Ahead\",\n  \"body\": \"Hi Priya,\\n\\nThanks for being a valued member of our community \u2014 and for choosing to lease a 2020 Hyundai Tucson, which you\u2019ve clearly enjoyed while raising your two kids. Your lease ends June 30, 2026, and we\u2019re here to help you make the next move seamless and stress-free.\\n\\nHere are a few options to consider as you plan ahead:\\n1. 2025 Volkswagen Jetta S \u2014 $21,990, a smart, sporty compact sedan perfect for your family\u2019s needs.\\n2. 2025 Volkswagen Golf Base \u2014 $25,990, a practical, efficient hatchback with great handling for your daily commute.\\n3. 2025 Volkswagen Tiguan S \u2014 $29,495, a versatile SUV if you\u2019re looking for extra space and comfort.\\n\\nWe can work together to find the right fit \u2014 whether you\u2019re seeking a new lease, a financing option, or a test drive \u2014 and we\u2019ll tailor it to your schedule and goals.\\n\\nLet me know what\u2019s on your mind, or give me a call anytime. I\u2019m happy to help you explore these or any other options that suit your lifestyle.\\n\\nWarmly,\\nRaj Patel\\nSales Associate\\nGreenfield Motors\\n(555) 123-4567\\nwww.greenfieldmotors.com\"\n}"}}], "created": 1781366423, "model": "Qwen3VL-4B-Instruct-Q4_K_M.gguf", "system_fingerprint": "b9590-d2462f8f7", "object": "chat.completion", "usage": {"completion_tokens": 336, "prompt_tokens": 980, "total_tokens": 1316, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0}}, "id": "chatcmpl-GbNpiMTuIdLhtLkpyFIWArMuvS0ts7ef", "timings": {"cache_n": 0, "prompt_n": 980, "prompt_ms": 4161.927, "prompt_per_token_ms": 4.2468642857142855, "prompt_per_second": 235.4678493880359, "predicted_n": 336, "predicted_ms": 8121.753, "predicted_per_token_ms": 24.17188392857143, "predicted_per_second": 41.37037903024138}}', '2026-06-13 16:00:23.731448+00');
INSERT INTO public.llm_request_logs (id, url, model, input, output, created_at) VALUES (56, 'http://host.docker.internal:8080/v1/chat/completions', 'Qwen3VL-4B-Instruct-Q4_K_M.ggu', '{"model": "Qwen3VL-4B-Instruct-Q4_K_M.ggu", "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are reading ONLY the vehicle pricing / fee breakdown column on a dealership deal worksheet.\nIgnore lease terms, customer info, and payment tables. Return ONLY one JSON object \u2014 no markdown.\n\nRead each printed row label in the left pricing column exactly. Do NOT calculate or infer totals.\n{\n  \"base_price\": number,\n  \"selling_price\": number,\n  \"discount\": number,\n  \"fees_total\": number,\n  \"tax_total\": number,\n  \"capital_cost\": number,\n  \"cash_down\": number,\n  \"cap_reduction\": number,\n  \"drive_off_total\": number,\n  \"line_items\": [{\"item_name\": \"Air Tax\", \"category\": \"gov_levy\", \"amount\": 100.00}]\n}\n\nRow mapping (Canadian O''Regan / VW-style sheets):\n- \"MSRP\" / list price -> base_price (optional)\n- \"Selling Price\" -> selling_price (e.g. 42340.00 \u2014 vehicle price before fees)\n- \"Discount\" -> discount (negative; e.g. -250 from parenthesized amount)\n- Each fee line -> line_items with positive amount (Admin Fee, Air Tax, Tire Levy, etc.)\n- \"Sub-Total\" / \"Capital Cost\" -> capital_cost (e.g. 44119.45 \u2014 BEFORE cap reduction)\n- \"Cash Down / Cap Reduction\" -> cash_down AND cap_reduction (same value, e.g. 8781.75)\n- \"Net Lease\" is NOT capital_cost \u2014 it is capital_cost minus cap_reduction (~35337.70)\n- \"Total Balance Due\" / \"Drive Off\" -> drive_off_total (e.g. 11000.00 \u2014 amount due today)\nNEVER output round placeholder guesses (1000, 2500, 5000). Use null when a row is illegible.\ncapital_cost must exceed selling_price. drive_off_total is typically $8k\u2013$15k on leases, not $40k.\n"}, {"role": "user", "content": [{"type": "image_url", "image_url": {"url": "<image omitted, 305415 chars>"}}, {"type": "text", "text": "Read ONLY the pricing / fee breakdown column. Return ONLY the JSON object. Capital Cost is Sub-Total BEFORE cap reduction; Drive Off is NOT Net Lease."}]}], "max_tokens": 2048, "temperature": 0.0}', '{"choices": [{"finish_reason": "stop", "index": 0, "message": {"role": "assistant", "content": "{\n  \"base_price\": 42640.00,\n  \"selling_price\": 42340.00,\n  \"discount\": -250.00,\n  \"fees_total\": 100.00,\n  \"tax_total\": 0.00,\n  \"capital_cost\": 44119.45,\n  \"cash_down\": 8781.75,\n  \"cap_reduction\": 8781.75,\n  \"drive_off_total\": 11000.00,\n  \"line_items\": [\n    {\n      \"item_name\": \"Air Tax\",\n      \"category\": \"gov_levy\",\n      \"amount\": 100.00\n    }\n  ]\n}"}}], "created": 1781366129, "model": "Qwen3VL-4B-Instruct-Q4_K_M.gguf", "system_fingerprint": "b9590-d2462f8f7", "object": "chat.completion", "usage": {"completion_tokens": 172, "prompt_tokens": 2523, "total_tokens": 2695, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0}}, "id": "chatcmpl-uklDWOO0qHqsfeoXxlbrJGDKh7FMLkuv", "timings": {"cache_n": 0, "prompt_n": 2523, "prompt_ms": 12379.956, "prompt_per_token_ms": 4.9068394768133174, "prompt_per_second": 203.79717019995869, "predicted_n": 172, "predicted_ms": 4495.8, "predicted_per_token_ms": 26.138372093023257, "predicted_per_second": 38.25792962320388}}', '2026-06-13 15:55:29.768753+00');
