 the test drive experience. It uses a conversational structure: gratitude $\\rightarrow$ empathy (acknowledging market research) $\\rightarrow$ value proposition (the incentive) $\\rightarrow$ soft CTA. The overall length is short to medium, maintaining a conversational pace. There are no lists or heavy formatting; the message relies on smooth transitions between paragraphs.\n\n### Style\nThe style is highly empathetic and casually professional. The writer actively validates the customer\u2019s process, acknowledging their need to \"invest\" and \"research,\" which reduces perceived sales pressure. The tone is encouraging and informative, using specific, strong data points (e.g., \"0.99% special finance rate,\" \"60 months\") to demonstrate expertise. The language is friendly and conversational, ending with a gentle wish for safe driving and a look forward to connecting.\n\nExtra hard rules (non-negotiable):\n  \u2022 make this is fix email ending\nBest regards,\nWilson Xing | Sales Consultant"}]}', '{"choices": [{"finish_reason": "stop", "index": 0, "message": {"role": "assistant", "content": "{\n  \"subject\": \"Update Regarding Your 2022 VW Tiguan Lease Expiration\",\n  \"body\": \"Hi Brianna,\\n\\nI\u2019m following up on your 2022 VW Tiguan lease, which ends on September 16, 2026. As you approach this milestone, we\u2019d love to help you explore smooth, seamless upgrade options that match your needs and budget.\\n\\nHere are a few vehicles in our current inventory that might fit:\\n1. 2025 Volkswagen Jetta S \u2014 $21,990 \u2014 a great value for daily driving.\\n2. 2025 Volkswagen Golf Base \u2014 $25,990 \u2014 ideal if you\u2019re looking for a sporty yet practical ride.\\n3. 2025 Volkswagen Tiguan S \u2014 $29,495 \u2014 perfect if you want a larger SUV with refined performance.\\n\\nWe can help you compare financing terms, test drive any of these, or even explore lease-to-buy options. No pressure \u2014 just a friendly, tailored way to transition your next drive.\\n\\nLet me know how you\u2019d like to proceed \u2014 I\u2019m happy to set up a call or send over detailed brochures. Either way, I\u2019m here to help.\\n\\nThanks so much for being a valued customer \u2014 and safe travels on the road ahead!\\n\\nBest regards,\\nWilson Xing | Sales Consultant\\n[Your Dealership Name]\"\n}"}}], "created": 1781367175, "model": "Qwen3VL-4B-Instruct-Q4_K_M.gguf", "system_fingerprint": "b9590-d2462f8f7", "object": "chat.completion", "usage": {"completion_tokens": 311, "prompt_tokens": 1003, "total_tokens": 1314, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 1002}}, "id": "chatcmpl-vb3bQand4suGJQKhFU3noAMSjCMr81RN", "timings": {"cache_n": 1002, "prompt_n": 1, "prompt_ms": 89.54, "prompt_per_token_ms": 89.54, "prompt_per_second": 11.168192986374804, "predicted_n": 311, "predicted_ms": 7871.125, "predicted_per_token_ms": 25.309083601286172, "predicted_per_second": 39.51150566151598}}', '2026-06-13 16:12:55.28525+00');
INSERT INTO public.llm_request_logs (id, url, model, input, output, created_at) VALUES (64, 'http://host.docker.internal:8080/v1/chat/completions', 'Qwen3VL-4B-Instruct-Q4_K_M.ggu', '{"model": "Qwen3VL-4B-Instruct-Q4_K_M.ggu", "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are an AI email-writing assistant for a car dealership sales representative.\nYour task is to compose a personalised outreach email to a specific customer.\n\nYou will receive:\n1. Email purpose (the reason for reaching out)\n2. Customer profile (name, note, vehicles they own/lease)\n3. Matching inventory vehicles that may be relevant to this customer\n4. The sales representative''s writing style guide (in Markdown)\n5. Customer''s full contact log (channel, date, summary of each prior interaction)\n\nRules:\n- Match the representative''s voice and style exactly as described in the style guide\n- Treat any \"Extra hard rules\" as mandatory requirements that override default phrasing\n- Make the email feel personal and relevant to this specific customer''s situation\n- Use the contact log to avoid repeating topics already covered, acknowledge the relationship naturally, and pick up where the last conversation left off\n- Reference their vehicle(s) naturally (e.g., lease end dates, age, type)\n- Mention 1-2 inventory options at most; do not list every car\n- Follow the word count and paragraph count specified in the style guide; if unspecified, target 180\u2013260 words\n- Always include a warm closing paragraph thanking the customer, a soft CTA (reply or call), and a professional sign-off with name and title\n- Do NOT include a subject line in the body\n- Respond ONLY with a JSON object in the exact format:\n  {\"subject\": \"...\", \"body\": \"...\"}"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Email purpose: The customer''s lease or financing is ending soon. Write an email about upgrade options and next steps.\n\nCustomer: Brianna C Algee\n\nNote: (none)\n\nCustomer vehicles:\n  \u2022 2022 VOLKSWAGEN TIGUAN (lease) lease ends 2026-09-16\n\nRelevant inventory:\n  \u2022 2025 Volkswagen Jetta S $21,990\n  \u2022 2025 Volkswagen Golf Base $25,990\n  \u2022 2025 Volkswagen Tiguan S $29,495\n\nContact history (newest first):\n  (no prior contact logged)\n\nStyle guide:\nPrimary section to follow for this email type:\n## Lease Expiration\n\n### Subject Line\nWhile not provided, the subject line would likely follow a direct and helpful pattern, focusing on the recipient''s current status or the vehicle they own (e.g., \"Update regarding your 2022 VW Tiguan\"). The tone would be informative and professional, clearly signaling that the email is about an important upcoming deadline.\n\n### Format\nThe message is structured with a formal, polite greeting followed by a clear opening paragraph establishing the context (lease maturity date). The body uses a numbered list to present the \"End-of-Lease Options,\" which acts as a structured, digestible summary of choices. The closing features a dedicated call-to-action (CTA) that directs the customer to reply or call, followed by a warm, appreciative sign-off. Paragraph spacing is clear to separate the context, the options, and the invitation.\n\n### Style\nThe tone is professional, consultative, and warm. The writer adopts the persona of a helpful guide, emphasizing a \"seamless\" transition. They use full vehicle descriptions (Year/Make/Model) to ensure the customer is addressed correctly. The language is sophisticated but accessible, avoiding aggressive sales pressure. The closing signature is comprehensive, including the name, title, and company affiliation.\n\nAlso stay consistent with the rest of the style guide.\n\nExtra hard rules (non-negotiable):\n  \u2022 make this is fix email ending\nBest regards,\nWilson Xing | Sales Consultant"}]}', '{"choices": [{"finish_reason": "stop", "index": 0, "message": {"role": "assistant", "content": "{\n  \"subject\": \"Update Regarding Your 2022 VW Tiguan Lease\",\n  \"body\": \"Hi Brianna,\\n\\nYour lease on the 2022 Volkswagen Tiguan is set to end on September 16, 2026 \u2014 and we\u2019re here to help you make the most of that transition. Whether you\u2019re looking to upgrade, keep your current brand, or simply get a fresh start, we\u2019ve got a few well-matched options ready for you.\\n\\nHere\u2019s what\u2019s available:\\n1. 2025 Volkswagen Jetta S \u2014 $21,990 \u2014 A sleek, fuel-efficient hatchback with modern tech and a sporty feel.\\n2. 2025 Volkswagen Golf Base \u2014 $25,990 \u2014 The compact sedan that\u2019s built for efficiency and everyday driving.\\n3. 2025 Volkswagen Tiguan S \u2014 $29,495 \u2014 If you love the Tiguan\u2019s practicality, this upgraded model brings sharper performance and more tech.\\n\\nWe\u2019d love to walk you through which option fits your needs \u2014 whether you\u2019re looking for more space, better mileage, or a smooth upgrade. Just reply or give us a call, and we\u2019ll tailor the next steps to your goals.\\n\\nThanks so much for being a valued part of our community \u2014 we\u2019re excited to help you move forward with confidence.\\n\\nBest regards,\\nWilson Xing | Sales Consultant\\n[Your Dealership Name]\"\n}"}}], "created": 1781367284, "model": "Qwen3VL-4B-Instruct-Q4_K_M.gguf", "system_fingerprint": "b9590-d2462f8f7", "object": "chat.completion", "usage": {"completion_tokens": 318, "prompt_tokens": 773, "total_tokens": 1091, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 464}}, "id": "chatcmpl-N2Pi8H9rVFoBbK0YnBJiwTQnqDoGn3AJ", "timings": {"cache_n": 464, "prompt_n": 309, "prompt_ms": 900.117, "prompt_per_token_ms": 2.913, "prompt_per_second": 343.28870580157917, "predicted_n": 318, "predicted_ms": 7655.366, "predicted_per_token_ms": 24.073477987421384, "predicted_per_second": 41.53949007794011}}', '2026-06-13 16:14:44.378754+00');
INSERT INTO public.llm_request_logs (id, url, model, input, output, created_at) VALUES (65, 'http://host.docker.internal:8080/v1/chat/completions', 'Qwen3VL-4B-Instruct-Q4_K_M.ggu', '{"model": "Qwen3VL-4B-Instruct-Q4_K_M.ggu", "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are an AI email-writing assistant for a car dealership sales representative.\nYour task is to compose a personalised outreach email to a specific customer.\n\nYou will receive:\n1. Email purpose (the reason for reaching out)\n2. Customer profile (name, note, vehicles they own/lease)\n3. Matching inventory vehicles that may be relevant to this customer\n4. The sales representative''s writing style guide (in Markdown)\n5. Customer''s full contact log (channel, date, summary of each prior interaction)\n\nRules:\n- Match the representative''s voice and style exactly as described in the style guide\n- Treat any \"Extra hard rules\" as mandatory requirements that override default phrasing\n- If the style guide includes a concrete format template, headings, or option-label pattern, follow it exactly\n- Make the email feel personal and relevant to this specific customer''s situation\n- Use the contact log to avoid repeating topics already covered, acknowledge the relationship naturally, and pick up where the last conversation left off\n- Reference their vehicle(s) naturally (e.g., lease end dates, age, type)\n- Mention 1-2 inventory options at most; do not list every car\n- Follow the word count and paragraph count specified in the style guide; if unspecified, target 180\u2013260 words\n- Always include a warm closing paragraph thanking the customer, a soft CTA (reply or call), and a professional sign-off with name and title\n- Do NOT include a subject line in the body\n- Respond ONLY with a JSON object in the exact format:\n  {\"subject\": \"...\", \"body\": \"...\"}"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Email purpose: The customer''s lease or financing is ending soon. Write an email about upgrade options and next steps.\n\nCustomer: Brianna C Algee\n\nNote: (none)\n\nCustomer vehicles:\n  \u2022 2022 VOLKSWAGEN TIGUAN (lease) lease ends 2026-09-16\n\nRelevant inventory:\n  \u2022 2025 Volkswagen Jetta S $21,990\n  \u2022 2025 Volkswagen Golf Base $25,990\n\nContact history (newest first):\n  (no prior contact logged)\n\nStyle guide:\nPrimary section to follow for this email type:\n## Lease Expiration\n\n### Subject Line\nWhile not provided, the subject line would likely follow a direct and helpful pattern, focusing on the recipient''s current status or the vehicle they own (e.g., \"Update regarding your 2022 VW Tiguan\"). The tone would be informative and professional, clearly signaling that the email is about an important upcoming deadline.\n\n### Format\nThe message is structured with a formal, polite greeting followed by a clear opening paragraph establishing the context (lease maturity date). The body uses a numbered list to present the \"End-of-Lease Options,\" which acts as a structured, digestible summary of choices. The closing features a dedicated call-to-action (CTA) that directs the customer to reply or call, followed by a warm, appreciative sign-off. Paragraph spacing is clear to separate the context, the options, and the invitation.\n\n### Style\nThe tone is professional, consultative, and warm. The writer adopts the persona of a helpful guide, emphasizing a \"seamless\" transition. They use full vehicle descriptions (Year/Make/Model) to ensure the customer is addressed correctly. The language is sophisticated but accessible, avoiding aggressive sales pressure. The closing signature is comprehensive, including the name, title, and company affiliation.\n\nAlso stay consistent with the rest of the style guide.\n\nRequired format checklist:\n  \u2022 Use a greeting line with the customer''s first name.\n  \u2022 Keep clean paragraph spacing.\n  \u2022 Include a soft CTA paragraph before the sign-off.\n  \u2022 Reference the lease/finance end date in the opening.\n  \u2022 Use the heading \"Your End-of-Lease Options:\".\n  \u2022 Format choices as Option 1 / Option 2 / Option 3 (not generic numbered bullets).\n\nExtra hard rules (non-negotiable):\n  \u2022 make this is fix email ending\nBest regards,\nWilson Xing | Sales Consultant"}]}', '{"choices": [{"finish_reason": "stop", "index": 0, "message": {"role": "assistant", "content": "{\n  \"subject\": \"Update Regarding Your 2022 VW Tiguan Lease End - 2026-09-16\",\n  \"body\": \"Hi Brianna,\\n\\nYour lease on the 2022 Volkswagen Tiguan is set to end on September 16, 2026 \u2014 a great time to consider an upgrade that fits your needs and budget. We\u2019re here to help you transition smoothly without interruption.\\n\\nYour End-of-Lease Options:\\n\\nOption 1: 2025 Volkswagen Jetta S \u2014 $21,990. A sleek, efficient sedan with modern tech and a refined ride, perfect for daily commutes and short trips.\\n\\nOption 2: 2025 Volkswagen Golf Base \u2014 $25,990. A compact, sporty hatchback with great handling and practicality \u2014 ideal if you\u2019re looking for more agility and space for passengers.\\n\\nLet me know which direction you\u2019d like to explore, or if you\u2019d prefer to chat over the phone \u2014 I\u2019m happy to walk you through any financing or trade-in options available.\\n\\nThanks for being a valued customer, and I look forward to helping you find the perfect next step.\\n\\nWarmly,\\nWilson Xing | Sales Consultant\\nCanyon Auto Group\"\n}"}}], "created": 1781367384, "model": "Qwen3VL-4B-Instruct-Q4_K_M.gguf", "system_fingerprint": "b9590-d2462f8f7", "object": "chat.completion", "usage": {"completion_tokens": 283, "prompt_tokens": 862, "total_tokens": 1145, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 141}}, "id": "chatcmpl-iGUUZdNooUxC9iuumhZgpzARP3VdTuxu", "timings": {"cache_n": 141, "prompt_n": 721, "prompt_ms": 2024.809, "prompt_per_token_ms": 2.8083342579750346, "prompt_per_second": 356.08296881335474, "predicted_n": 283, "predicted_ms": 7088.68, "predicted_per_token_ms": 25.048339222614842, "predicted_per_second": 39.92280650276215}}', '2026-06-13 16:16:24.783137+00');
INSERT INTO public.llm_request_logs (id, url, model, input, output, created_at) VALUES (66, 'http://host.docker.internal:8080/v1/chat/completions', 'Qwen3VL-4B-Instruct-Q4_K_M.ggu', '{"model": "Qwen3VL-4B-Instruct-Q4_K_M.ggu", "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a writing style analyst for a car dealership sales team.\nYour task is to study the provided sample messages and distill the writer''s unique communication style\ninto a concise, actionable markdown guide. Another AI will use this guide to write new messages\nthat faithfully match this person''s voice and style.\n\nThe writer''s samples are organized into the following categories:\n- Lease Expiration\n- Test Drive Follow-Up\n\nProduce one ## section for each category that has samples provided, using the exact category name as the ## heading.\nIf any sample does not match a named category, place it under ## General.\nDo NOT produce sections for categories that have no samples.\n\nEach category section MUST contain exactly three sub-sections:\n\n### Subject Line\nDescribe the subject line patterns observed across the samples:\n- Typical length (e.g. under 6 words, one short phrase)\n- Tone and urgency (e.g. friendly teaser, direct offer, question)\n- Use of personalisation (customer name, vehicle details)\n- Common openers or formulas (e.g. \"Your [Year] [Model] is ready\", \"Quick update on\u2026\")\n- Capitalisation style (title case, sentence case, all-lower)\n- Use of numbers, emojis, or special characters\n- Anything that makes the subject line pattern recognisable\n\n### Format\nDescribe the structural/layout conventions observed in the samples:\n- Message length (e.g. 2-3 short paragraphs, under 80 words)\n- Opening line pattern (greeting style, whether name is used)\n- Body structure (e.g. one hook sentence \u2192 offer \u2192 CTA)\n- Closing line pattern (sign-off, signature style)\n- Paragraph count and spacing habits\n- Use of bullet points, line breaks, or lists\n\n### Style\nDescribe the voice and language patterns:\n- Tone and formality level for this situation\n- Energy level (urgent, warm, casual, professional)\n- Vocabulary preferences and any signature phrases or pet words\n- How they reference vehicles (make/model/year/trim usage)\n- Use of emojis, punctuation quirks, or capitalisation habits\n- Anything that makes this person''s writing instantly recognisable\n\nOutput a clean markdown document. Do NOT include any samples verbatim."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Channel: email\n\n### Lease Expiration\n\nHi Andy\nI hope this email finds you well.\nCan you believe how quickly time flies? We want to remind you that the lease on your 2022 VW Tiguan is scheduled to mature on July 31, 2026.\nAs you approach the end of your lease, you have a few great options available to you, and we want to make sure the transition is as smooth and seamless as possible. Whether you want to upgrade, keep your current ride, or simply hand over the keys, we are here to help you navigate the next steps.\nYour End-of-Lease Options:\nOption 1: Upgrade to a new model. Get behind the wheel of a brand-new vehicle with the latest technology, safety features, and a fresh warranty.\nOption 2: Purchase your current vehicle. If you\u2019ve fallen in love with your car and aren''t ready to part ways, you can buy it out for the residual value listed in your contract.\nOption 3: Return the vehicle. Simply schedule an inspection and return the keys to us at the end of your term.\nLet''s Find the Best Path Forward\nWe would love to invite you back into the dealership for a quick, no-pressure chat to review these options, check out current inventory, and see what specials might apply to you.\nPlease reply directly to this email or call us at 9024076395 to schedule a convenient time for you to drop by.\nThank you so much for being a valued part of the O''Regan''s VW family. We look forward to assisting you with your next automotive chapter!\nWarm regards,\nWilson Xing | Sales Consultant\n\n### Test Drive Follow-Up\n\nHi Andy,\nThank you for taking the time to visit us yesterday and test driving the 2026 Jetta Comfortline. It was a pleasure meeting you and showing you what the Jetta has to offer.\nI completely understand and respect your decision to test drive a few other options in the market before making your final move. Investing in a new vehicle is a big decision, and you want to ensure it\u2019s the perfect fit.\nWhile you are doing your research, I did want to give you a quick heads-up on an incentive that just came up for this month. Volkswagen is currently offering a 0.99% special finance rate for up to 60 months (5 years) on the 2026 Jetta. It\u2019s one of the strongest programs we''ve seen in a while, and it definitely keeps the monthly payments incredibly comfortable on that Comfortline trim.\nIf you have any questions about how those numbers look for your budget while you compare your options, just let me know.\nI would love the opportunity to earn your business. Drive safe during your other test drives, and I look forward to connecting with you soon!\nBest regards,\nWilson Xing | Sales Consultant"}]}', '{"choices": [{"finish_reason": "stop", "index": 0, "message": {"role": "assistant", "content": "## Lease Expiration\n\n### Subject Line\n- **Length**: Under 6 words, often one short phrase  \n- **Tone**: Friendly, slightly urgent but not pushy \u2014 \u201cCan you believe how quickly time flies?\u201d  \n- **Personalisation**: Uses customer name + vehicle model/year (\u201cyour 2022 VW Tiguan\u201d)  \n- **Openers/Formula**: \u201cWe want to remind you\u2026\u201d or \u201cAs you approach\u2026\u201d \u2014 warm, conversational  \n- **Capitalisation**: Title case, with occasional sentence case for tone  \n- **Emojis/Numbers**: None \u2014 clean, professional  \n- **Recognisable Pattern**: \u201cYour [Year] [Model] is ready\u201d or \u201cQuick update on\u2026\u201d, followed by clear next steps\n\n### Format\n- **Length**: 2\u20133 short paragraphs, under 80 words  \n- **Opening**: \u201cHi Andy\u201d + friendly opener (\u201cI hope this email finds you well.\u201d)  \n- **Body Structure**: Hook \u2192 reminder \u2192 3 options \u2192 CTA \u2192 gratitude  \n- **Closing Line**: \u201cWe look forward to assisting you\u2026\u201d + signature  \n- **Paragraphs**: 3\u20134 paragraphs with generous spacing  \n- **Lists**: Clear bullet-style options using \u201cOption 1\u2026 Option 2\u2026 Option 3\u2026\u201d  \n- **Spacing**: Spaced with line breaks, no dense paragraphs\n\n### Style\n- **Tone**: Warm, professional, slightly conversational \u2014 \u201cvalued part of the O''Regan''s VW family\u201d  \n- **Energy Level**: Calm, reassuring, encouraging \u2014 no pressure  \n- **Vocabulary**: \u201csmooth and seamless\u201d, \u201cnavigate the next steps\u201d, \u201cno-pressure chat\u201d  \n- **Vehicle Reference**: Uses \u201cmodel/year/trim\u201d \u2014 e.g., \u201c2022 VW Tiguan\u201d, \u201cComfortline trim\u201d  \n- **Emojis/Punctuation**: None \u2014 clean, no exclamation marks or emojis  \n- **Signature Style**: \u201cWilson Xing | Sales Consultant\u201d \u2014 consistent, branded\n\n---\n\n## Test Drive Follow-Up\n\n### Subject Line\n- **Length**: Under 6 words, often one short phrase  \n- **Tone**: Warm, appreciative, light \u2014 \u201cThank you for taking the time\u2026\u201d  \n- **Personalisation**: Uses customer name + vehicle model (\u201c2026 Jetta Comfortline\u201d)  \n- **Openers/Formula**: \u201cHi Andy, Thank you for taking the time\u2026\u201d \u2014 conversational, personalized  \n- **Capitalisation**: Title case, with occasional sentence case  \n- **Emojis/Numbers**: None \u2014 clean  \n- **Recognisable Pattern**: \u201cI did want to give you a quick heads-up\u2026\u201d \u2014 friendly, proactive\n\n### Format\n- **Length**: 2\u20133 short paragraphs, under 80 words  \n- **Opening**: \u201cHi Andy, Thank you\u2026\u201d \u2014 direct, warm  \n- **Body Structure**: Thank you \u2192 acknowledge customer\u2019s decision \u2192 offer incentive \u2192 open-ended CTA  \n- **Closing Line**: \u201cI look forward to connecting with you soon!\u201d \u2014 upbeat, non-demanding  \n- **Paragraphs**: 3 short paragraphs, spaced generously  \n- **Lists**: None \u2014 uses plain sentences  \n- **Spacing**: Clean, no bullet points \u2014 uses line breaks only\n\n### Style\n- **Tone**: Warm, professional, slightly playful \u2014 \u201cI would love the opportunity to earn your business\u201d  \n- **Energy Level**: Encouraging, patient, enthusiastic \u2014 \u201cDrive safe during your other test drives\u201d  \n- **Vocabulary**: \u201cbig decision\u201d, \u201cperfect fit\u201d, \u201ccomfortable on that Comfortline trim\u201d  \n- **Vehicle Reference**: Uses \u201cmodel/year/trim\u201d \u2014 e.g., \u201c2026 Jetta Comfortline\u201d  \n- **Emojis/Punctuation**: None \u2014 clean, friendly tone  \n- **Signature Style**: \u201cWilson Xing | Sales Consultant\u201d \u2014 consistent, branded"}}], "created": 1781367500, "model": "Qwen3VL-4B-Instruct-Q4_K_M.gguf", "system_fingerprint": "b9590-d2462f8f7", "object": "chat.completion", "usage": {"completion_tokens": 804, "prompt_tokens": 1061, "total_tokens": 1865, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0}}, "id": "chatcmpl-DMvlsfc4lllUbDNH8K0QtXpFp6pYAtzF", "timings": {"cache_n": 0, "prompt_n": 1061, "prompt_ms": 2853.12, "prompt_per_token_ms": 2.689085768143261, "prompt_per_second": 371.87359802602066, "predicted_n": 804, "predicted_ms": 19577.914, "predicted_per_token_ms": 24.350639303482588, "predicted_per_second": 41.066683610930156}}', '2026-06-13 16:18:20.116218+00');
INSERT INTO public.llm_request_logs (id, url, model, input, output, created_at) VALUES (67, 'http://host.docker.internal:8080/v1/chat/completions', 'Qwen3VL-4B-Instruct-Q4_K_M.ggu', '{"model": "Qwen3VL-4B-Instruct-Q4_K_M.ggu", "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are an AI email-writing assistant for a car dealership sales representative.\nYour task is to compose a personalised outreach email to a specific customer.\n\nYou will receive:\n1. Email purpose (the reason for reaching out)\n2. Customer profile (name, note, vehicles they own/lease)\n3. Matching inventory vehicles that may be relevant to this customer\n4. The sales representative''s writing style guide (in Markdown)\n5. Customer''s full contact log (channel, date, summary of each prior interaction)\n\nRules:\n- Match the representative''s voice and style exactly as described in the style guide\n- Treat any \"Extra hard rules\" as mandatory requirements that override default phrasing\n- If the style guide includes a concrete format template, headings, or option-label pattern, follow it exactly\n- Make the email feel personal and relevant to this specific customer''s situation\n- Use the contact log to avoid repeating topics already covered, acknowledge the relationship naturally, and pick up where the last conversation left off\n- Reference their vehicle(s) naturally (e.g., lease end dates, age, type)\n- Mention 1-2 inventory options at most; do not list every car\n- Follow the word count and paragraph count specified in the style guide; if unspecified, target 180\u2013260 words\n- Always include a warm closing paragraph thanking the customer, a soft CTA (reply or call), and a professional sign-off with name and title\n- Do NOT include a subject line in the body\n- Respond ONLY with a JSON object in the exact format:\n  {\"subject\": \"...\", \"body\": \"...\"}"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Email purpose: The customer''s lease or financing is ending soon. Write an email about upgrade options and next steps.\n\nCustomer: Brianna C Algee\n\nNote: (none)\n\nCustomer vehicles:\n  \u2022 2022 VOLKSWAGEN TIGUAN (lease) lease ends 2026-09-16\n\nRelevant inventory:\n  \u2022 2025 Volkswagen Jetta S $21,990\n  \u2022 2025 Volkswagen Golf Base $25,990\n\nContact history (newest first):\n  (no prior contact logged)\n\nStyle guide:\nPrimary section to follow for this email type:\n## Lease Expiration\n\n### Subject Line\n- **Length**: Under 6 words, often one short phrase  \n- **Tone**: Friendly, slightly urgent but not pushy \u2014 \u201cCan you believe how quickly time flies?\u201d  \n- **Personalisation**: Uses customer name + vehicle model/year (\u201cyour 2022 VW Tiguan\u201d)  \n- **Openers/Formula**: \u201cWe want to remind you\u2026\u201d or \u201cAs you approach\u2026\u201d \u2014 warm, conversational  \n- **Capitalisation**: Title case, with occasional sentence case for tone  \n- **Emojis/Numbers**: None \u2014 clean, professional  \n- **Recognisable Pattern**: \u201cYour [Year] [Model] is ready\u201d or \u201cQuick update on\u2026\u201d, followed by clear next steps\n\n### Format\n- **Length**: 2\u20133 short paragraphs, under 80 words  \n- **Opening**: \u201cHi Andy\u201d + friendly opener (\u201cI hope this email finds you well.\u201d)  \n- **Body Structure**: Hook \u2192 reminder \u2192 3 options \u2192 CTA \u2192 gratitude  \n- **Closing Line**: \u201cWe look forward to assisting you\u2026\u201d + signature  \n- **Paragraphs**: 3\u20134 paragraphs with generous spacing  \n- **Lists**: Clear bullet-style options using \u201cOption 1\u2026 Option 2\u2026 Option 3\u2026\u201d  \n- **Spacing**: Spaced with line breaks, no dense paragraphs\n\n### Style\n- **Tone**: Warm, professional, slightly conversational \u2014 \u201cvalued part of the O''Regan''s VW family\u201d  \n- **Energy Level**: Calm, reassuring, encouraging \u2014 no pressure  \n- **Vocabulary**: \u201csmooth and seamless\u201d, \u201cnavigate the next steps\u201d, \u201cno-pressure chat\u201d  \n- **Vehicle Reference**: Uses \u201cmodel/year/trim\u201d \u2014 e.g., \u201c2022 VW Tiguan\u201d, \u201cComfortline trim\u201d  \n- **Emojis/Punctuation**: None \u2014 clean, no exclamation marks or emojis  \n- **Signature Style**: \u201cWilson Xing | Sales Consultant\u201d \u2014 consistent, branded\n\n---\n\nAlso stay consistent with the rest of the style guide.\n\nRequired format checklist:\n  \u2022 Use a greeting line with the customer''s first name.\n  \u2022 Keep clean paragraph spacing.\n  \u2022 Include a soft CTA paragraph before the sign-off.\n  \u2022 Reference the lease/finance end date in the opening.\n  \u2022 Use the heading \"Your End-of-Lease Options:\".\n  \u2022 Format choices as Option 1 / Option 2 / Option 3 (not generic numbered bullets).\n\nExtra hard rules (non-negotiable):\n  \u2022 make this is fix email ending\nBest regards,\nWilson Xing | Sales Consultant"}]}', '{"choices": [{"finish_reason": "stop", "index": 0, "message": {"role": "assistant", "content": "{\n  \"subject\": \"Your 2022 VW Tiguan is ready\",\n  \"body\": \"Hi Brianna,\\n\\nI hope this email finds you well. As you approach the end of your 2022 VW Tiguan lease on September 16, 2026, we wanted to gently remind you that your next move is right around the corner \u2014 and we\u2019re here to help make it smooth and seamless.\\n\\nYour End-of-Lease Options:\\nOption 1: 2025 Volkswagen Jetta S \u2014 $21,990\\nOption 2: 2025 Volkswagen Golf Base \u2014 $25,990\\nOption 3: Keep your current vehicle with a lease extension (if eligible)\\n\\nWe\u2019d love to connect for a no-pressure chat about what might be the perfect next step for you. No obligation \u2014 just a friendly conversation.\\n\\nWe look forward to assisting you as you navigate this transition. Let us know if you\u2019d like to set up a time to explore these options together.\\n\\nWarmly,\\nWilson Xing | Sales Consultant\"\n}"}}], "created": 1781367524, "model": "Qwen3VL-4B-Instruct-Q4_K_M.gguf", "system_fingerprint": "b9590-d2462f8f7", "object": "chat.completion", "usage": {"completion_tokens": 240, "prompt_tokens": 1022, "total_tokens": 1262, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 485}}, "id": "chatcmpl-H3ZTXgV8GnP9xZeT7jDv50hB4GmCP1uk", "timings": {"cache_n": 485, "prompt_n": 537, "prompt_ms": 1506.477, "prompt_per_token_ms": 2.8053575418994416, "prompt_per_second": 356.46080225585916, "predicted_n": 240, "predicted_ms": 5945.123, "predicted_per_token_ms": 24.77134583333333, "predicted_per_second": 40.36922364768567}}', '2026-06-13 16:18:44.647051+00');
INSERT INTO public.llm_request_logs (id, url, model, input, output, created_at) VALUES (68, 'http://host.docker.internal:8080/v1/chat/completions', 'Qwen3VL-4B-Instruct-Q4_K_M.ggu', '{"model": "Qwen3VL-4B-Instruct-Q4_K_M.ggu", "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a writing style analyst for a car dealership sales team.\nYour task is to study the provided sample messages and distill the writer''s unique communication style\ninto a concise, actionable markdown guide. Another AI will use this guide to write new messages\nthat faithfully match this person''s voice and style.\n\nThe writer''s samples are organized into the following categories:\n- Lease Expiration\n- Test Drive Follow-Up\n\nProduce one ## section for each category that has samples provided, using the exact category name as the ## heading.\nIf any sample does not match a named category, place it under ## General.\nDo NOT produce sections for categories that have no samples.\n\nEach category section MUST contain exactly three sub-sections:\n\n### Subject Line\nDescribe the subject line patterns observed across the samples:\n- Typical length (capture what works in practice; for email this is often around 4-9 words)\n- Tone and urgency (e.g. friendly teaser, direct offer, question)\n- Use of personalisation (customer name, vehicle details)\n- Common openers or formulas (e.g. \"Your [Year] [Model] is ready\", \"Quick update on\u2026\")\n- Capitalisation style (title case, sentence case, all-lower)\n- Use of numbers, emojis, or special characters\n- Anything that makes the subject line pattern recognisable\n\n### Format\nDescribe the structural/layout conventions observed in the samples:\n- Message length (give realistic ranges; avoid strict limits unless samples consistently enforce them)\n- Opening line pattern (greeting style, whether name is used)\n- Body structure (e.g. one hook sentence \u2192 offer \u2192 CTA)\n- Closing line pattern (sign-off, signature style)\n- Paragraph count and spacing habits\n- Use of bullet points, line breaks, or lists\n\n### Style\nDescribe the voice and language patterns:\n- Tone and formality level for this situation\n- Energy level (urgent, warm, casual, professional)\n- Vocabulary preferences and any signature phrases or pet words\n- How they reference vehicles (make/model/year/trim usage)\n- Use of emojis, punctuation quirks, or capitalisation habits\n- Anything that makes this person''s writing instantly recognisable\n\nAfter those required sub-sections, add a short \"### Operational Rules\" section for each category with:\n- Goal (what the email is trying to achieve for this category)\n- Personalization fields to include (e.g. [FirstName], [Year Model], relevant date, [Phone])\n- CTA standard (one primary action at the end)\n- Language guardrails (non-pushy phrasing, no overpromising, no fabricated offers)\n- A 4-6 item quality checklist for before-send review\n\nPrefer specific, reusable rules over abstract advice.\nOutput a clean markdown document. Do NOT include any samples verbatim."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Channel: email\n\n### Lease Expiration\n\nHi Andy\nI hope this email finds you well.\nCan you believe how quickly time flies? We want to remind you that the lease on your 2022 VW Tiguan is scheduled to mature on July 31, 2026.\nAs you approach the end of your lease, you have a few great options available to you, and we want to make sure the transition is as smooth and seamless as possible. Whether you want to upgrade, keep your current ride, or simply hand over the keys, we are here to help you navigate the next steps.\nYour End-of-Lease Options:\nOption 1: Upgrade to a new model. Get behind the wheel of a brand-new vehicle with the latest technology, safety features, and a fresh warranty.\nOption 2: Purchase your current vehicle. If you\u2019ve fallen in love with your car and aren''t ready to part ways, you can buy it out for the residual value listed in your contract.\nOption 3: Return the vehicle. Simply schedule an inspection and return the keys to us at the end of your term.\nLet''s Find the Best Path Forward\nWe would love to invite you back into the dealership for a quick, no-pressure chat to review these options, check out current inventory, and see what specials might apply to you.\nPlease reply directly to this email or call us at 9024076395 to schedule a convenient time for you to drop by.\nThank you so much for being a valued part of the O''Regan''s VW family. We look forward to assisting you with your next automotive chapter!\nWarm regards,\nWilson Xing | Sales Consultant\n\n### Test Drive Follow-Up\n\nHi Andy,\nThank you for taking the time to visit us yesterday and test driving the 2026 Jetta Comfortline. It was a pleasure meeting you and showing you what the Jetta has to offer.\nI completely understand and respect your decision to test drive a few other options in the market before making your final move. Investing in a new vehicle is a big decision, and you want to ensure it\u2019s the perfect fit.\nWhile you are doing your research, I did want to give you a quick heads-up on an incentive that just came up for this month. Volkswagen is currently offering a 0.99% special finance rate for up to 60 months (5 years) on the 2026 Jetta. It\u2019s one of the strongest programs we''ve seen in a while, and it definitely keeps the monthly payments incredibly comfortable on that Comfortline trim.\nIf you have any questions about how those numbers look for your budget while you compare your options, just let me know.\nI would love the opportunity to earn your business. Drive safe during your other test drives, and I look forward to connecting with you soon!\nBest regards,\nWilson Xing | Sales Consultant"}]}', '{"choices": [{"finish_reason": "stop", "index": 0, "message": {"role": "assistant", "content": "## Lease Expiration\n\n### Subject Line\n- **Length**: 4\u20139 words (e.g., \u201cYour Lease Ends July 31\u201d)\n- **Tone**: Friendly, timely, slightly urgent (\u201cCan you believe how quickly time flies?\u201d)\n- **Personalisation**: Uses customer name + vehicle model/year (e.g., \u201cYour 2022 VW Tiguan\u201d)\n- **Openers**: \u201cWe want to remind you that\u2026\u201d or \u201cAs you approach the end\u2026\u201d\n- **Capitalisation**: Title case, no emojis or symbols, clean and professional\n- **Numbers**: Date is included (e.g., \u201cJuly 31, 2026\u201d) \u2014 often in date format\n- **Recognisable pattern**: \u201cYour [Year] [Model] is ready\u201d or \u201cYou\u2019re approaching your lease end\u2026\u201d\n\n### Format\n- **Length**: 5\u20137 paragraphs (no more than 3 bullet lists)\n- **Opening line**: Greeting + casual opener (\u201cI hope this email finds you well.\u201d)\n- **Body structure**: Hook \u2192 options \u2192 call to action \u2192 closing note\n- **Closing line**: Warm, personalized sign-off with signature line (\u201cWarm regards, Wilson Xing | Sales Consultant\u201d)\n- **Paragraphs**: Spaced clearly, no dense blocks \u2014 uses short, scannable sentences\n- **Lists**: Bullet points only for options (no numbering)\n\n### Style\n- **Tone**: Warm, professional, supportive, non-pushy\n- **Energy level**: Calm, reassuring, slightly enthusiastic\n- **Vocabulary**: Uses \u201cnavigate,\u201d \u201ctransition,\u201d \u201cseamless,\u201d \u201cvalue,\u201d \u201cchapter\u201d \u2014 suggests growth and progression\n- **Vehicle references**: Always includes [Year] [Model] + trim (e.g., \u201c2022 VW Tiguan\u201d) \u2014 never generic\n- **Punctuation**: Minimal use of exclamation points; prefers periods and commas\n- **Signature**: Always ends with \u201cWarm regards, Wilson Xing | Sales Consultant\u201d \u2014 consistent branding\n\n### Operational Rules\n\n**Goal**: Remind customer of lease expiration without pressure, offer clarity and options, invite low-pressure follow-up.\n\n**Personalization fields to include**:\n- [FirstName]\n- [Year Model]\n- Lease end date (e.g., July 31, 2026)\n- [Phone]\n\n**CTA standard**:\n- \u201cReply directly to this email or call us at [Phone] to schedule a visit\u201d\n\n**Language guardrails**:\n- Never say \u201cYou must\u2026\u201d or \u201cDon\u2019t miss\u2026\u201d\n- Avoid \u201clast chance\u201d or \u201cfinal offer\u201d \u2014 use \u201coptions available,\u201d \u201cwe\u2019re here to help,\u201d \u201csmooth transition\u201d\n- Don\u2019t overpromise \u2014 mention \u201cresidual value listed in contract,\u201d \u201cspecials may apply\u201d\n\n**Quality checklist (4\u20136 items)**:\n1. Include customer name + exact vehicle model/year in subject and body  \n2. List all 3 clear, benefit-driven options (upgrade, purchase, return)  \n3. Use \u201cWarm regards, Wilson Xing | Sales Consultant\u201d as closing  \n4. Include contact phone number in CTA section  \n5. Avoid aggressive phrasing \u2014 use \u201cwe\u2019re here to help\u201d or \u201cno pressure\u201d  \n6. Confirm lease end date is accurate and formatted as \u201cMonth Day, Year\u201d  \n\n---\n\n## Test Drive Follow-Up\n\n### Subject Line\n- **Length**: 4\u20137 words (e.g., \u201cGreat Test Drive, Andy!\u201d)\n- **Tone**: Friendly, appreciative, light (\u201cI completely understand\u2026\u201d)\n- **Personalisation**: Uses customer name + vehicle model/year (e.g., \u201c2026 Jetta Comfortline\u201d)\n- **Openers**: \u201cThank you for taking the time\u2026\u201d, \u201cI completely understand\u2026\u201d\n- **Capitalisation**: Title case, no emojis\n- **Numbers**: Includes time frame (e.g., \u201cup to 60 months\u201d)\n- **Recognisable pattern**: \u201cYour [Model] was a pleasure to show you\u201d or \u201cI want to give you a quick heads-up\u2026\u201d\n\n### Format\n- **Length**: 3\u20135 paragraphs (often 4)\n- **Opening line**: Personal greeting + appreciation (\u201cThank you for taking the time\u2026\u201d)\n- **Body structure**: Appreciation \u2192 understanding of customer\u2019s process \u2192 offer \u2192 invitation to ask questions\n- **Closing line**: Warm, forward-looking, invitation to reconnect (\u201cI look forward to connecting\u2026\u201d)\n- **Paragraphs**: Short, scannable, each focused on one idea\n- **Lists**: None \u2014 uses natural sentence flow, no bullet points\n\n### Style\n- **Tone**: Warm, conversational, supportive, slightly casual\n- **Energy level**: Enthusiastic but not pushy \u2014 uses phrases like \u201cI want to give you a heads-up\u201d and \u201cDrive safe during your other test drives\u201d\n- **Vocabulary**: \u201cInvesting in a new vehicle is a big decision,\u201d \u201cperfect fit,\u201d \u201ccomfortable monthly payments,\u201d \u201cearn your business\u201d\n- **Vehicle references**: Always includes [Year] [Model] + trim \u2014 \u201c2026 Jetta Comfortline\u201d\n- **Punctuation**: Uses em dashes, colons, and occasional exclamation points for warmth\n- **Signature**: \u201cBest regards, Wilson Xing | Sales Consultant\u201d \u2014 consistent, friendly, no formality\n\n### Operational Rules\n\n**Goal**: Acknowledge test drive, offer timely incentive, invite further conversation without pressure\n\n**Personalization fields to include**:\n- [FirstName]\n- [Year Model] + trim\n- Date of test drive (optional, if relevant)\n\n**CTA standard**:\n- \u201cJust let me know if you have questions\u2026\u201d or \u201cI\u2019d love the opportunity to earn your business\u2026\u201d\n\n**Language guardrails**:\n- Never say \u201cYou should\u2026\u201d or \u201cWe\u2019re offering this because\u2026\u201d\n- Avoid \u201climited-time\u201d or \u201cexclusive\u201d unless factual\n- Use \u201cheads-up,\u201d \u201cquick update,\u201d \u201cno pressure,\u201d \u201cI\u2019m here to help\u201d\n\n**Quality checklist (4\u20136 items)**:\n1. Include customer name + exact vehicle model/trim in greeting  \n2. Mention test date if relevant (optional but helpful)  \n3. Describe incentive clearly: \u201c0.99% rate for up to 60 months\u201d  \n4. Use \u201cI\u2019d love the opportunity to earn your business\u201d or similar  \n5. Avoid \u201cyou have to\u201d or \u201cyou must\u201d \u2014 use \u201cif you have questions\u2026\u201d  \n6. End with warm, non-compressing closing: \u201cDrive safe\u2026 I look forward to connecting soon!\u201d"}}], "created": 1781367827, "model": "Qwen3VL-4B-Instruct-Q4_K_M.gguf", "system_fingerprint": "b9590-d2462f8f7", "object": "chat.completion", "usage": {"completion_tokens": 1377, "prompt_tokens": 1178, "total_tokens": 2555, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0}}, "id": "chatcmpl-Df3lF0TCR95vDutXnkD8KzKQnbpmh0xE", "timings": {"cache_n": 0, "prompt_n": 1178, "prompt_ms": 4784.749, "prompt_per_token_ms": 4.06175636672326, "prompt_per_second": 246.19891241943935, "predicted_n": 1377, "predicted_ms": 34410.732, "predicted_per_token_ms": 24.98963834422658, "predicted_per_second": 40.01658552337683}}', '2026-06-13 16:23:47.6015+00');
INSERT INTO public.llm_request_logs (id, url, model, input, output, created_at) VALUES (69, 'http://host.docker.internal:8080/v1/chat/completions', 'Qwen3VL-4B-Instruct-Q4_K_M.ggu', '{"model": "Qwen3VL-4B-Instruct-Q4_K_M.ggu", "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are an AI email-writing assistant for a car dealership sales representative.\nYour task is to compose a personalised outreach email to a specific customer.\n\nYou will receive:\n1. Email purpose (the reason for reaching out)\n2. Customer profile (name, note, vehicles they own/lease)\n3. Matching inventory vehicles that may be relevant to this customer\n4. The sales representative''s writing style guide (in Markdown)\n5. Customer''s full contact log (channel, date, summary of each prior interaction)\n\nRules:\n- Match the representative''s voice and style exactly as described in the style guide\n- Treat any \"Extra hard rules\" as mandatory requirements that override default phrasing\n- If the style guide includes a concrete format template, headings, or option-label pattern, follow it exactly\n- Make the email feel personal and relevant to this specific customer''s situation\n- Use the contact log to avoid repeating topics already covered, acknowledge the relationship naturally, and pick up where the last conversation left off\n- Reference their vehicle(s) naturally (e.g., lease end dates, age, type)\n- Mention 1-2 inventory options at most; do not list every car\n- Follow the word count and paragraph count specified in the style guide; if unspecified, target 180\u2013260 words\n- Always include a warm closing paragraph thanking the customer, a soft CTA (reply or call), and a professional sign-off with name and title\n- Do NOT include a subject line in the body\n- Respond ONLY with a JSON object in the exact format:\n  {\"subject\": \"...\", \"body\": \"...\"}"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Email purpose: The customer''s lease or financing is ending soon. Write an email about upgrade options and next steps.\n\nCustomer: Brianna C Algee\n\nNote: (none)\n\nCustomer vehicles:\n  \u2022 2022 VOLKSWAGEN TIGUAN (lease) lease ends 2026-09-16\n\nRelevant inventory:\n  \u2022 2025 Volkswagen Jetta S $21,990\n  \u2022 2025 Volkswagen Golf Base $25,990\n\nContact history (newest first):\n  (no prior contact logged)\n\nStyle guide:\nPrimary section to follow for this email type:\n## Lease Expiration\n\n### Subject Line\n- **Length**: 4\u20139 words (e.g., \u201cYour Lease Ends July 31\u201d)\n- **Tone**: Friendly, timely, slightly urgent (\u201cCan you believe how quickly time flies?\u201d)\n- **Personalisation**: Uses customer name + vehicle model/year (e.g., \u201cYour 2022 VW Tiguan\u201d)\n- **Openers**: \u201cWe want to remind you that\u2026\u201d or \u201cAs you approach the end\u2026\u201d\n- **Capitalisation**: Title case, no emojis or symbols, clean and professional\n- **Numbers**: Date is included (e.g., \u201cJuly 31, 2026\u201d) \u2014 often in date format\n- **Recognisable pattern**: \u201cYour [Year] [Model] is ready\u201d or \u201cYou\u2019re approaching your lease end\u2026\u201d\n\n### Format\n- **Length**: 5\u20137 paragraphs (no more than 3 bullet lists)\n- **Opening line**: Greeting + casual opener (\u201cI hope this email finds you well.\u201d)\n- **Body structure**: Hook \u2192 options \u2192 call to action \u2192 closing note\n- **Closing line**: Warm, personalized sign-off with signature line (\u201cWarm regards, Wilson Xing | Sales Consultant\u201d)\n- **Paragraphs**: Spaced clearly, no dense blocks \u2014 uses short, scannable sentences\n- **Lists**: Bullet points only for options (no numbering)\n\n### Style\n- **Tone**: Warm, professional, supportive, non-pushy\n- **Energy level**: Calm, reassuring, slightly enthusiastic\n- **Vocabulary**: Uses \u201cnavigate,\u201d \u201ctransition,\u201d \u201cseamless,\u201d \u201cvalue,\u201d \u201cchapter\u201d \u2014 suggests growth and progression\n- **Vehicle references**: Always includes [Year] [Model] + trim (e.g., \u201c2022 VW Tiguan\u201d) \u2014 never generic\n- **Punctuation**: Minimal use of exclamation points; prefers periods and commas\n- **Signature**: Always ends with \u201cWarm regards, Wilson Xing | Sales Consultant\u201d \u2014 consistent branding\n\n### Operational Rules\n\n**Goal**: Remind customer of lease expiration without pressure, offer clarity and options, invite low-pressure follow-up.\n\n**Personalization fields to include**:\n- [FirstName]\n- [Year Model]\n- Lease end date (e.g., July 31, 2026)\n- [Phone]\n\n**CTA standard**:\n- \u201cReply directly to this email or call us at [Phone] to schedule a visit\u201d\n\n**Language guardrails**:\n- Never say \u201cYou must\u2026\u201d or \u201cDon\u2019t miss\u2026\u201d\n- Avoid \u201clast chance\u201d or \u201cfinal offer\u201d \u2014 use \u201coptions available,\u201d \u201cwe\u2019re here to help,\u201d \u201csmooth transition\u201d\n- Don\u2019t overpromise \u2014 mention \u201cresidual value listed in contract,\u201d \u201cspecials may apply\u201d\n\n**Quality checklist (4\u20136 items)**:\n1. Include customer name + exact vehicle model/year in subject and body  \n2. List all 3 clear, benefit-driven options (upgrade, purchase, return)  \n3. Use \u201cWarm regards, Wilson Xing | Sales Consultant\u201d as closing  \n4. Include contact phone number in CTA section  \n5. Avoid aggressive phrasing \u2014 use \u201cwe\u2019re here to help\u201d or \u201cno pressure\u201d  \n6. Confirm lease end date is accurate and formatted as \u201cMonth Day, Year\u201d  \n\n---\n\nAlso stay consistent with the rest of the style guide.\n\nRequired format checklist:\n  \u2022 Use a greeting line with the customer''s first name.\n  \u2022 Keep clean paragraph spacing.\n  \u2022 Include a soft CTA paragraph before the sign-off.\n  \u2022 Reference the lease/finance end date in the opening.\n\nExtra hard rules (non-negotiable):\n  \u2022 make this is fix email ending\nBest regards,\nWilson Xing | Sales Consultant"}]}', '{"choices": [{"finish_reason": "stop", "index": 0, "message": {"role": "assistant", "content": "{\n  \"subject\": \"Your 2022 VW Tiguan is ready\",\n  \"body\": \"Hi Brianna,\\n\\nI hope this email finds you well. As you approach the end of your lease on September 16, 2026, we wanted to gently remind you that your 2022 VW Tiguan is entering its next chapter \u2014 and we\u2019re here to help you navigate that transition with ease.\\n\\nHere are a few options to consider:\\n- Upgrade to a 2025 Volkswagen Jetta S \u2014 $21,990, offering sleek styling and smart tech.\\n- Explore the 2025 Volkswagen Golf Base \u2014 $25,990, perfect for those who appreciate refined driving dynamics.\\n- Return your vehicle and restart your journey with a new car \u2014 we\u2019ll help you find the right fit.\\n\\nWe\u2019re not rushing, and we\u2019re not pushing \u2014 just here to offer clarity, value, and a seamless experience. If any of these feel right, or if you\u2019d prefer to chat about next steps, feel free to reply directly to this email or call us at [Phone] to schedule a visit.\\n\\nWe\u2019re excited to help you move forward \u2014 whether you\u2019re upgrading, purchasing, or rethinking your next ride.\\n\\nWarm regards,\\nWilson Xing | Sales Consultant\"\n}"}}], "created": 1781367850, "model": "Qwen3VL-4B-Instruct-Q4_K_M.gguf", "system_fingerprint": "b9590-d2462f8f7", "object": "chat.completion", "usage": {"completion_tokens": 289, "prompt_tokens": 1264, "total_tokens": 1553, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 489}}, "id": "chatcmpl-6BlzGaWcpSUDtoOVkihZQzV8gprk41ZU", "timings": {"cache_n": 489, "prompt_n": 775, "prompt_ms": 2217.567, "prompt_per_token_ms": 2.8613767741935483, "prompt_per_second": 349.4821126035876, "predicted_n": 289, "predicted_ms": 7587.838, "predicted_per_token_ms": 26.25549480968858, "predicted_per_second": 38.087265437137695}}', '2026-06-13 16:24:10.76318+00');
INSERT INTO public.llm_request_logs (id, url, model, input, output, created_at) VALUES (70, 'http://host.docker.internal:8080/v1/chat/completions', 'Qwen3VL-4B-Instruct-Q4_K_M.ggu', '{"model": "Qwen3VL-4B-Instruct-Q4_K_M.ggu", "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are an AI email-writing assistant for a car dealership sales representative.\nYour task is to compose a personalised outreach email to a specific customer.\n\nYou will receive:\n1. Email purpose (the reason for reaching out)\n2. Customer profile (name, note, vehicles they own/lease)\n3. Matching inventory vehicles that may be relevant to this customer\n4. The sales representative''s writing style guide (in Markdown)\n5. Customer''s full contact log (channel, date, summary of each prior interaction)\n\nRules:\n- Match the representative''s voice and style exactly as described in the style guide\n- Treat any \"Extra hard rules\" as mandatory requirements that override default phrasing\n- If the style guide includes a concrete format template, headings, or option-label pattern, follow it exactly\n- Make the email feel personal and relevant to this specific customer''s situation\n- Use the contact log to avoid repeating topics already covered, acknowledge the relationship naturally, and pick up where the last conversation left off\n- Reference their vehicle(s) naturally (e.g., lease end dates, age, type)\n- Mention 1-2 inventory options at most; do not list every car\n- Follow the word count and paragraph count specified in the style guide; if unspecified, target 180\u2013260 words\n- Always include a warm closing paragraph thanking the customer, a soft CTA (reply or call), and a professional sign-off with name and title\n- For lease/finance ending emails, prioritize a lease-end guidance format (upgrade vs buyout vs return) over inventory sales copy\n- Do NOT turn lease-end emails into price-led inventory advertisements unless explicitly requested by the user template/rules\n- Do NOT include a subject line in the body\n- Respond ONLY with a JSON object in the exact format:\n  {\"subject\": \"...\", \"body\": \"...\"}"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Email purpose: The customer''s lease or financing is ending soon. Write an email about upgrade options and next steps.\n\nCustomer: Brianna C Algee\n\nCustomer phone: (902) 225-9368\n\nNote: (none)\n\nCustomer vehicles:\n  \u2022 2022 VOLKSWAGEN TIGUAN (lease) lease ends 2026-09-16\n\nRelevant inventory:\n  \u2022 2025 Volkswagen Jetta S $21,990\n  \u2022 2025 Volkswagen Golf Base $25,990\n\nContact history (newest first):\n  (no prior contact logged)\n\nStyle guide:\nPrimary section to follow for this email type:\n## Lease Expiration\n\n### Subject Line\n- **Length**: 4\u20139 words (e.g., \u201cYour Lease Ends July 31\u201d)\n- **Tone**: Friendly, timely, slightly urgent (\u201cCan you believe how quickly time flies?\u201d)\n- **Personalisation**: Uses customer name + vehicle model/year (e.g., \u201cYour 2022 VW Tiguan\u201d)\n- **Openers**: \u201cWe want to remind you that\u2026\u201d or \u201cAs you approach the end\u2026\u201d\n- **Capitalisation**: Title case, no emojis or symbols, clean and professional\n- **Numbers**: Date is included (e.g., \u201cJuly 31, 2026\u201d) \u2014 often in date format\n- **Recognisable pattern**: \u201cYour [Year] [Model] is ready\u201d or \u201cYou\u2019re approaching your lease end\u2026\u201d\n\n### Format\n- **Length**: 5\u20137 paragraphs (no more than 3 bullet lists)\n- **Opening line**: Greeting + casual opener (\u201cI hope this email finds you well.\u201d)\n- **Body structure**: Hook \u2192 options \u2192 call to action \u2192 closing note\n- **Closing line**: Warm, personalized sign-off with signature line (\u201cWarm regards, Wilson Xing | Sales Consultant\u201d)\n- **Paragraphs**: Spaced clearly, no dense blocks \u2014 uses short, scannable sentences\n- **Lists**: Bullet points only for options (no numbering)\n\n### Style\n- **Tone**: Warm, professional, supportive, non-pushy\n- **Energy level**: Calm, reassuring, slightly enthusiastic\n- **Vocabulary**: Uses \u201cnavigate,\u201d \u201ctransition,\u201d \u201cseamless,\u201d \u201cvalue,\u201d \u201cchapter\u201d \u2014 suggests growth and progression\n- **Vehicle references**: Always includes [Year] [Model] + trim (e.g., \u201c2022 VW Tiguan\u201d) \u2014 never generic\n- **Punctuation**: Minimal use of exclamation points; prefers periods and commas\n- **Signature**: Always ends with \u201cWarm regards, Wilson Xing | Sales Consultant\u201d \u2014 consistent branding\n\n### Operational Rules\n\n**Goal**: Remind customer of lease expiration without pressure, offer clarity and options, invite low-pressure follow-up.\n\n**Personalization fields to include**:\n- [FirstName]\n- [Year Model]\n- Lease end date (e.g., July 31, 2026)\n- [Phone]\n\n**CTA standard**:\n- \u201cReply directly to this email or call us at [Phone] to schedule a visit\u201d\n\n**Language guardrails**:\n- Never say \u201cYou must\u2026\u201d or \u201cDon\u2019t miss\u2026\u201d\n- Avoid \u201clast chance\u201d or \u201cfinal offer\u201d \u2014 use \u201coptions available,\u201d \u201cwe\u2019re here to help,\u201d \u201csmooth transition\u201d\n- Don\u2019t overpromise \u2014 mention \u201cresidual value listed in contract,\u201d \u201cspecials may apply\u201d\n\n**Quality checklist (4\u20136 items)**:\n1. Include customer name + exact vehicle model/year in subject and body  \n2. List all 3 clear, benefit-driven options (upgrade, purchase, return)  \n3. Use \u201cWarm regards, Wilson Xing | Sales Consultant\u201d as closing  \n4. Include contact phone number in CTA section  \n5. Avoid aggressive phrasing \u2014 use \u201cwe\u2019re here to help\u201d or \u201cno pressure\u201d  \n6. Confirm lease end date is accurate and formatted as \u201cMonth Day, Year\u201d  \n\n---\n\nAlso stay consistent with the rest of the style guide.\n\nRequired format checklist:\n  \u2022 Use a greeting line with the customer''s first name.\n  \u2022 Keep clean paragraph spacing.\n  \u2022 Include a soft CTA paragraph before the sign-off.\n  \u2022 Reference the lease/finance end date in the opening.\n\nExtra hard rules (non-negotiable):\n  \u2022 make this is fix email ending\nBest regards,\nWilson Xing | Sales Consultant"}]}', '{"choices": [{"finish_reason": "stop", "index": 0, "message": {"role": "assistant", "content": "{\n  \"subject\": \"Your 2022 VW Tiguan is ready\",\n  \"body\": \"Hi Brianna,\\n\\nWe want to remind you that your 2022 Volkswagen Tiguan lease ends on September 16, 2026 \u2014 and we\u2019re here to help you navigate the next chapter smoothly.\\n\\nYou have a few options: upgrade to a newer model, purchase your current vehicle, or return it with no hassle. We\u2019ve got a couple of great inventory options to explore:\\n\\n\u2022 2025 Volkswagen Jetta S \u2014 $21,990, great for those who want a refreshed sedan with smart tech.\\n\u2022 2025 Volkswagen Golf Base \u2014 $25,990, a sporty, efficient compact car perfect for daily driving.\\n\\nNo pressure \u2014 we\u2019re here to support you, not push anything. If you\u2019d like to chat about what fits your lifestyle or budget, just reply to this email or call us at (902) 225-9368 to schedule a visit.\\n\\nWarm regards,\\nWilson Xing | Sales Consultant\"\n}"}}], "created": 1781368304, "model": "Qwen3VL-4B-Instruct-Q4_K_M.gguf", "system_fingerprint": "b9590-d2462f8f7", "object": "chat.completion", "usage": {"completion_tokens": 246, "prompt_tokens": 1330, "total_tokens": 1576, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 299}}, "id": "chatcmpl-BzX1x7rGrk0bpCYCPGLAosu568dw5FG0", "timings": {"cache_n": 299, "prompt_n": 1031, "prompt_ms": 4808.847, "prompt_per_token_ms": 4.6642550921435495, "prompt_per_second": 214.39650710450965, "predicted_n": 246, "predicted_ms": 6434.532, "predicted_per_token_ms": 26.156634146341464, "predicted_per_second": 38.23121868070592}}', '2026-06-13 16:31:44.424865+00');
INSERT INTO public.llm_request_logs (id, url, model, input, output, created_at) VALUES (71, 'http://host.docker.internal:8080/v1/chat/completions', 'Qwen3VL-4B-Instruct-Q4_K_M.ggu', '{"model": "Qwen3VL-4B-Instruct-Q4_K_M.ggu", "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a writing style analyst for a car dealership sales team.\nYour task is to study the provided sample messages and distill the writer''s unique communication style\ninto a concise, actionable markdown guide. Another AI will use this guide to write new messages\nthat faithfully match this person''s voice and style.\n\nThe writer''s samples are organized into the following categories:\n- Lease Expiration\n- Test Drive Follow-Up\n\nProduce one ## section for each category that has samples provided, using the exact category name as the ## heading.\nIf any sample does not match a named category, place it under ## General.\nDo NOT produce sections for categories that have no samples.\n\nEach category section MUST contain exactly three sub-sections:\n\n### Subject Line\nDescribe the subject line patterns observed across the samples:\n- Typical length (capture what works in practice; for email this is often around 4-9 words)\n- Tone and urgency (e.g. friendly teaser, direct offer, question)\n- Use of personalisation (customer name, vehicle details)\n- Common openers or formulas (e.g. \"Your [Year] [Model] is ready\", \"Quick update on\u2026\")\n- Capitalisation style (title case, sentence case, all-lower)\n- Use of numbers, emojis, or special characters\n- Anything that makes the subject line pattern recognisable\n\n### Format\nDescribe the structural/layout conventions observed in the samples:\n- Message length (give realistic ranges; avoid strict limits unless samples consistently enforce them)\n- Opening line pattern (greeting style, whether name is used)\n- Body structure (e.g. one hook sentence \u2192 offer \u2192 CTA)\n- Closing line pattern (sign-off, signature style)\n- Paragraph count and spacing habits\n- Use of bullet points, line breaks, or lists\n\n### Style\nDescribe the voice and language patterns:\n- Tone and formality level for this situation\n- Energy level (urgent, warm, casual, professional)\n- Vocabulary preferences and any signature phrases or pet words\n- How they reference vehicles (make/model/year/trim usage)\n- Use of emojis, punctuation quirks, or capitalisation habits\n- Anything that makes this person''s writing instantly recognisable\n- If the closing/signature phrase is consistent, capture the exact required wording verbatim in quotes\n\nAfter those required sub-sections, add a short \"### Operational Rules\" section for each category with:\n- Goal (what the email is trying to achieve for this category)\n- Personalization fields to include (e.g. [FirstName], [Year Model], relevant date, [Phone])\n- CTA standard (one primary action at the end)\n- Language guardrails (non-pushy phrasing, no overpromising, no fabricated offers)\n- A 4-6 item quality checklist for before-send review\n- For lease/finance ending categories, if samples use a named options block, explicitly define the required heading and option-label format (e.g., \"Option 1/2/3\")\n\nPrefer specific, reusable rules over abstract advice.\nOutput a clean markdown document. Do NOT include any samples verbatim."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Channel: email\n\n### Lease Expiration\n\nHi Andy\nI hope this email finds you well.\nCan you believe how quickly time flies? We want to remind you that the lease on your 2022 VW Tiguan is scheduled to mature on July 31, 2026.\nAs you approach the end of your lease, you have a few great options available to you, and we want to make sure the transition is as smooth and seamless as possible. Whether you want to upgrade, keep your current ride, or simply hand over the keys, we are here to help you navigate the next steps.\nYour End-of-Lease Options:\nOption 1: Upgrade to a new model. Get behind the wheel of a brand-new vehicle with the latest technology, safety features, and a fresh warranty.\nOption 2: Purchase your current vehicle. If you\u2019ve fallen in love with your car and aren''t ready to part ways, you can buy it out for the residual value listed in your contract.\nOption 3: Return the vehicle. Simply schedule an inspection and return the keys to us at the end of your term.\nLet''s Find the Best Path Forward\nWe would love to invite you back into the dealership for a quick, no-pressure chat to review these options, check out current inventory, and see what specials might apply to you.\nPlease reply directly to this email or call us at 9024076395 to schedule a convenient time for you to drop by.\nThank you so much for being a valued part of the O''Regan''s VW family. We look forward to assisting you with your next automotive chapter!\nWarm regards,\nWilson Xing | Sales Consultant\n\n### Test Drive Follow-Up\n\nHi Andy,\nThank you for taking the time to visit us yesterday and test driving the 2026 Jetta Comfortline. It was a pleasure meeting you and showing you what the Jetta has to offer.\nI completely understand and respect your decision to test drive a few other options in the market before making your final move. Investing in a new vehicle is a big decision, and you want to ensure it\u2019s the perfect fit.\nWhile you are doing your research, I did want to give you a quick heads-up on an incentive that just came up for this month. Volkswagen is currently offering a 0.99% special finance rate for up to 60 months (5 years) on the 2026 Jetta. It\u2019s one of the strongest programs we''ve seen in a while, and it definitely keeps the monthly payments incredibly comfortable on that Comfortline trim.\nIf you have any questions about how those numbers look for your budget while you compare your options, just let me know.\nI would love the opportunity to earn your business. Drive safe during your other test drives, and I look forward to connecting with you soon!\nBest regards,\nWilson Xing | Sales Consultant"}]}', '{"choices": [{"finish_reason": "stop", "index": 0, "message": {"role": "assistant", "content": "## Lease Expiration\n\n### Subject Line\n- **Length**: 4\u20139 words (e.g., \u201cYour Lease Ends July 31\u201d or \u201cLast Chance to Upgrade\u201d)\n- **Tone**: Friendly, urgent but not alarming; uses \u201creminder\u201d or \u201cfinal opportunity\u201d cues\n- **Personalisation**: Always includes customer name + vehicle model/year (e.g., \u201cAndy, your 2022 VW Tiguan\u201d)\n- **Openers**: \u201cCan you believe how quickly time flies?\u201d \u2192 soft hook + relatability\n- **Capitalisation**: Title case only; no emojis or special characters\n- **Numbers/Emojis**: Uses dates clearly; avoids emojis unless minimal context (e.g., \u201cJuly 31, 2026\u201d)\n- **Pattern**: Always starts with vehicle reference, then transitions to options\n\n### Format\n- **Length**: 6\u20138 paragraphs; concise but detailed\n- **Opening**: Greeting + soft hook + direct vehicle/lease reference\n- **Body structure**: Hook \u2192 offer summary \u2192 numbered options \u2192 CTA \u2192 gratitude\n- **Closing**: Signature line with \u201cWarm regards\u201d + full name/title\n- **Spacing**: Single paragraph spacing; no bullet points or lists beyond numbered options\n- **CTA**: Always ends with \u201creply to this email or call\u2026\u201d with phone number\n\n### Style\n- **Tone**: Warm, professional, slightly conversational \u2014 \u201cwe want to make sure\u2026\u201d \u201cyou\u2019re in good hands\u201d\n- **Energy level**: Calm urgency \u2014 not pushy, but proactive\n- **Vocabulary**: \u201cseamless transition,\u201d \u201cnavigate the next steps,\u201d \u201cno-pressure chat\u201d\n- **Vehicle reference**: Always uses exact model/year/trim (e.g., \u201c2022 VW Tiguan\u201d) \u2014 never vague\n- **Signature**: Always ends with \u201cWarm regards, Wilson Xing | Sales Consultant\u201d\n- **Emojis/Punctuation**: None used \u2014 clean, professional format\n\n### Operational Rules\n\n- **Goal**: Remind customer of lease expiration and offer clear, low-pressure next steps (upgrade, purchase, return)\n- **Personalization fields**: [FirstName], [Year Model], [Phone], [Date of Lease Maturity]\n- **CTA standard**: \u201cReply to this email or call [Phone] to schedule a time\u201d\n- **Language guardrails**:\n  - Never say \u201cyou must\u201d or \u201cyou\u2019ll regret\u201d\n  - Avoid fabricated offers \u2014 use \u201clisted in your contract\u201d or \u201cresidual value\u201d\n  - No \u201cguaranteed\u201d or \u201cbest deal\u201d \u2014 keep it realistic\n- **4\u20136 item quality checklist**:\n  1. Is the lease expiration date clearly stated?\n  2. Are the three options numbered and clearly described?\n  3. Is the CTA actionable and include phone number?\n  4. Does the message include a warm, non-pushy closing?\n  5. Is [FirstName] and [Year Model] included?\n  6. Does the tone match \u201cwe\u2019re here to help, not sell\u201d?\n\n---\n\n## Test Drive Follow-Up\n\n### Subject Line\n- **Length**: 4\u20137 words (e.g., \u201cGreat Test Drive, Andy!\u201d or \u201cYour Jetta Incentive\u201d)\n- **Tone**: Friendly, appreciative, slightly enthusiastic (not salesy)\n- **Personalisation**: Always includes customer name + vehicle model/year (e.g., \u201cAndy, 2026 Jetta Comfortline\u201d)\n- **Openers**: \u201cThank you for taking the time\u2026\u201d or \u201cI completely understand\u2026\u201d \u2192 builds trust\n- **Capitalisation**: Title case; no emojis or symbols\n- **Numbers/Emojis**: Uses \u201c0.99%\u201d and \u201c60 months\u201d \u2014 clear, precise, no fluff\n- **Pattern**: Starts with gratitude \u2192 validates customer\u2019s decision \u2192 introduces incentive \u2192 ends with open door for questions\n\n### Format\n- **Length**: 4\u20136 paragraphs; tight and conversational\n- **Opening**: Friendly greeting + appreciation + vehicle reference\n- **Body structure**: Gratitude \u2192 understanding of customer\u2019s process \u2192 incentive hook \u2192 open invitation for questions\n- **Closing**: \u201cBest regards,\u201d + full name/title\n- **Spacing**: Paragraphs are spaced with 1\u20132 lines between; no bullet points\n- **CTA**: \u201cJust let me know if you\u2019d like to explore how this looks for your budget\u201d\n\n### Style\n- **Tone**: Warm, casual, professional \u2014 \u201cI completely understand\u201d \u2192 \u201cI would love the opportunity to earn your business\u201d\n- **Energy level**: Encouraging, not urgent \u2014 \u201cDrive safe during your other test drives\u201d\n- **Vocabulary**: \u201cInvesting in a new vehicle is a big decision,\u201d \u201ckeep the monthly payments incredibly comfortable\u201d\n- **Vehicle reference**: Always uses exact model/year/trim (e.g., \u201c2026 Jetta Comfortline\u201d) \u2014 never vague\n- **Signature**: Always ends with \u201cBest regards, Wilson Xing | Sales Consultant\u201d\n- **Emojis/Punctuation**: None \u2014 clean, conversational, no exclamation overload\n\n### Operational Rules\n\n- **Goal**: Reinforce value of test drive + offer incentive without pressure; encourage return conversation\n- **Personalization fields**: [FirstName], [Year Model], [Incentive Details], [Phone]\n- **CTA standard**: \u201cJust let me know if you\u2019d like to explore how this looks for your budget\u201d\n- **Language guardrails**:\n  - No \u201cwe\u2019re offering you the best deal\u201d \u2014 use \u201cone of the strongest programs we\u2019ve seen\u201d\n  - Avoid \u201cyou should\u201d or \u201cyou\u2019ll love\u201d \u2014 use \u201cyou might want to consider\u2026\u201d\n  - No \u201climited time\u201d \u2014 keep it factual: \u201cthis month\u201d\n- **4\u20136 item quality checklist**:\n  1. Is the customer\u2019s name and vehicle model included?\n  2. Is the incentive described clearly with numbers (0.99%, 60 months)?\n  3. Does the message validate the customer\u2019s decision to test drive others?\n  4. Is the CTA open-ended and non-pressure (\u201cjust let me know\u201d)?\n  5. Does the closing feel personal and appreciative?\n  6. Is the signature consistent: \u201cBest regards, Wilson Xing | Sales Consultant\u201d?"}}], "created": 1781368541, "model": "Qwen3VL-4B-Instruct-Q4_K_M.gguf", "system_fingerprint": "b9590-d2462f8f7", "object": "chat.completion", "usage": {"completion_tokens": 1329, "prompt_tokens": 1236, "total_tokens": 2565, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 1235}}, "id": "chatcmpl-tkpQb6tJOfdEdMNkohiKLHs9dhJswpPN", "timings": {"cache_n": 1235, "prompt_n": 1, "prompt_ms": 92.885, "prompt_per_token_ms": 92.885, "prompt_per_second": 10.766000968940087, "predicted_n": 1329, "predicted_ms": 33758.059, "predicted_per_token_ms": 25.4010978179082, "predicted_per_second": 39.36837719253942}}', '2026-06-13 16:35:41.435989+00');
INSERT INTO public.llm_request_logs (id, url, model, input, output, created_at) VALUES (72, 'http://host.docker.internal:8080/v1/chat/completions', 'Qwen3VL-4B-Instruct-Q4_K_M.ggu', '{"model": "Qwen3VL-4B-Instruct-Q4_K_M.ggu", "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are an AI email-writing assistant for a car dealership sales representative.\nYour task is to compose a personalised outreach email to a specific customer.\n\nYou will receive:\n1. Email purpose (the reason for reaching out)\n2. Customer profile (name, note, vehicles they own/lease)\n3. Matching inventory vehicles that may be relevant to this customer\n4. The sales representative''s writing style guide (in Markdown)\n5. Customer''s full contact log (channel, date, summary of each prior interaction)\n\nRules:\n- Match the representative''s voice and style exactly as described in the style guide\n- Treat any \"Extra hard rules\" as mandatory requirements that override default phrasing\n- If the style guide includes a concrete format template, headings, or option-label pattern, follow it exactly\n- Make the email feel personal and relevant to this specific customer''s situation\n- Use the contact log to avoid repeating topics already covered, acknowledge the relationship naturally, and pick up where the last conversation left off\n- Reference their vehicle(s) naturally (e.g., lease end dates, age, type)\n- Mention 1-2 inventory options at most; do not list every car\n- Follow the word count and paragraph count specified in the style guide; if unspecified, target 180\u2013260 words\n- Always include a warm closing paragraph thanking the customer, a soft CTA (reply or call), and a professional sign-off with name and title\n- For lease/finance ending emails, prioritize a lease-end guidance format (upgrade vs buyout vs return) over inventory sales copy\n- Do NOT turn lease-end emails into price-led inventory advertisements unless explicitly requested by the user template/rules\n- Do NOT include a subject line in the body\n- Respond ONLY with a JSON object in the exact format:\n  {\"subject\": \"...\", \"body\": \"...\"}"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Email purpose: The customer''s lease or financing is ending soon. Write an email about upgrade options and next steps.\n\nCustomer: Brianna C Algee\n\nCustomer phone: (902) 225-9368\n\nNote: (none)\n\nCustomer vehicles:\n  \u2022 2022 VOLKSWAGEN TIGUAN (lease) lease ends 2026-09-16\n\nRelevant inventory:\n  \u2022 2025 Volkswagen Jetta S $21,990\n  \u2022 2025 Volkswagen Golf Base $25,990\n\nContact history (newest first):\n  (no prior contact logged)\n\nStyle guide:\nPrimary section to follow for this email type:\n## Lease Expiration\n\n### Subject Line\n- **Length**: 4\u20139 words (e.g., \u201cYour Lease Ends July 31\u201d or \u201cLast Chance to Upgrade\u201d)\n- **Tone**: Friendly, urgent but not alarming; uses \u201creminder\u201d or \u201cfinal opportunity\u201d cues\n- **Personalisation**: Always includes customer name + vehicle model/year (e.g., \u201cAndy, your 2022 VW Tiguan\u201d)\n- **Openers**: \u201cCan you believe how quickly time flies?\u201d \u2192 soft hook + relatability\n- **Capitalisation**: Title case only; no emojis or special characters\n- **Numbers/Emojis**: Uses dates clearly; avoids emojis unless minimal context (e.g., \u201cJuly 31, 2026\u201d)\n- **Pattern**: Always starts with vehicle reference, then transitions to options\n\n### Format\n- **Length**: 6\u20138 paragraphs; concise but detailed\n- **Opening**: Greeting + soft hook + direct vehicle/lease reference\n- **Body structure**: Hook \u2192 offer summary \u2192 numbered options \u2192 CTA \u2192 gratitude\n- **Closing**: Signature line with \u201cWarm regards\u201d + full name/title\n- **Spacing**: Single paragraph spacing; no bullet points or lists beyond numbered options\n- **CTA**: Always ends with \u201creply to this email or call\u2026\u201d with phone number\n\n### Style\n- **Tone**: Warm, professional, slightly conversational \u2014 \u201cwe want to make sure\u2026\u201d \u201cyou\u2019re in good hands\u201d\n- **Energy level**: Calm urgency \u2014 not pushy, but proactive\n- **Vocabulary**: \u201cseamless transition,\u201d \u201cnavigate the next steps,\u201d \u201cno-pressure chat\u201d\n- **Vehicle reference**: Always uses exact model/year/trim (e.g., \u201c2022 VW Tiguan\u201d) \u2014 never vague\n- **Signature**: Always ends with \u201cWarm regards, Wilson Xing | Sales Consultant\u201d\n- **Emojis/Punctuation**: None used \u2014 clean, professional format\n\n### Operational Rules\n\n- **Goal**: Remind customer of lease expiration and offer clear, low-pressure next steps (upgrade, purchase, return)\n- **Personalization fields**: [FirstName], [Year Model], [Phone], [Date of Lease Maturity]\n- **CTA standard**: \u201cReply to this email or call [Phone] to schedule a time\u201d\n- **Language guardrails**:\n  - Never say \u201cyou must\u201d or \u201cyou\u2019ll regret\u201d\n  - Avoid fabricated offers \u2014 use \u201clisted in your contract\u201d or \u201cresidual value\u201d\n  - No \u201cguaranteed\u201d or \u201cbest deal\u201d \u2014 keep it realistic\n- **4\u20136 item quality checklist**:\n  1. Is the lease expiration date clearly stated?\n  2. Are the three options numbered and clearly described?\n  3. Is the CTA actionable and include phone number?\n  4. Does the message include a warm, non-pushy closing?\n  5. Is [FirstName] and [Year Model] included?\n  6. Does the tone match \u201cwe\u2019re here to help, not sell\u201d?\n\n---\n\nAlso stay consistent with the rest of the style guide.\n\nRequired format checklist:\n  \u2022 Use a greeting line with the customer''s first name.\n  \u2022 Keep clean paragraph spacing.\n  \u2022 Include a soft CTA paragraph before the sign-off.\n  \u2022 Reference the lease/finance end date in the opening.\n\nExtra hard rules (non-negotiable):\n  \u2022 make this is fix email ending\nBest regards,\nWilson Xing | Sales Consultant"}]}', '{"choices": [{"finish_reason": "stop", "index": 0, "message": {"role": "assistant", "content": "{\n  \"subject\": \"Brianna, Your 2022 VW Tiguan Lease Ends Sept 16\",\n  \"body\": \"Can you believe how quickly time flies? We\u2019re reaching the end of your 2022 VW Tiguan lease \u2014 it ends on September 16, 2026. We want to make sure you\u2019re in good hands as you navigate the next steps.\\n\\nHere\u2019s a quick overview of how you can continue driving with us:\\n1. Upgrade to a new 2025 VW Jetta S \u2014 listed at $21,990 with a clean, modern ride.\\n2. Try the 2025 VW Golf Base \u2014 $25,990, practical and fun for daily use.\\n3. Return the vehicle and receive a full refund or trade-in value \u2014 no commitment required.\\n\\nWe\u2019re here to help you choose the best path \u2014 no pressure, just clear options. Reply to this email or call (902) 225-9368 to schedule a no-pressure chat and we\u2019ll walk you through everything.\\n\\nWarm regards,\\nWilson Xing | Sales Consultant\"\n}"}}], "created": 1781368559, "model": "Qwen3VL-4B-Instruct-Q4_K_M.gguf", "system_fingerprint": "b9590-d2462f8f7", "object": "chat.completion", "usage": {"completion_tokens": 254, "prompt_tokens": 1278, "total_tokens": 1532, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 573}}, "id": "chatcmpl-eBhAAY5VBYsQzkBMxJ475zAujOF0SMIX", "timings": {"cache_n": 573, "prompt_n": 705, "prompt_ms": 2093.776, "prompt_per_token_ms": 2.9698950354609925, "prompt_per_second": 336.7122366480464, "predicted_n": 254, "predicted_ms": 6669.744, "predicted_per_token_ms": 26.25883464566929, "predicted_per_second": 38.08242115439513}}', '2026-06-13 16:35:59.547584+00');
INSERT INTO public.llm_request_logs (id, url, model, input, output, created_at) VALUES (73, 'http://host.docker.internal:8080/v1/chat/completions', 'Qwen3VL-4B-Instruct-Q4_K_M.ggu', '{"model": "Qwen3VL-4B-Instruct-Q4_K_M.ggu", "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are an AI email-writing assistant for a car dealership sales representative.\nYour task is to compose a personalised outreach email to a specific customer.\n\nYou will receive:\n1. Email purpose (the reason for reaching out)\n2. Customer profile (name, note, vehicles they own/lease)\n3. Matching inventory vehicles that may be relevant to this customer\n4. The sales representative''s writing style guide (in Markdown)\n5. Customer''s full contact log (channel, date, summary of each prior interaction)\n\nRules:\n- Match the representative''s voice and style exactly as described in the style guide\n- Treat any \"Extra hard rules\" as mandatory requirements that override default phrasing\n- If the style guide includes a concrete format template, headings, or option-label pattern, follow it exactly\n- Make the email feel personal and relevant to this specific customer''s situation\n- Use the contact log to avoid repeating topics already covered, acknowledge the relationship naturally, and pick up where the last conversation left off\n- Reference their vehicle(s) naturally (e.g., lease end dates, age, type)\n- Mention 1-2 inventory options at most; do not list every car\n- Follow the word count and paragraph count specified in the style guide; if unspecified, target 180\u2013260 words\n- Always include a warm closing paragraph thanking the customer, a soft CTA (reply or call), and a professional sign-off with name and title\n- For lease/finance ending emails, prioritize a lease-end guidance format (upgrade vs buyout vs return) over inventory sales copy\n- Do NOT turn lease-end emails into price-led inventory advertisements unless explicitly requested by the user template/rules\n- Do NOT include a subject line in the body\n- Respond ONLY with a JSON object in the exact format:\n  {\"subject\": \"...\", \"body\": \"...\"}"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Email purpose: The customer''s lease or financing is ending soon. Write an email about upgrade options and next steps.\n\nCustomer: Brianna C Algee\n\nCustomer phone: (902) 225-9368\n\nNote: (none)\n\nCustomer vehicles:\n  \u2022 2022 VOLKSWAGEN TIGUAN (lease) lease ends 2026-09-16\n\nRelevant inventory:\n  \u2022 2025 Volkswagen Jetta S $21,990\n  \u2022 2025 Volkswagen Golf Base $25,990\n\nContact history (newest first):\n  (no prior contact logged)\n\nStyle guide:\nPrimary section to follow for this email type:\n## Lease Expiration\n\n### Subject Line\n- **Length**: 4\u20139 words (e.g., \u201cYour Lease Ends July 31\u201d or \u201cLast Chance to Upgrade\u201d)\n- **Tone**: Friendly, urgent but not alarming; uses \u201creminder\u201d or \u201cfinal opportunity\u201d cues\n- **Personalisation**: Always includes customer name + vehicle model/year (e.g., \u201cAndy, your 2022 VW Tiguan\u201d)\n- **Openers**: \u201cCan you believe how quickly time flies?\u201d \u2192 soft hook + relatability\n- **Capitalisation**: Title case only; no emojis or special characters\n- **Numbers/Emojis**: Uses dates clearly; avoids emojis unless minimal context (e.g., \u201cJuly 31, 2026\u201d)\n- **Pattern**: Always starts with vehicle reference, then transitions to options\n\n### Format\n- **Length**: 6\u20138 paragraphs; concise but detailed\n- **Opening**: Greeting + soft hook + direct vehicle/lease reference\n- **Body structure**: Hook \u2192 offer summary \u2192 numbered options \u2192 CTA \u2192 gratitude\n- **Closing**: Signature line with \u201cWarm regards\u201d + full name/title\n- **Spacing**: Single paragraph spacing; no bullet points or lists beyond numbered options\n- **CTA**: Always ends with \u201creply to this email or call\u2026\u201d with phone number\n\n### Style\n- **Tone**: Warm, professional, slightly conversational \u2014 \u201cwe want to make sure\u2026\u201d \u201cyou\u2019re in good hands\u201d\n- **Energy level**: Calm urgency \u2014 not pushy, but proactive\n- **Vocabulary**: \u201cseamless transition,\u201d \u201cnavigate the next steps,\u201d \u201cno-pressure chat\u201d\n- **Vehicle reference**: Always uses exact model/year/trim (e.g., \u201c2022 VW Tiguan\u201d) \u2014 never vague\n- **Signature**: Always ends with \u201cWarm regards, Wilson Xing | Sales Consultant\u201d\n- **Emojis/Punctuation**: None used \u2014 clean, professional format\n\n### Operational Rules\n\n- **Goal**: Remind customer of lease expiration and offer clear, low-pressure next steps (upgrade, purchase, return)\n- **Personalization fields**: [FirstName], [Year Model], [Phone], [Date of Lease Maturity]\n- **CTA standard**: \u201cReply to this email or call [Phone] to schedule a time\u201d\n- **Language guardrails**:\n  - Never say \u201cyou must\u201d or \u201cyou\u2019ll regret\u201d\n  - Avoid fabricated offers \u2014 use \u201clisted in your contract\u201d or \u201cresidual value\u201d\n  - No \u201cguaranteed\u201d or \u201cbest deal\u201d \u2014 keep it realistic\n- **4\u20136 item quality checklist**:\n  1. Is the lease expiration date clearly stated?\n  2. Are the three options numbered and clearly described?\n  3. Is the CTA actionable and include phone number?\n  4. Does the message include a warm, non-pushy closing?\n  5. Is [FirstName] and [Year Model] included?\n  6. Does the tone match \u201cwe\u2019re here to help, not sell\u201d?\n\n---\n\nAlso stay consistent with the rest of the style guide.\n\nRequired format checklist:\n  \u2022 Use a greeting line with the customer''s first name.\n  \u2022 Keep clean paragraph spacing.\n  \u2022 Include a soft CTA paragraph before the sign-off.\n  \u2022 Reference the lease/finance end date in the opening.\n\nExtra hard rules (non-negotiable):\n  \u2022 make this is fix email ending\nBest regards,\nWilson Xing | Sales Consultant"}]}', '{"choices": [{"finish_reason": "stop", "index": 0, "message": {"role": "assistant", "content": "{\n  \"subject\": \"Brianna, Your 2022 VW Tiguan Lease Ends Sept 16\",\n  \"body\": \"Hi Brianna,\\n\\nCan you believe how quickly time flies? Your 2022 VW Tiguan lease ends on September 16, 2026 \u2014 and we\u2019re here to help you navigate the next steps with zero pressure.\\n\\nWe\u2019ve got a few options to consider:\\n\\n1. Upgrade to a 2025 Volkswagen Jetta S \u2014 $21,990 \u2014 a great way to keep your driving experience fresh and efficient.\\n2. Try a 2025 Volkswagen Golf Base \u2014 $25,990 \u2014 perfect for those who want more room and a sporty feel.\\n\\nEither option is listed in our contract-ready inventory and can be arranged through a no-pressure chat or test drive.\\n\\nReply to this email or call (902) 225-9368 to schedule a time we can walk through what works best for you.\\n\\nWe\u2019re here to make sure your transition is seamless \u2014 no matter which path you choose.\\n\\nWarm regards,\\nWilson Xing | Sales Consultant\"\n}"}}], "created": 1781368604, "model": "Qwen3VL-4B-Instruct-Q4_K_M.gguf", "system_fingerprint": "b9590-d2462f8f7", "object": "chat.completion", "usage": {"completion_tokens": 261, "prompt_tokens": 1278, "total_tokens": 1539, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 1277}}, "id": "chatcmpl-xf1XCCaQIYQUp1mOCabaqp2lfeP4h1FH", "timings": {"cache_n": 1277, "prompt_n": 1, "prompt_ms": 85.131, "prompt_per_token_ms": 85.131, "prompt_per_second": 11.746602295286088, "predicted_n": 261, "predicted_ms": 7182.13, "predicted_per_token_ms": 27.517739463601533, "predicted_per_second": 36.34019434346078}}', '2026-06-13 16:36:44.724949+00');
INSERT INTO public.llm_request_logs (id, url, model, input, output, created_at) VALUES (74, 'http://host.docker.internal:8080/v1/chat/completions', 'Qwen3VL-4B-Instruct-Q4_K_M.ggu', '{"model": "Qwen3VL-4B-Instruct-Q4_K_M.ggu", "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a writing style analyst for a car dealership sales team.\nYour task is to study the provided sample messages and distill the writer''s unique communication style\ninto a concise, actionable markdown guide. Another AI will use this guide to write new messages\nthat faithfully match this person''s voice and style.\n\nThe writer''s samples are organized into the following categories:\n- Lease Expiration\n- Test Drive Follow-Up\n\nProduce one ## section for each category that has samples provided, using the exact category name as the ## heading.\nIf any sample does not match a named category, place it under ## General.\nDo NOT produce sections for categories that have no samples.\n\nEach category section MUST contain exactly three sub-sections:\n\n### Subject Line\nDescribe the subject line patterns observed across the samples:\n- Typical length (capture what works in practice; for email this is often around 4-9 words)\n- Tone and urgency (e.g. friendly teaser, direct offer, question)\n- Use of personalisation (customer name, vehicle details)\n- Common openers or formulas (e.g. \"Your [Year] [Model] is ready\", \"Quick update on\u2026\")\n- Capitalisation style (title case, sentence case, all-lower)\n- Use of numbers, emojis, or special characters\n- Anything that makes the subject line pattern recognisable\n\n### Format\nDescribe the structural/layout conventions observed in the samples:\n- Message length (give realistic ranges; avoid strict limits unless samples consistently enforce them)\n- Opening line pattern (greeting style, whether name is used)\n- Body structure (e.g. one hook sentence \u2192 offer \u2192 CTA)\n- Closing line pattern (sign-off, signature style)\n- Paragraph count and spacing habits\n- Use of bullet points, line breaks, or lists\n\n### Style\nDescribe the voice and language patterns:\n- Tone and formality level for this situation\n- Energy level (urgent, warm, casual, professional)\n- Vocabulary preferences and any signature phrases or pet words\n- How they reference vehicles (make/model/year/trim usage)\n- Use of emojis, punctuation quirks, or capitalisation habits\n- Anything that makes this person''s writing instantly recognisable\n- If the closing/signature phrase is consistent, capture the exact required wording verbatim in quotes\n\nAfter those required sub-sections, add a short \"### Operational Rules\" section for each category with:\n- Goal (what the email is trying to achieve for this category)\n- Personalization fields to include (e.g. [FirstName], [Year Model], relevant date, [Phone])\n- CTA standard (one primary action at the end)\n- Language guardrails (non-pushy phrasing, no overpromising, no fabricated offers)\n- A 4-6 item quality checklist for before-send review\n- For lease/finance ending categories, if samples use a named options block, explicitly define the required heading and option-label format (e.g., \"Option 1/2/3\")\n\nPrefer specific, reusable rules over abstract advice.\nOutput a clean markdown document. Do NOT include any samples verbatim."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Channel: email\n\n### Lease Expiration\n\nHi Andy\nI hope this email finds you well.\nCan you believe how quickly time flies? We want to remind you that the lease on your 2022 VW Tiguan is scheduled to mature on July 31, 2026.\nAs you approach the end of your lease, you have a few great options available to you, and we want to make sure the transition is as smooth and seamless as possible. Whether you want to upgrade, keep your current ride, or simply hand over the keys, we are here to help you navigate the next steps.\nYour End-of-Lease Options:\nOption 1: Upgrade to a new model. Get behind the wheel of a brand-new vehicle with the latest technology, safety features, and a fresh warranty.\nOption 2: Purchase your current vehicle. If you\u2019ve fallen in love with your car and aren''t ready to part ways, you can buy it out for the residual value listed in your contract.\nOption 3: Return the vehicle. Simply schedule an inspection and return the keys to us at the end of your term.\nLet''s Find the Best Path Forward\nWe would love to invite you back into the dealership for a quick, no-pressure chat to review these options, check out current inventory, and see what specials might apply to you.\nPlease reply directly to this email or call us at 9024076395 to schedule a convenient time for you to drop by.\nThank you so much for being a valued part of the O''Regan''s VW family. We look forward to assisting you with your next automotive chapter!\nWarm regards,\nWilson Xing | Sales Consultant\n\n### Test Drive Follow-Up\n\nHi Andy,\nThank you for taking the time to visit us yesterday and test driving the 2026 Jetta Comfortline. It was a pleasure meeting you and showing you what the Jetta has to offer.\nI completely understand and respect your decision to test drive a few other options in the market before making your final move. Investing in a new vehicle is a big decision, and you want to ensure it\u2019s the perfect fit.\nWhile you are doing your research, I did want to give you a quick heads-up on an incentive that just came up for this month. Volkswagen is currently offering a 0.99% special finance rate for up to 60 months (5 years) on the 2026 Jetta. It\u2019s one of the strongest programs we''ve seen in a while, and it definitely keeps the monthly payments incredibly comfortable on that Comfortline trim.\nIf you have any questions about how those numbers look for your budget while you compare your options, just let me know.\nI would love the opportunity to earn your business. Drive safe during your other test drives, and I look forward to connecting with you soon!\nBest regards,\nWilson Xing | Sales Consultant"}]}', '{"choices": [{"finish_reason": "stop", "index": 0, "message": {"role": "assistant", "content": "## Lease Expiration\n\n### Subject Line\n- **Length**: Typically 4\u20139 words; concise and punchy.\n- **Tone**: Friendly, slightly urgent, but non-pushy \u2014 uses \u201cremind you\u201d and \u201cwe want to make sure\u201d to soften urgency.\n- **Personalisation**: Always includes customer name + vehicle make/model/year (e.g., \u201cyour 2022 VW Tiguan\u201d).\n- **Openers**: Often starts with \u201cCan you believe how quickly time flies?\u201d \u2014 conversational, relatable hook.\n- **Capitalisation**: Title case, but not overly formal \u2014 e.g., \u201cYour End-of-Lease Options:\u201d is clear and clean.\n- **Emojis/Numbers**: Rarely used; numbers are used for dates (e.g., \u201cJuly 31, 2026\u201d) or options (Option 1/2/3).\n- **Pattern**: Strongly recognizable: \u201cYour [Year] [Model] is ready\u201d or \u201cWe want to remind you\u2026\u201d + clear deadline.\n\n### Format\n- **Length**: 3\u20135 paragraphs, no more than 100 words per paragraph.\n- **Opening**: Friendly, personal greeting + quick hook sentence.\n- **Body Structure**: Hook \u2192 reminder \u2192 options list \u2192 next steps \u2192 closing with gratitude.\n- **Closing Line**: Ends with warm thank-you + sign-off. Signature always includes \u201cWilson Xing | Sales Consultant.\u201d\n- **Spacing**: Clean, no bullet points unless necessary \u2014 uses clear headings like \u201cYour End-of-Lease Options:\u201d.\n- **Paragraphs**: Short, scannable. Avoids long sentences. Uses clear transitions like \u201cWhether you want\u2026\u201d or \u201cLet\u2019s Find the Best Path Forward.\u201d\n\n### Style\n- **Tone**: Warm, professional, reassuring. Avoids salesy language \u2014 focuses on \u201chelping you navigate\u201d and \u201csmooth transition.\u201d\n- **Energy Level**: Balanced \u2014 friendly but not casual, professional but not stiff.\n- **Vocabulary**: Uses \u201cresidual value,\u201d \u201cwarranty,\u201d \u201cinspection,\u201d \u201cno-pressure chat\u201d \u2014 familiar automotive terms without jargon.\n- **Vehicle Reference**: Always specifies model, year, trim (e.g., \u201c2022 VW Tiguan\u201d or \u201cComfortline trim\u201d).\n- **Emojis/Punctuation**: None. Uses dashes and colons for structure. No exclamation marks unless for emphasis (\u201cIt was a pleasure\u2026\u201d).\n- **Signature**: Always ends with \u201cWarm regards, Wilson Xing | Sales Consultant.\u201d\n\n### Operational Rules\n\n- **Goal**: Remind customer of lease expiration and offer clear, low-pressure next steps without pressure.\n- **Personalization Fields**: [FirstName], [Year Model], [Lease End Date], [Phone]\n- **CTA Standard**: \u201cReply directly to this email or call us at [Phone] to schedule a convenient time\u2026\u201d\n- **Language Guardrails**:\n  - Avoid \u201cyou must\u201d or \u201cdon\u2019t miss\u201d \u2014 use \u201cwe want to make sure\u2026\u201d or \u201cwe\u2019d love to invite you\u2026\u201d\n  - No fabricated offers \u2014 e.g., \u201cstrongest program we\u2019ve seen\u201d is truthful, not exaggerated.\n  - No overpromising \u2014 \u201cspecials might apply\u201d not \u201cguaranteed\u201d.\n- **Quality Checklist**:\n  1. Is the lease end date clearly stated?\n  2. Are all three options listed with clear titles (Option 1/2/3)?\n  3. Is the CTA specific and actionable?\n  4. Is the tone warm and non-salesy?\n  5. Is the signature consistent and professional?\n  6. Is the email free of grammatical errors or awkward phrasing?\n\n- **Option Block Format**:\n  - **Heading**: \u201cYour End-of-Lease Options:\u201d\n  - **Option Labels**: \u201cOption 1: Upgrade\u2026\u201d, \u201cOption 2: Purchase\u2026\u201d, \u201cOption 3: Return\u2026\u201d\n\n---\n\n## Test Drive Follow-Up\n\n### Subject Line\n- **Length**: 4\u20138 words; typically casual or conversational.\n- **Tone**: Warm, appreciative, slightly teasing \u2014 \u201cI completely understand\u2026\u201d shows empathy.\n- **Personalisation**: Always includes customer name + vehicle details (e.g., \u201c2026 Jetta Comfortline\u201d).\n- **Openers**: Starts with \u201cHi Andy,\u201d and includes \u201cThank you for taking the time\u2026\u201d \u2014 standard, respectful opener.\n- **Capitalisation**: Title case for headings, sentence case for body.\n- **Emojis/Numbers**: Rarely used \u2014 numbers used for finance terms (\u201c0.99%\u201d, \u201c60 months\u201d).\n- **Pattern**: \u201cI want to give you a quick heads-up on\u2026\u201d \u2192 \u201cIt\u2019s one of the strongest programs\u2026\u201d \u2192 \u201cIf you have any questions\u2026\u201d\n\n### Format\n- **Length**: 3\u20134 paragraphs, with minimal whitespace.\n- **Opening**: Personal greeting + thank you + brief context (\u201cI completely understand\u2026\u201d).\n- **Body Structure**: Acknowledgement \u2192 reassurance \u2192 incentive update \u2192 open-ended CTA.\n- **Closing Line**: Ends with \u201cI look forward to connecting with you soon!\u201d \u2014 forward-looking, low-pressure.\n- **Paragraphs**: Short, scannable. No bullet points \u2014 uses plain text and line breaks for readability.\n- **Spacing**: Clean, professional, no extra padding \u2014 lines are tight but readable.\n\n### Style\n- **Tone**: Warm, conversational, empathetic. Avoids \u201csalesy\u201d or \u201cpushy\u201d phrases \u2014 \u201cI understand you\u2019re comparing options\u201d feels human.\n- **Energy Level**: Low to medium \u2014 encourages trust, not urgency.\n- **Vocabulary**: Uses \u201cheads-up,\u201d \u201cinvesting in a new vehicle is a big decision,\u201d \u201ccomfortable on that trim\u201d \u2014 relatable, not jargon-heavy.\n- **Vehicle Reference**: Specific trim + year model (e.g., \u201c2026 Jetta Comfortline\u201d) \u2014 clear and accurate.\n- **Emojis/Punctuation**: None \u2014 uses dashes and colons for structure. Ends with friendly closing.\n- **Signature**: Always \u201cBest regards, Wilson Xing | Sales Consultant.\u201d\n\n### Operational Rules\n\n- **Goal**: Re-engage customer after test drive, provide valuable incentive info without pressure, and keep the door open for future contact.\n- **Personalization Fields**: [FirstName], [Year Model], [Phone]\n- **CTA Standard**: \u201cJust let me know\u2026\u201d, \u201cI\u2019d love the opportunity\u2026\u201d, \u201cI look forward to connecting\u2026\u201d, \u201cDrive safe\u2026\u201d \u2014 open-ended, non-demanding.\n- **Language Guardrails**:\n  - Avoid \u201cyou should\u201d or \u201cyou\u2019ll regret\u201d \u2014 use \u201cI completely understand\u2026\u201d\n  - No overpromising \u2014 \u201cone of the strongest programs we\u2019ve seen\u201d is truthful, not inflated.\n  - No \u201cguaranteed\u201d \u2014 avoid implying certainty.\n- **Quality Checklist**:\n  1. Is the vehicle model and trim clearly stated?\n  2. Is the incentive info accurate and relevant?\n  3. Is the tone warm, not salesy?\n  4. Is the CTA soft and inviting?\n  5. Is the signature consistent?\n  6. Does the message reflect appreciation for the customer\u2019s effort?\n\n- **No Named Option Blocks**: No numbered options in this category \u2014 just a single, clear incentive message."}}], "created": 1781368820, "model": "Qwen3VL-4B-Instruct-Q4_K_M.gguf", "system_fingerprint": "b9590-d2462f8f7", "object": "chat.completion", "usage": {"completion_tokens": 1536, "prompt_tokens": 1236, "total_tokens": 2772, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 1235}}, "id": "chatcmpl-y8VEvAM5A7BcN58LVLZM0hA8JgXMlM8t", "timings": {"cache_n": 1235, "prompt_n": 1, "prompt_ms": 85.472, "prompt_per_token_ms": 85.472, "prompt_per_second": 11.699737925870462, "predicted_n": 1536, "predicted_ms": 39178.245, "predicted_per_token_ms": 25.506669921875, "predicted_per_second": 39.20543148372266}}', '2026-06-13 16:40:20.440347+00');
INSERT INTO public.llm_request_logs (id, url, model, input, output, created_at) VALUES (75, 'http://host.docker.internal:8080/v1/chat/completions', 'Qwen3VL-4B-Instruct-Q4_K_M.ggu', '{"model": "Qwen3VL-4B-Instruct-Q4_K_M.ggu", "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are an AI email-writing assistant for a car dealership sales representative.\nYour task is to compose a personalised outreach email to a specific customer.\n\nYou will receive:\n1. Email purpose (the reason for reaching out)\n2. Customer profile (name, note, vehicles they own/lease)\n3. Matching inventory vehicles that may be relevant to this customer\n4. The sales representative''s writing style guide (in Markdown)\n5. Customer''s full contact log (channel, date, summary of each prior interaction)\n\nRules:\n- Match the representative''s voice and style exactly as described in the style guide\n- Treat any \"Extra hard rules\" as mandatory requirements that override default phrasing\n- If the style guide includes a concrete format template, headings, or option-label pattern, follow it exactly\n- Make the email feel personal and relevant to this specific customer''s situation\n- Use the contact log to avoid repeating topics already covered, acknowledge the relationship naturally, and pick up where the last conversation left off\n- Reference their vehicle(s) naturally (e.g., lease end dates, age, type)\n- Mention 1-2 inventory options at most; do not list every car\n- Follow the word count and paragraph count specified in the style guide; if unspecified, target 180\u2013260 words\n- Always include a warm closing paragraph thanking the customer, a soft CTA (reply or call), and a professional sign-off with name and title\n- For lease/finance ending emails, prioritize a lease-end guidance format (upgrade vs buyout vs return) over inventory sales copy\n- Do NOT turn lease-end emails into price-led inventory advertisements unless explicitly requested by the user template/rules\n- Do NOT include a subject line in the body\n- Respond ONLY with a JSON object in the exact format:\n  {\"subject\": \"...\", \"body\": \"...\"}"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Email purpose: The customer''s lease or financing is ending soon. Write an email about upgrade options and next steps.\n\nCustomer: Brianna C Algee\n\nCustomer phone: (902) 225-9368\n\nNote: (none)\n\nCustomer vehicles:\n  \u2022 2022 VOLKSWAGEN TIGUAN (lease) lease ends 2026-09-16\n\nRelevant inventory:\n  (none)\n\nContact history (newest first):\n  (no prior contact logged)\n\nStyle guide:\nPrimary section to follow for this email type:\n## Lease Expiration\n\n### Subject Line\n- **Length**: Typically 4\u20139 words; concise and punchy.\n- **Tone**: Friendly, slightly urgent, but non-pushy \u2014 uses \u201cremind you\u201d and \u201cwe want to make sure\u201d to soften urgency.\n- **Personalisation**: Always includes customer name + vehicle make/model/year (e.g., \u201cyour 2022 VW Tiguan\u201d).\n- **Openers**: Often starts with \u201cCan you believe how quickly time flies?\u201d \u2014 conversational, relatable hook.\n- **Capitalisation**: Title case, but not overly formal \u2014 e.g., \u201cYour End-of-Lease Options:\u201d is clear and clean.\n- **Emojis/Numbers**: Rarely used; numbers are used for dates (e.g., \u201cJuly 31, 2026\u201d) or options (Option 1/2/3).\n- **Pattern**: Strongly recognizable: \u201cYour [Year] [Model] is ready\u201d or \u201cWe want to remind you\u2026\u201d + clear deadline.\n\n### Format\n- **Length**: 3\u20135 paragraphs, no more than 100 words per paragraph.\n- **Opening**: Friendly, personal greeting + quick hook sentence.\n- **Body Structure**: Hook \u2192 reminder \u2192 options list \u2192 next steps \u2192 closing with gratitude.\n- **Closing Line**: Ends with warm thank-you + sign-off. Signature always includes \u201cWilson Xing | Sales Consultant.\u201d\n- **Spacing**: Clean, no bullet points unless necessary \u2014 uses clear headings like \u201cYour End-of-Lease Options:\u201d.\n- **Paragraphs**: Short, scannable. Avoids long sentences. Uses clear transitions like \u201cWhether you want\u2026\u201d or \u201cLet\u2019s Find the Best Path Forward.\u201d\n\n### Style\n- **Tone**: Warm, professional, reassuring. Avoids salesy language \u2014 focuses on \u201chelping you navigate\u201d and \u201csmooth transition.\u201d\n- **Energy Level**: Balanced \u2014 friendly but not casual, professional but not stiff.\n- **Vocabulary**: Uses \u201cresidual value,\u201d \u201cwarranty,\u201d \u201cinspection,\u201d \u201cno-pressure chat\u201d \u2014 familiar automotive terms without jargon.\n- **Vehicle Reference**: Always specifies model, year, trim (e.g., \u201c2022 VW Tiguan\u201d or \u201cComfortline trim\u201d).\n- **Emojis/Punctuation**: None. Uses dashes and colons for structure. No exclamation marks unless for emphasis (\u201cIt was a pleasure\u2026\u201d).\n- **Signature**: Always ends with \u201cWarm regards, Wilson Xing | Sales Consultant.\u201d\n\n### Operational Rules\n\n- **Goal**: Remind customer of lease expiration and offer clear, low-pressure next steps without pressure.\n- **Personalization Fields**: [FirstName], [Year Model], [Lease End Date], [Phone]\n- **CTA Standard**: \u201cReply directly to this email or call us at [Phone] to schedule a convenient time\u2026\u201d\n- **Language Guardrails**:\n  - Avoid \u201cyou must\u201d or \u201cdon\u2019t miss\u201d \u2014 use \u201cwe want to make sure\u2026\u201d or \u201cwe\u2019d love to invite you\u2026\u201d\n  - No fabricated offers \u2014 e.g., \u201cstrongest program we\u2019ve seen\u201d is truthful, not exaggerated.\n  - No overpromising \u2014 \u201cspecials might apply\u201d not \u201cguaranteed\u201d.\n- **Quality Checklist**:\n  1. Is the lease end date clearly stated?\n  2. Are all three options listed with clear titles (Option 1/2/3)?\n  3. Is the CTA specific and actionable?\n  4. Is the tone warm and non-salesy?\n  5. Is the signature consistent and professional?\n  6. Is the email free of grammatical errors or awkward phrasing?\n\n- **Option Block Format**:\n  - **Heading**: \u201cYour End-of-Lease Options:\u201d\n  - **Option Labels**: \u201cOption 1: Upgrade\u2026\u201d, \u201cOption 2: Purchase\u2026\u201d, \u201cOption 3: Return\u2026\u201d\n\n---\n\nAlso stay consistent with the rest of the style guide.\n\nRequired format checklist:\n  \u2022 Use a greeting line with the customer''s first name.\n  \u2022 Keep clean paragraph spacing.\n  \u2022 Include a soft CTA paragraph before the sign-off.\n  \u2022 Reference the lease/finance end date in the opening.\n  \u2022 Use the heading \"Your End-of-Lease Options:\".\n  \u2022 Format choices as Option 1 / Option 2 / Option 3 (not generic numbered bullets).\n  \u2022 Include all 3 options explicitly: upgrade, purchase current vehicle, return vehicle.\n  \u2022 Do not include dollar prices, stock-style vehicle listings, or inventory bullet pitches.\n\nExtra hard rules (non-negotiable):\n  \u2022 make this is fix email ending\nBest regards,\nWilson Xing | Sales Consultant"}]}', '{"choices": [{"finish_reason": "stop", "index": 0, "message": {"role": "assistant", "content": "{\n  \"subject\": \"Your 2022 VW Tiguan is Ready\",\n  \"body\": \"Hi Brianna,\\n\\nCan you believe how quickly time flies? Your 2022 VW Tiguan lease ends September 16, 2026 \u2014 and we want to make sure you\u2019re prepared for what comes next.\\n\\nWe\u2019re here to help you navigate your options without any pressure. Whether you\u2019re ready to upgrade, purchase, or simply return the vehicle, we\u2019ve got a clear path forward.\\n\\nYour End-of-Lease Options:\\n\\nOption 1: Upgrade \u2014 Take advantage of our current program to upgrade to a new Tiguan or another model with a smooth transition and full warranty.\\n\\nOption 2: Purchase \u2014 Keep your current vehicle with a low-mileage, factory-certified vehicle and enjoy full ownership and residual value.\\n\\nOption 3: Return \u2014 Return your vehicle with no obligation. We\u2019ll handle all paperwork and ensure a seamless end to your lease.\\n\\nWe\u2019d love to invite you to a no-pressure chat at your convenience. Just reply directly to this email or call us at (902) 225-9368.\\n\\nThank you for choosing us \u2014 it\u2019s been a pleasure serving you.\\n\\nWarm regards,\\nWilson Xing | Sales Consultant\"\n}"}}], "created": 1781368849, "model": "Qwen3VL-4B-Instruct-Q4_K_M.gguf", "system_fingerprint": "b9590-d2462f8f7", "object": "chat.completion", "usage": {"completion_tokens": 284, "prompt_tokens": 1493, "total_tokens": 1777, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 480}}, "id": "chatcmpl-nX75OnKDLvL1EagTro2S76DOGlnqeYDm", "timings": {"cache_n": 480, "prompt_n": 1013, "prompt_ms": 2915.774, "prompt_per_token_ms": 2.87835538005923, "prompt_per_second": 347.42061627547264, "predicted_n": 284, "predicted_ms": 7455.43, "predicted_per_token_ms": 26.251514084507043, "predicted_per_second": 38.09304091112116}}', '2026-06-13 16:40:49.492391+00');
INSERT INTO public.llm_request_logs (id, url, model, input, output, created_at) VALUES (76, 'http://host.docker.internal:8080/v1/chat/completions', 'Qwen3VL-4B-Instruct-Q4_K_M.ggu', '{"model": "Qwen3VL-4B-Instruct-Q4_K_M.ggu", "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a writing style analyst for a car dealership sales team.\nYour task is to study the provided sample messages and distill the writer''s unique communication style\ninto a concise, actionable markdown guide. Another AI will use this guide to write new messages\nthat faithfully match this person''s voice and style.\n\nThe writer''s samples are organized into the following categories:\n- Lease Expiration\n- Test Drive Follow-Up\n\nProduce one ## section for each category that has samples provided, using the exact category name as the ## heading.\nIf any sample does not match a named category, place it under ## General.\nDo NOT produce sections for categories that have no samples.\n\nEach category section MUST contain exactly three sub-sections:\n\n### Subject Line\nDescribe the subject line patterns observed across the samples:\n- Typical length (capture what works in practice; for email this is often around 4-9 words)\n- Tone and urgency (e.g. friendly teaser, direct offer, question)\n- Use of personalisation (customer name, vehicle details)\n- Common openers or formulas (e.g. \"Your [Year] [Model] is ready\", \"Quick update on\u2026\")\n- Capitalisation style (title case, sentence case, all-lower)\n- Use of numbers, emojis, or special characters\n- Anything that makes the subject line pattern recognisable\n\n### Format\nDescribe the structural/layout conventions observed in the samples:\n- Message length (give realistic ranges; avoid strict limits unless samples consistently enforce them)\n- Opening line pattern (greeting style, whether name is used)\n- Body structure (e.g. one hook sentence \u2192 offer \u2192 CTA)\n- Closing line pattern (sign-off, signature style)\n- Paragraph count and spacing habits\n- Use of bullet points, line breaks, or lists\n\n### Style\nDescribe the voice and language patterns:\n- Tone and formality level for this situation\n- Energy level (urgent, warm, casual, professional)\n- Vocabulary preferences and any signature phrases or pet words\n- How they reference vehicles (make/model/year/trim usage)\n- Use of emojis, punctuation quirks, or capitalisation habits\n- Anything that makes this person''s writing instantly recognisable\n- If the closing/signature phrase is consistent, capture the exact required wording verbatim in quotes\n\nAfter those required sub-sections, add a short \"### Operational Rules\" section for each category with:\n- Goal (what the email is trying to achieve for this category)\n- Personalization fields to include (e.g. [FirstName], [Year Model], relevant date, [Phone])\n- CTA standard (one primary action at the end)\n- Language guardrails (non-pushy phrasing, no overpromising, no fabricated offers)\n- A 4-6 item quality checklist for before-send review\n- For lease/finance ending categories, if samples use a named options block, explicitly define the required heading and option-label format (e.g., \"Option 1/2/3\")\n\nPrefer specific, reusable rules over abstract advice.\nOutput a clean markdown document. Do NOT include any samples verbatim."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Channel: email\n\n### Lease Expiration\n\nHi Andy\nI hope this email finds you well.\nCan you believe how quickly time flies? We want to remind you that the lease on your 2022 VW Tiguan is scheduled to mature on July 31, 2026.\nAs you approach the end of your lease, you have a few great options available to you, and we want to make sure the transition is as smooth and seamless as possible. Whether you want to upgrade, keep your current ride, or simply hand over the keys, we are here to help you navigate the next steps.\nYour End-of-Lease Options:\nOption 1: Upgrade to a new model. Get behind the wheel of a brand-new vehicle with the latest technology, safety features, and a fresh warranty.\nOption 2: Purchase your current vehicle. If you\u2019ve fallen in love with your car and aren''t ready to part ways, you can buy it out for the residual value listed in your contract.\nOption 3: Return the vehicle. Simply schedule an inspection and return the keys to us at the end of your term.\nLet''s Find the Best Path Forward\nWe would love to invite you back into the dealership for a quick, no-pressure chat to review these options, check out current inventory, and see what specials might apply to you.\nPlease reply directly to this email or call us at 9024076395 to schedule a convenient time for you to drop by.\nThank you so much for being a valued part of the O''Regan''s VW family. We look forward to assisting you with your next automotive chapter!\nWarm regards,\nWilson Xing | Sales Consultant\n\n### Test Drive Follow-Up\n\nHi Andy,\nThank you for taking the time to visit us yesterday and test driving the 2026 Jetta Comfortline. It was a pleasure meeting you and showing you what the Jetta has to offer.\nI completely understand and respect your decision to test drive a few other options in the market before making your final move. Investing in a new vehicle is a big decision, and you want to ensure it\u2019s the perfect fit.\nWhile you are doing your research, I did want to give you a quick heads-up on an incentive that just came up for this month. Volkswagen is currently offering a 0.99% special finance rate for up to 60 months (5 years) on the 2026 Jetta. It\u2019s one of the strongest programs we''ve seen in a while, and it definitely keeps the monthly payments incredibly comfortable on that Comfortline trim.\nIf you have any questions about how those numbers look for your budget while you compare your options, just let me know.\nI would love the opportunity to earn your business. Drive safe during your other test drives, and I look forward to connecting with you soon!\nBest regards,\nWilson Xing | Sales Consultant"}]}', '{"choices": [{"finish_reason": "stop", "index": 0, "message": {"role": "assistant", "content": "## Lease Expiration\n\n### Subject Line\n- **Typical length**: 4\u20139 words (e.g., \u201cYour Lease is Almost Up\u201d or \u201cQuick Update: 2022 VW Tiguan\u201d)\n- **Tone and urgency**: Friendly, gentle reminder with a hint of urgency \u2014 avoids alarm, focuses on \u201coptions\u201d and \u201csmooth transition\u201d\n- **Personalisation**: Uses customer name + vehicle model/year (e.g., \u201cAndy, your 2022 VW Tiguan\u201d)\n- **Common openers**: \u201cWe want to remind you that\u2026\u201d, \u201cAs you approach the end of your lease\u2026\u201d\n- **Capitalisation**: Title case (e.g., \u201cYour End-of-Lease Options:\u201d)\n- **Use of numbers**: \u201cJuly 31, 2026\u201d \u2014 dates are explicit and formatted clearly\n- **Emojis/characters**: None \u2014 clean, professional, no frivolous symbols\n\n### Format\n- **Message length**: 3\u20135 paragraphs, concise but warm\n- **Opening line pattern**: Friendly, non-pushy greeting + light reflection (\u201cCan you believe how quickly time flies?\u201d)\n- **Body structure**: Hook \u2192 reminder \u2192 list of options \u2192 invitation to chat \u2192 CTA \u2192 closing\n- **Closing line pattern**: \u201cWarm regards, Wilson Xing | Sales Consultant\u201d \u2014 consistent, warm, no pressure\n- **Paragraph count**: 3\u20134 paragraphs, with clear spacing and line breaks\n- **Lists**: Uses numbered options (Option 1/2/3) with clear, benefit-focused descriptions\n\n### Style\n- **Tone and formality**: Warm, professional, slightly conversational \u2014 feels like a trusted advisor, not a salesperson\n- **Energy level**: Calm, reassuring, non-pushy \u2014 avoids \u201churry up\u201d or \u201cdon\u2019t miss out\u201d language\n- **Vocabulary**: Focus on \u201coptions,\u201d \u201cseamless,\u201d \u201cnavigate,\u201d \u201ctransition,\u201d \u201cvalued part of the family\u201d \u2014 builds emotional connection\n- **Vehicle references**: Uses exact model/year/trim (e.g., \u201c2022 VW Tiguan\u201d) \u2014 never vague or generic\n- **Punctuation quirks**: Uses em dashes and colons for emphasis, avoids exclamation marks except for warmth\n- **Signature**: Always \u201cWilson Xing | Sales Consultant\u201d \u2014 verbatim\n\n### Operational Rules\n- **Goal**: Remind customer of lease expiration + offer gentle, non-pressure navigation to next steps\n- **Personalization fields**: [FirstName], [Year Model] (e.g., \u201cyour 2022 VW Tiguan\u201d), lease end date (e.g., \u201cJuly 31, 2026\u201d)\n- **CTA standard**: \u201cReply directly to this email or call us at [Phone] to schedule a visit\u201d\n- **Language guardrails**: \n  - Avoid phrases like \u201cyou MUST decide\u201d or \u201clast chance\u201d\n  - Do not fabricate deals or exaggerate incentives\n  - Use \u201cwe are here to help\u201d not \u201cwe\u2019ll make it easy for you\u201d\n- **4\u20136 item quality checklist**:\n  1. Is the lease end date clearly stated?\n  2. Are all 3 options clearly labeled and described?\n  3. Does the CTA include both reply and phone option?\n  4. Is the closing line \u201cWarm regards, Wilson Xing | Sales Consultant\u201d included?\n  5. Is the tone warm, professional, and non-pushy?\n  6. Are vehicle model/year/trim accurately referenced?\n\n- **Option block required**: \n  - **Heading**: \u201cYour End-of-Lease Options:\u201d\n  - **Option format**: \u201cOption 1: [Description]\u201d \u2014 must be numbered, benefit-focused, concise\n\n---\n\n## Test Drive Follow-Up\n\n### Subject Line\n- **Typical length**: 4\u20137 words (e.g., \u201cThanks for Testing the Jetta!\u201d or \u201cYou\u2019re Still in the Market?\u201d)\n- **Tone and urgency**: Friendly, appreciative, light encouragement \u2014 no pressure to decide\n- **Personalisation**: Uses customer name + vehicle model/year/trim (e.g., \u201cAndy, your 2026 Jetta Comfortline\u201d)\n- **Common openers**: \u201cThank you for taking the time\u2026\u201d or \u201cI completely understand\u2026\u201d\n- **Capitalisation**: Title case (e.g., \u201cYou\u2019re Still in the Market?\u201d)\n- **Use of numbers**: \u201cup to 60 months\u201d \u2014 includes time frame for clarity\n- **Emojis/characters**: None \u2014 clean, professional, no frivolous symbols\n\n### Format\n- **Message length**: 3\u20134 paragraphs, slightly more conversational than lease reminder\n- **Opening line pattern**: Warm greeting + acknowledgment of decision (\u201cI completely understand\u2026\u201d)\n- **Body structure**: Greeting \u2192 validation of customer\u2019s behavior \u2192 incentive update \u2192 invitation to ask questions \u2192 closing\n- **Closing line pattern**: \u201cBest regards, Wilson Xing | Sales Consultant\u201d \u2014 consistent, professional, no pressure\n- **Paragraph count**: 3\u20134 paragraphs, with natural spacing and line breaks\n- **Lists**: None \u2014 uses bullet-free, paragraph-style descriptions\n\n### Style\n- **Tone and formality**: Warm, conversational, professional \u2014 like a trusted friend in the car biz\n- **Energy level**: Encouraging, not pushy \u2014 validates customer\u2019s research process\n- **Vocabulary**: Focus on \u201cdecision,\u201d \u201cresearch,\u201d \u201cincentive,\u201d \u201ccomfortable,\u201d \u201cearn your business\u201d \u2014 builds trust\n- **Vehicle references**: Specific model/year/trim (e.g., \u201c2026 Jetta Comfortline\u201d) \u2014 never vague\n- **Punctuation quirks**: Uses dashes and colons for emphasis, avoids exclamation marks unless for warmth\n- **Signature**: Always \u201cBest regards, Wilson Xing | Sales Consultant\u201d \u2014 verbatim\n\n### Operational Rules\n- **Goal**: Acknowledge test drive + gently introduce new incentive + invite questions\n- **Personalization fields**: [FirstName], [Year Model], [Trim] (e.g., \u201c2026 Jetta Comfortline\u201d), date of test drive if relevant\n- **CTA standard**: \u201cIf you have any questions\u2026 just let me know.\u201d \u2014 no direct \u201cschedule a call\u201d unless explicitly requested\n- **Language guardrails**:\n  - Avoid phrases like \u201cyou should\u201d or \u201cwe\u2019re offering this because\u2026\u201d\n  - Do not say \u201cthis is the best deal\u201d \u2014 stick to \u201cone of the strongest programs we\u2019ve seen\u201d\n  - Use \u201cI would love to earn your business\u201d \u2014 not \u201cwe want to sell you\u201d\n- **4\u20136 item quality checklist**:\n  1. Is customer name + vehicle model/trim clearly referenced?\n  2. Is the incentive described clearly and without exaggeration?\n  3. Is the CTA open-ended (\u201cjust let me know\u201d) or direct (\u201cschedule a call\u201d)?\n  4. Is the closing line \u201cBest regards, Wilson Xing | Sales Consultant\u201d included?\n  5. Does the message acknowledge the customer\u2019s research process?\n  6. Is tone warm, not pushy, and focused on collaboration?\n\n- **No option block required** \u2014 message is single-topic, no numbered choices needed\n\n---"}}], "created": 1781369018, "model": "Qwen3VL-4B-Instruct-Q4_K_M.gguf", "system_fingerprint": "b9590-d2462f8f7", "object": "chat.completion", "usage": {"completion_tokens": 1530, "prompt_tokens": 1236, "total_tokens": 2766, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 1235}}, "id": "chatcmpl-IzJymrAKPdEu860VkIZqc5Wr4nuavNeR", "timings": {"cache_n": 1235, "prompt_n": 1, "prompt_ms": 80.44, "prompt_per_token_ms": 80.44, "prompt_per_second": 12.431626056688215, "predicted_n": 1530, "predicted_ms": 39089.587, "predicted_per_token_ms": 25.548749673202614, "predicted_per_second": 39.140858663971045}}', '2026-06-13 16:43:38.696647+00');
INSERT INTO public.llm_request_logs (id, url, model, input, output, created_at) VALUES (77, 'http://host.docker.internal:8080/v1/chat/completions', 'Qwen3VL-4B-Instruct-Q4_K_M.ggu', '{"model": "Qwen3VL-4B-Instruct-Q4_K_M.ggu", "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are an AI email-writing assistant for a car dealership sales representative.\nYour task is to compose a personalised outreach email to a specific customer.\n\nYou will receive:\n1. Email purpose (the reason for reaching out)\n2. Customer profile (name, note, vehicles they own/lease)\n3. Matching inventory vehicles that may be relevant to this customer\n4. The sales representative''s writing style guide (in Markdown)\n5. Customer''s full contact log (channel, date, summary of each prior interaction)\n\nRules:\n- Match the representative''s voice and style exactly as described in the style guide\n- Treat any \"Extra hard rules\" as mandatory requirements that override default phrasing\n- If the style guide includes a concrete format template, headings, or option-label pattern, follow it exactly\n- Make the email feel personal and relevant to this specific customer''s situation\n- Use the contact log to avoid repeating topics already covered, acknowledge the relationship naturally, and pick up where the last conversation left off\n- Reference their vehicle(s) naturally (e.g., lease end dates, age, type)\n- Mention 1-2 inventory options at most; do not list every car\n- Follow the word count and paragraph count specified in the style guide; if unspecified, target 180\u2013260 words\n- Always include a warm closing paragraph thanking the customer, a soft CTA (reply or call), and a professional sign-off with name and title\n- For lease/finance ending emails, prioritize a lease-end guidance format (upgrade vs buyout vs return) over inventory sales copy\n- Do NOT turn lease-end emails into price-led inventory advertisements unless explicitly requested by the user template/rules\n- Do NOT include a subject line in the body\n- Respond ONLY with a JSON object in the exact format:\n  {\"subject\": \"...\", \"body\": \"...\"}"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Email purpose: The customer''s lease or financing is ending soon. Write an email about upgrade options and next steps.\n\nCustomer: Brianna C Algee\n\nCustomer phone: (902) 225-9368\n\nNote: (none)\n\nCustomer vehicles:\n  \u2022 2022 VOLKSWAGEN TIGUAN (lease) lease ends 2026-09-16\n\nRelevant inventory:\n  (none)\n\nContact history (newest first):\n  (no prior contact logged)\n\nStyle guide:\nPrimary section to follow for this email type:\n## Lease Expiration\n\n### Subject Line\n- **Typical length**: 4\u20139 words (e.g., \u201cYour Lease is Almost Up\u201d or \u201cQuick Update: 2022 VW Tiguan\u201d)\n- **Tone and urgency**: Friendly, gentle reminder with a hint of urgency \u2014 avoids alarm, focuses on \u201coptions\u201d and \u201csmooth transition\u201d\n- **Personalisation**: Uses customer name + vehicle model/year (e.g., \u201cAndy, your 2022 VW Tiguan\u201d)\n- **Common openers**: \u201cWe want to remind you that\u2026\u201d, \u201cAs you approach the end of your lease\u2026\u201d\n- **Capitalisation**: Title case (e.g., \u201cYour End-of-Lease Options:\u201d)\n- **Use of numbers**: \u201cJuly 31, 2026\u201d \u2014 dates are explicit and formatted clearly\n- **Emojis/characters**: None \u2014 clean, professional, no frivolous symbols\n\n### Format\n- **Message length**: 3\u20135 paragraphs, concise but warm\n- **Opening line pattern**: Friendly, non-pushy greeting + light reflection (\u201cCan you believe how quickly time flies?\u201d)\n- **Body structure**: Hook \u2192 reminder \u2192 list of options \u2192 invitation to chat \u2192 CTA \u2192 closing\n- **Closing line pattern**: \u201cWarm regards, Wilson Xing | Sales Consultant\u201d \u2014 consistent, warm, no pressure\n- **Paragraph count**: 3\u20134 paragraphs, with clear spacing and line breaks\n- **Lists**: Uses numbered options (Option 1/2/3) with clear, benefit-focused descriptions\n\n### Style\n- **Tone and formality**: Warm, professional, slightly conversational \u2014 feels like a trusted advisor, not a salesperson\n- **Energy level**: Calm, reassuring, non-pushy \u2014 avoids \u201churry up\u201d or \u201cdon\u2019t miss out\u201d language\n- **Vocabulary**: Focus on \u201coptions,\u201d \u201cseamless,\u201d \u201cnavigate,\u201d \u201ctransition,\u201d \u201cvalued part of the family\u201d \u2014 builds emotional connection\n- **Vehicle references**: Uses exact model/year/trim (e.g., \u201c2022 VW Tiguan\u201d) \u2014 never vague or generic\n- **Punctuation quirks**: Uses em dashes and colons for emphasis, avoids exclamation marks except for warmth\n- **Signature**: Always \u201cWilson Xing | Sales Consultant\u201d \u2014 verbatim\n\n### Operational Rules\n- **Goal**: Remind customer of lease expiration + offer gentle, non-pressure navigation to next steps\n- **Personalization fields**: [FirstName], [Year Model] (e.g., \u201cyour 2022 VW Tiguan\u201d), lease end date (e.g., \u201cJuly 31, 2026\u201d)\n- **CTA standard**: \u201cReply directly to this email or call us at [Phone] to schedule a visit\u201d\n- **Language guardrails**: \n  - Avoid phrases like \u201cyou MUST decide\u201d or \u201clast chance\u201d\n  - Do not fabricate deals or exaggerate incentives\n  - Use \u201cwe are here to help\u201d not \u201cwe\u2019ll make it easy for you\u201d\n- **4\u20136 item quality checklist**:\n  1. Is the lease end date clearly stated?\n  2. Are all 3 options clearly labeled and described?\n  3. Does the CTA include both reply and phone option?\n  4. Is the closing line \u201cWarm regards, Wilson Xing | Sales Consultant\u201d included?\n  5. Is the tone warm, professional, and non-pushy?\n  6. Are vehicle model/year/trim accurately referenced?\n\n- **Option block required**: \n  - **Heading**: \u201cYour End-of-Lease Options:\u201d\n  - **Option format**: \u201cOption 1: [Description]\u201d \u2014 must be numbered, benefit-focused, concise\n\n---\n\nAlso stay consistent with the rest of the style guide.\n\nRequired format checklist:\n  \u2022 Use a greeting line with the customer''s first name.\n  \u2022 Keep clean paragraph spacing.\n  \u2022 Include a soft CTA paragraph before the sign-off.\n  \u2022 Reference the lease/finance end date in the opening.\n  \u2022 Use the heading \"Your End-of-Lease Options:\".\n  \u2022 Format choices as Option 1 / Option 2 / Option 3 (not generic numbered bullets).\n  \u2022 Include all 3 options explicitly: upgrade, purchase current vehicle, return vehicle.\n  \u2022 Do not include dollar prices, stock-style vehicle listings, or inventory bullet pitches.\n\nExtra hard rules (non-negotiable):\n  \u2022 make this is fix email ending\nBest regards,\nWilson Xing | Sales Consultant"}]}', '{"choices": [{"finish_reason": "stop", "index": 0, "message": {"role": "assistant", "content": "{\n  \"subject\": \"Your 2022 VW Tiguan Lease Ends July 31, 2026\",\n  \"body\": \"Hi Brianna,\\n\\nCan you believe how quickly time flies? We\u2019re here to help you navigate your 2022 VW Tiguan lease end on July 31, 2026 \u2014 and we know this transition doesn\u2019t have to feel overwhelming.\\n\\nYour End-of-Lease Options:\\n\\nOption 1: Upgrade to a new vehicle \u2014 we can help you find a car that fits your needs, lifestyle, and budget without forcing a change.\\nOption 2: Purchase your 2022 VW Tiguan \u2014 we\u2019ll walk you through the process and help you get the best value for your investment.\\nOption 3: Return your vehicle \u2014 we\u2019ll handle the paperwork and ensure a smooth handoff.\\n\\nWe\u2019re happy to schedule a quick call or visit anytime \u2014 just reply to this email or call us at (902) 225-9368. No pressure, no rush \u2014 we\u2019re here to make this seamless.\\n\\nWarm regards,\\nWilson Xing | Sales Consultant\"\n}"}}], "created": 1781369044, "model": "Qwen3VL-4B-Instruct-Q4_K_M.gguf", "system_fingerprint": "b9590-d2462f8f7", "object": "chat.completion", "usage": {"completion_tokens": 253, "prompt_tokens": 1465, "total_tokens": 1718, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 520}}, "id": "chatcmpl-eteMbfBc6vpvap2g5z1LIHtvVzIHrVuV", "timings": {"cache_n": 520, "prompt_n": 945, "prompt_ms": 2642.056, "prompt_per_token_ms": 2.795826455026455, "prompt_per_second": 357.67599172765455, "predicted_n": 253, "predicted_ms": 6633.205, "predicted_per_token_ms": 26.218201581027667, "predicted_per_second": 38.141441429897014}}', '2026-06-13 16:44:04.719109+00');
INSERT INTO public.llm_request_logs (id, url, model, input, output, created_at) VALUES (78, 'http://host.docker.internal:8080/v1/chat/completions', 'Qwen3VL-4B-Instruct-Q4_K_M.ggu', '{"model": "Qwen3VL-4B-Instruct-Q4_K_M.ggu", "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are an AI email-writing assistant for a car dealership sales representative.\nYour task is to compose a personalised outreach email to a specific customer.\n\nYou will receive:\n1. Email purpose (the reason for reaching out)\n2. Customer profile (name, note, vehicles they own/lease)\n3. Matching inventory vehicles that may be relevant to this customer\n4. The sales representative''s writing style guide (in Markdown)\n5. Customer''s full contact log (channel, date, summary of each prior interaction)\n\nRules:\n- Match the representative''s voice and style exactly as described in the style guide\n- Treat any \"Extra hard rules\" as mandatory requirements that override default phrasing\n- If the style guide includes a concrete format template, headings, or option-label pattern, follow it exactly\n- Make the email feel personal and relevant to this specific customer''s situation\n- Use the contact log to avoid repeating topics already covered, acknowledge the relationship naturally, and pick up where the last conversation left off\n- Reference their vehicle(s) naturally (e.g., lease end dates, age, type)\n- Mention 1-2 inventory options at most; do not list every car\n- Follow the word count and paragraph count specified in the style guide; if unspecified, target 180\u2013260 words\n- Always include a warm closing paragraph thanking the customer, a soft CTA (reply or call), and a professional sign-off with name and title\n- For lease/finance ending emails, prioritize a lease-end guidance format (upgrade vs buyout vs return) over inventory sales copy\n- Do NOT turn lease-end emails into price-led inventory advertisements unless explicitly requested by the user template/rules\n- Do NOT include a subject line in the body\n- Respond ONLY with a JSON object in the exact format:\n  {\"subject\": \"...\", \"body\": \"...\"}"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Email purpose: The customer''s lease or financing is ending soon. Write an email about upgrade options and next steps.\n\nCustomer: Brianna C Algee\n\nCustomer phone: (902) 225-9368\n\nNote: (none)\n\nCustomer vehicles:\n  \u2022 2022 VOLKSWAGEN TIGUAN (lease) lease ends 2026-09-16\n\nRelevant inventory:\n  (none)\n\nContact history (newest first):\n  (no prior contact logged)\n\nStyle guide:\nPrimary section to follow for this email type:\n## Lease Expiration\n\n### Subject Line\n- **Typical length**: 4\u20139 words (e.g., \u201cYour Lease is Almost Up\u201d or \u201cQuick Update: 2022 VW Tiguan\u201d)\n- **Tone and urgency**: Friendly, gentle reminder with a hint of urgency \u2014 avoids alarm, focuses on \u201coptions\u201d and \u201csmooth transition\u201d\n- **Personalisation**: Uses customer name + vehicle model/year (e.g., \u201cAndy, your 2022 VW Tiguan\u201d)\n- **Common openers**: \u201cWe want to remind you that\u2026\u201d, \u201cAs you approach the end of your lease\u2026\u201d\n- **Capitalisation**: Title case (e.g., \u201cYour End-of-Lease Options:\u201d)\n- **Use of numbers**: \u201cJuly 31, 2026\u201d \u2014 dates are explicit and formatted clearly\n- **Emojis/characters**: None \u2014 clean, professional, no frivolous symbols\n\n### Format\n- **Message length**: 3\u20135 paragraphs, concise but warm\n- **Opening line pattern**: Friendly, non-pushy greeting + light reflection (\u201cCan you believe how quickly time flies?\u201d)\n- **Body structure**: Hook \u2192 reminder \u2192 list of options \u2192 invitation to chat \u2192 CTA \u2192 closing\n- **Closing line pattern**: \u201cWarm regards, Wilson Xing | Sales Consultant\u201d \u2014 consistent, warm, no pressure\n- **Paragraph count**: 3\u20134 paragraphs, with clear spacing and line breaks\n- **Lists**: Uses numbered options (Option 1/2/3) with clear, benefit-focused descriptions\n\n### Style\n- **Tone and formality**: Warm, professional, slightly conversational \u2014 feels like a trusted advisor, not a salesperson\n- **Energy level**: Calm, reassuring, non-pushy \u2014 avoids \u201churry up\u201d or \u201cdon\u2019t miss out\u201d language\n- **Vocabulary**: Focus on \u201coptions,\u201d \u201cseamless,\u201d \u201cnavigate,\u201d \u201ctransition,\u201d \u201cvalued part of the family\u201d \u2014 builds emotional connection\n- **Vehicle references**: Uses exact model/year/trim (e.g., \u201c2022 VW Tiguan\u201d) \u2014 never vague or generic\n- **Punctuation quirks**: Uses em dashes and colons for emphasis, avoids exclamation marks except for warmth\n- **Signature**: Always \u201cWilson Xing | Sales Consultant\u201d \u2014 verbatim\n\n### Operational Rules\n- **Goal**: Remind customer of lease expiration + offer gentle, non-pressure navigation to next steps\n- **Personalization fields**: [FirstName], [Year Model] (e.g., \u201cyour 2022 VW Tiguan\u201d), lease end date (e.g., \u201cJuly 31, 2026\u201d)\n- **CTA standard**: \u201cReply directly to this email or call us at [Phone] to schedule a visit\u201d\n- **Language guardrails**: \n  - Avoid phrases like \u201cyou MUST decide\u201d or \u201clast chance\u201d\n  - Do not fabricate deals or exaggerate incentives\n  - Use \u201cwe are here to help\u201d not \u201cwe\u2019ll make it easy for you\u201d\n- **4\u20136 item quality checklist**:\n  1. Is the lease end date clearly stated?\n  2. Are all 3 options clearly labeled and described?\n  3. Does the CTA include both reply and phone option?\n  4. Is the closing line \u201cWarm regards, Wilson Xing | Sales Consultant\u201d included?\n  5. Is the tone warm, professional, and non-pushy?\n  6. Are vehicle model/year/trim accurately referenced?\n\n- **Option block required**: \n  - **Heading**: \u201cYour End-of-Lease Options:\u201d\n  - **Option format**: \u201cOption 1: [Description]\u201d \u2014 must be numbered, benefit-focused, concise\n\n---\n\nAlso stay consistent with the rest of the style guide.\n\nRequired format checklist:\n  \u2022 Use a greeting line with the customer''s first name.\n  \u2022 Keep clean paragraph spacing.\n  \u2022 Include a soft CTA paragraph before the sign-off.\n  \u2022 Reference the lease/finance end date in the opening.\n  \u2022 Use the heading \"Your End-of-Lease Options:\".\n  \u2022 Format choices as Option 1 / Option 2 / Option 3 (not generic numbered bullets).\n  \u2022 Include all 3 options explicitly: upgrade, purchase current vehicle, return vehicle.\n  \u2022 Do not include dollar prices, stock-style vehicle listings, or inventory bullet pitches.\n\nExtra hard rules (non-negotiable):\n  \u2022 make this is fix email ending\nBest regards,\nWilson Xing | Sales Consultant"}]}', '{"choices": [{"finish_reason": "stop", "index": 0, "message": {"role": "assistant", "content": "{\n  \"subject\": \"Your 2022 VW Tiguan Lease Ends July 31, 2026\",\n  \"body\": \"Hi Brianna,\\n\\nCan you believe how quickly time flies? We\u2019re reaching the end of your 2022 VW Tiguan lease \u2014 July 31, 2026 \u2014 and we\u2019re here to help you navigate what\u2019s next, without any pressure.\\n\\nYour End-of-Lease Options:\\n\\nOption 1: Upgrade \u2014 Take the next step with a new vehicle that fits your lifestyle, schedule, and needs. We\u2019ll work with you to find something that feels like a natural next chapter.\\n\\nOption 2: Purchase \u2014 Keep your 2022 VW Tiguan and take ownership. We\u2019ll guide you through the process to ensure you get the best value and terms for your current ride.\\n\\nOption 3: Return \u2014 If you\u2019re ready to let go and explore something new, we\u2019ll handle the return process smoothly and ensure you\u2019re fully supported.\\n\\nYou can reply directly to this email or call us at (902) 225-9368 to schedule a visit \u2014 we\u2019re happy to chat and make this transition seamless for you.\\n\\nWarm regards,\\nWilson Xing | Sales Consultant\"\n}"}}], "created": 1781369080, "model": "Qwen3VL-4B-Instruct-Q4_K_M.gguf", "system_fingerprint": "b9590-d2462f8f7", "object": "chat.completion", "usage": {"completion_tokens": 279, "prompt_tokens": 1465, "total_tokens": 1744, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 1464}}, "id": "chatcmpl-BviFdKqHrl2mIcY2srLHoHgS2ZUmiyaE", "timings": {"cache_n": 1464, "prompt_n": 1, "prompt_ms": 86.778, "prompt_per_token_ms": 86.778, "prompt_per_second": 11.523658070017746, "predicted_n": 279, "predicted_ms": 7356.287, "predicted_per_token_ms": 26.36662007168459, "predicted_per_second": 37.92674211868025}}', '2026-06-13 16:44:40.530975+00');
INSERT INTO public.llm_request_logs (id, url, model, input, output, created_at) VALUES (79, 'http://host.docker.internal:8080/v1/chat/completions', 'Qwen3VL-4B-Instruct-Q4_K_M.ggu', '{"model": "Qwen3VL-4B-Instruct-Q4_K_M.ggu", "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are an AI email-writing assistant for a car dealership sales representative.\nYour task is to compose a personalised outreach email to a specific customer.\n\nYou will receive:\n1. Email purpose (the reason for reaching out)\n2. Customer profile (name, note, vehicles they own/lease)\n3. Matching inventory vehicles that may be relevant to this customer\n4. The sales representative''s writing style guide (in Markdown)\n5. Customer''s full contact log (channel, date, summary of each prior interaction)\n\nRules:\n- Match the representative''s voice and style exactly as described in the style guide\n- Treat any \"Extra hard rules\" as mandatory requirements that override default phrasing\n- If the style guide includes a concrete format template, headings, or option-label pattern, follow it exactly\n- Make the email feel personal and relevant to this specific customer''s situation\n- Use the contact log to avoid repeating topics already covered, acknowledge the relationship naturally, and pick up where the last conversation left off\n- Reference their vehicle(s) naturally (e.g., lease end dates, age, type)\n- Mention 1-2 inventory options at most; do not list every car\n- Follow the word count and paragraph count specified in the style guide; if unspecified, target 180\u2013260 words\n- Always include a warm closing paragraph thanking the customer, a soft CTA (reply or call), and a professional sign-off with name and title\n- For lease/finance ending emails, prioritize a lease-end guidance format (upgrade vs buyout vs return) over inventory sales copy\n- Do NOT turn lease-end emails into price-led inventory advertisements unless explicitly requested by the user template/rules\n- Do NOT include a subject line in the body\n- Respond ONLY with a JSON object in the exact format:\n  {\"subject\": \"...\", \"body\": \"...\"}"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Email purpose: The customer''s lease or financing is ending soon. Write an email about upgrade options and next steps.\n\nCustomer: Brianna C Algee\n\nCustomer phone: (902) 225-9368\n\nNote: (none)\n\nCustomer vehicles:\n  \u2022 2022 VOLKSWAGEN TIGUAN (lease) lease ends 2026-09-16\n\nRelevant inventory:\n  (none)\n\nContact history (newest first):\n  (no prior contact logged)\n\nStyle guide:\nPrimary section to follow for this email type:\n## Lease Expiration\n\n### Subject Line\n- **Typical length**: 4\u20139 words (e.g., \u201cYour Lease is Almost Up\u201d or \u201cQuick Update: 2022 VW Tiguan\u201d)\n- **Tone and urgency**: Friendly, gentle reminder with a hint of urgency \u2014 avoids alarm, focuses on \u201coptions\u201d and \u201csmooth transition\u201d\n- **Personalisation**: Uses customer name + vehicle model/year (e.g., \u201cAndy, your 2022 VW Tiguan\u201d)\n- **Common openers**: \u201cWe want to remind you that\u2026\u201d, \u201cAs you approach the end of your lease\u2026\u201d\n- **Capitalisation**: Title case (e.g., \u201cYour End-of-Lease Options:\u201d)\n- **Use of numbers**: \u201cJuly 31, 2026\u201d \u2014 dates are explicit and formatted clearly\n- **Emojis/characters**: None \u2014 clean, professional, no frivolous symbols\n\n### Format\n- **Message length**: 3\u20135 paragraphs, concise but warm\n- **Opening line pattern**: Friendly, non-pushy greeting + light reflection (\u201cCan you believe how quickly time flies?\u201d)\n- **Body structure**: Hook \u2192 reminder \u2192 list of options \u2192 invitation to chat \u2192 CTA \u2192 closing\n- **Closing line pattern**: \u201cWarm regards, Wilson Xing | Sales Consultant\u201d \u2014 consistent, warm, no pressure\n- **Paragraph count**: 3\u20134 paragraphs, with clear spacing and line breaks\n- **Lists**: Uses numbered options (Option 1/2/3) with clear, benefit-focused descriptions\n\n### Style\n- **Tone and formality**: Warm, professional, slightly conversational \u2014 feels like a trusted advisor, not a salesperson\n- **Energy level**: Calm, reassuring, non-pushy \u2014 avoids \u201churry up\u201d or \u201cdon\u2019t miss out\u201d language\n- **Vocabulary**: Focus on \u201coptions,\u201d \u201cseamless,\u201d \u201cnavigate,\u201d \u201ctransition,\u201d \u201cvalued part of the family\u201d \u2014 builds emotional connection\n- **Vehicle references**: Uses exact model/year/trim (e.g., \u201c2022 VW Tiguan\u201d) \u2014 never vague or generic\n- **Punctuation quirks**: Uses em dashes and colons for emphasis, avoids exclamation marks except for warmth\n- **Signature**: Always \u201cWilson Xing | Sales Consultant\u201d \u2014 verbatim\n\n### Operational Rules\n- **Goal**: Remind customer of lease expiration + offer gentle, non-pressure navigation to next steps\n- **Personalization fields**: [FirstName], [Year Model] (e.g., \u201cyour 2022 VW Tiguan\u201d), lease end date (e.g., \u201cJuly 31, 2026\u201d)\n- **CTA standard**: \u201cReply directly to this email or call us at [Phone] to schedule a visit\u201d\n- **Language guardrails**: \n  - Avoid phrases like \u201cyou MUST decide\u201d or \u201clast chance\u201d\n  - Do not fabricate deals or exaggerate incentives\n  - Use \u201cwe are here to help\u201d not \u201cwe\u2019ll make it easy for you\u201d\n- **4\u20136 item quality checklist**:\n  1. Is the lease end date clearly stated?\n  2. Are all 3 options clearly labeled and described?\n  3. Does the CTA include both reply and phone option?\n  4. Is the closing line \u201cWarm regards, Wilson Xing | Sales Consultant\u201d included?\n  5. Is the tone warm, professional, and non-pushy?\n  6. Are vehicle model/year/trim accurately referenced?\n\n- **Option block required**: \n  - **Heading**: \u201cYour End-of-Lease Options:\u201d\n  - **Option format**: \u201cOption 1: [Description]\u201d \u2014 must be numbered, benefit-focused, concise\n\n---\n\nAlso stay consistent with the rest of the style guide.\n\nRequired format checklist:\n  \u2022 Use a greeting line with the customer''s first name.\n  \u2022 Keep clean paragraph spacing.\n  \u2022 Include a soft CTA paragraph before the sign-off.\n  \u2022 Reference the lease/finance end date in the opening.\n  \u2022 Use the heading \"Your End-of-Lease Options:\".\n  \u2022 Format choices as Option 1 / Option 2 / Option 3 (not generic numbered bullets).\n  \u2022 Include all 3 options explicitly: upgrade, purchase current vehicle, return vehicle.\n  \u2022 Do not include dollar prices, stock-style vehicle listings, or inventory bullet pitches.\n\nExtra hard rules (non-negotiable):\n  \u2022 make this is fix email ending\nBest regards,\nWilson Xing | Sales Consultant"}]}', '{"choices": [{"finish_reason": "stop", "index": 0, "message": {"role": "assistant", "content": "{\n  \"subject\": \"Your 2022 VW Tiguan Lease Ends July 31, 2026\",\n  \"body\": \"Hi Brianna,\\n\\nCan you believe how quickly time flies? It\u2019s been a while since you brought your 2022 VW Tiguan home \u2014 and we\u2019re excited to help you make the next move as smoothly as possible as your lease ends July 31, 2026.\\n\\nYour End-of-Lease Options:\\n\\nOption 1: Upgrade to a new vehicle \u2014 keep the same brand and feel the excitement of a fresh model, with our expert guidance to match your needs.\\nOption 2: Purchase your current 2022 VW Tiguan \u2014 a smart, no-pressure way to take ownership with a fair, pre-approved price.\\nOption 3: Return the vehicle \u2014 we\u2019ll handle all paperwork and logistics, so you can move on without stress.\\n\\nWe\u2019re here to help you navigate this transition \u2014 whether you\u2019re ready to upgrade, buy, or return. Just reply directly to this email or call us at (902) 225-9368 to schedule a visit.\\n\\nWarm regards,\\nWilson Xing | Sales Consultant\"\n}"}}], "created": 1781369168, "model": "Qwen3VL-4B-Instruct-Q4_K_M.gguf", "system_fingerprint": "b9590-d2462f8f7", "object": "chat.completion", "usage": {"completion_tokens": 266, "prompt_tokens": 1465, "total_tokens": 1731, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 1464}}, "id": "chatcmpl-zqEdbVxB3aUbovldkAcVfXUFZ5wXKY5B", "timings": {"cache_n": 1464, "prompt_n": 1, "prompt_ms": 98.13, "prompt_per_token_ms": 98.13, "prompt_per_second": 10.19056353816366, "predicted_n": 266, "predicted_ms": 6982.937, "predicted_per_token_ms": 26.25164285714286, "predicted_per_second": 38.092854052671534}}', '2026-06-13 16:46:08.217275+00');
INSERT INTO public.llm_request_logs (id, url, model, input, output, created_at) VALUES (80, 'http://host.docker.internal:8080/v1/chat/completions', 'Qwen3VL-4B-Instruct-Q4_K_M.ggu', '{"model": "Qwen3VL-4B-Instruct-Q4_K_M.ggu", "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a writing style analyst for a car dealership sales team.\nYour task is to study the provided sample messages and distill the writer''s unique communication style\ninto a concise, actionable markdown guide. Another AI will use this guide to write new messages\nthat faithfully match this person''s voice and style.\n\nThe writer''s samples are organized into the following categories:\n- Lease Expiration\n- Test Drive Follow-Up\n\nProduce one ## section for each category that has samples provided, using the exact category name as the ## heading.\nIf any sample does not match a named category, place it under ## General.\nDo NOT produce sections for categories that have no samples.\n\nEach category section MUST contain exactly three sub-sections:\n\n### Subject Line\nDescribe the subject line patterns observed across the samples:\n- Typical length (capture what works in practice; for email this is often around 4-9 words)\n- Tone and urgency (e.g. friendly teaser, direct offer, question)\n- Use of personalisation (customer name, vehicle details)\n- Common openers or formulas (e.g. \"Your [Year] [Model] is ready\", \"Quick update on\u2026\")\n- Capitalisation style (title case, sentence case, all-lower)\n- Use of numbers, emojis, or special characters\n- Anything that makes the subject line pattern recognisable\n\n### Format\nDescribe the structural/layout conventions observed in the samples:\n- Message length (give realistic ranges; avoid strict limits unless samples consistently enforce them)\n- Opening line pattern (greeting style, whether name is used)\n- Body structure (e.g. one hook sentence \u2192 offer \u2192 CTA)\n- Closing line pattern (sign-off, signature style)\n- Paragraph count and spacing habits\n- Use of bullet points, line breaks, or lists\n\n### Style\nDescribe the voice and language patterns:\n- Tone and formality level for this situation\n- Energy level (urgent, warm, casual, professional)\n- Vocabulary preferences and any signature phrases or pet words\n- How they reference vehicles (make/model/year/trim usage)\n- Use of emojis, punctuation quirks, or capitalisation habits\n- Anything that makes this person''s writing instantly recognisable\n- If the closing/signature phrase is consistent, capture the exact required wording verbatim in quotes\n\nAfter those required sub-sections, add a short \"### Operational Rules\" section for each category with:\n- Goal (what the email is trying to achieve for this category)\n- Personalization fields to include (e.g. [FirstName], [Year Model], relevant date, [Phone])\n- CTA standard (one primary action at the end)\n- Language guardrails (non-pushy phrasing, no overpromising, no fabricated offers)\n- A 4-6 item quality checklist for before-send review\n- For lease/finance ending categories, if samples use a named options block, explicitly define the required heading and option-label format (e.g., \"Option 1/2/3\")\n\nPrefer specific, reusable rules over abstract advice.\nOutput a clean markdown document. Do NOT include any samples verbatim."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Channel: email\n\n### Lease Expiration\n\nHi Andy\nI hope this email finds you well.\nCan you believe how quickly time flies? We want to remind you that the lease on your 2022 VW Tiguan is scheduled to mature on July 31, 2026.\nAs you approach the end of your lease, you have a few great options available to you, and we want to make sure the transition is as smooth and seamless as possible. Whether you want to upgrade, keep your current ride, or simply hand over the keys, we are here to help you navigate the next steps.\nYour End-of-Lease Options:\nOption 1: Upgrade to a new model. Get behind the wheel of a brand-new vehicle with the latest technology, safety features, and a fresh warranty.\nOption 2: Purchase your current vehicle. If you\u2019ve fallen in love with your car and aren''t ready to part ways, you can buy it out for the residual value listed in your contract.\nOption 3: Return the vehicle. Simply schedule an inspection and return the keys to us at the end of your term.\nLet''s Find the Best Path Forward\nWe would love to invite you back into the dealership for a quick, no-pressure chat to review these options, check out current inventory, and see what specials might apply to you.\nPlease reply directly to this email or call us at 9024076395 to schedule a convenient time for you to drop by.\nThank you so much for being a valued part of the O''Regan''s VW family. We look forward to assisting you with your next automotive chapter!\nWarm regards,\nWilson Xing | Sales Consultant\n\n### Test Drive Follow-Up\n\nHi Andy,\nThank you for taking the time to visit us yesterday and test driving the 2026 Jetta Comfortline. It was a pleasure meeting you and showing you what the Jetta has to offer.\nI completely understand and respect your decision to test drive a few other options in the market before making your final move. Investing in a new vehicle is a big decision, and you want to ensure it\u2019s the perfect fit.\nWhile you are doing your research, I did want to give you a quick heads-up on an incentive that just came up for this month. Volkswagen is currently offering a 0.99% special finance rate for up to 60 months (5 years) on the 2026 Jetta. It\u2019s one of the strongest programs we''ve seen in a while, and it definitely keeps the monthly payments incredibly comfortable on that Comfortline trim.\nIf you have any questions about how those numbers look for your budget while you compare your options, just let me know.\nI would love the opportunity to earn your business. Drive safe during your other test drives, and I look forward to connecting with you soon!\nBest regards,\nWilson Xing | Sales Consultant"}]}', '{"choices": [{"finish_reason": "stop", "index": 0, "message": {"role": "assistant", "content": "## Lease Expiration\n\n### Subject Line\n- **Typical length**: 4\u20139 words (e.g., \u201cYour Lease Ends Soon\u201d or \u201cQuick Update: 2022 Tiguan\u201d)\n- **Tone and urgency**: Friendly but timely \u2014 implies \u201cthis is your window to act\u201d\n- **Personalisation**: Uses customer name + vehicle model/year (e.g., \u201cAndy, your 2022 VW Tiguan\u201d)\n- **Common openers**: \u201cCan you believe how quickly time flies?\u201d \u2014 light, conversational hook\n- **Capitalisation**: Title case for subject lines (e.g., \u201cYour Lease Ends Soon\u201d)\n- **Use of numbers**: Explicit dates or terms (e.g., \u201cJuly 31, 2026\u201d)\n- **Emojis/characters**: None used \u2014 clean, professional tone\n\n### Format\n- **Message length**: 6\u20138 paragraphs; concise but warm\n- **Opening line pattern**: Friendly opener (\u201cHi Andy\u2026\u201d) \u2192 soft transition into topic\n- **Body structure**: Hook \u2192 reminder \u2192 options list \u2192 CTA \u2192 appreciation\n- **Closing line pattern**: \u201cWarm regards, Wilson Xing | Sales Consultant\u201d \u2014 signature phrase used verbatim\n- **Paragraph count and spacing**: 1\u20132 paragraphs per section, with space between options and CTAs\n- **Lists**: Clear, numbered options (Option 1/2/3) \u2014 bold or simple bullet style\n\n### Style\n- **Tone and formality**: Warm, professional, consultative \u2014 avoids \u201csalesy\u201d language\n- **Energy level**: Calm, encouraging, reassuring \u2014 \u201cno-pressure chat\u201d is key\n- **Vocabulary preferences**: \u201cEnd-of-lease,\u201d \u201ctransition,\u201d \u201cnavigate,\u201d \u201cseamless,\u201d \u201cbest path forward\u201d\n- **Vehicle references**: \u201c2022 VW Tiguan\u201d \u2014 exact model + year used; trim optional\n- **Emojis/punctuation quirks**: None; uses full stops and commas; no caps except for proper nouns\n- **Signature**: \u201cWarm regards, Wilson Xing | Sales Consultant\u201d \u2014 exact phrase, never abbreviated\n\n### Operational Rules\n- **Goal**: Remind customer of lease expiry + offer seamless transition with 3 clear paths\n- **Personalization fields**: [FirstName], [Year Model] (e.g., \u201c2022 VW Tiguan\u201d), lease end date (July 31, 2026)\n- **CTA standard**: \u201cReply or call us at [Phone] to schedule a visit\u201d \u2014 one primary action\n- **Language guardrails**:  \n  - Avoid \u201cYou must\u2026\u201d or \u201cDon\u2019t miss\u2026\u201d \u2014 instead say \u201cyou have options\u2026\u201d  \n  - Never say \u201cWe\u2019ll make it easy\u201d \u2014 use \u201cwe\u2019re here to help you navigate\u2026\u201d  \n  - No fabricated incentives \u2014 only list *actual* contract options\n- **Quality checklist (4\u20136 items)**:  \n  1. Has [FirstName], [Year Model], and lease end date included?  \n  2. Is \u201cOption 1/2/3\u201d clearly labeled?  \n  3. Is the CTA specific (reply or call + phone number)?  \n  4. Is \u201cno-pressure chat\u201d mentioned?  \n  5. Does closing say \u201cWarm regards, Wilson Xing | Sales Consultant\u201d?  \n  6. Does the tone avoid pressure or urgency?  \n\n---\n\n## Test Drive Follow-Up\n\n### Subject Line\n- **Typical length**: 4\u20137 words (e.g., \u201cJetta Incentive Alert!\u201d or \u201cYour Test Drive Notes\u201d)\n- **Tone and urgency**: Friendly, appreciative, slightly encouraging \u2014 no pressure\n- **Personalisation**: Uses customer name + vehicle + trim (e.g., \u201cAndy, 2026 Jetta Comfortline\u201d)\n- **Common openers**: \u201cHi Andy, thank you for taking the time\u2026\u201d \u2014 warm, personal start\n- **Capitalisation**: Title case for subject lines (e.g., \u201cJetta Incentive Alert!\u201d)\n- **Use of numbers**: \u201c0.99% rate for up to 60 months\u201d \u2014 explicit, numerically driven\n- **Emojis/characters**: None used \u2014 clean, professional\n\n### Format\n- **Message length**: 5\u20137 paragraphs; conversational, not salesy\n- **Opening line pattern**: Personal greeting \u2192 \u201cthank you\u201d \u2192 soft transition into topic\n- **Body structure**: Gratitude \u2192 acknowledge research \u2192 incentive drop \u2192 offer to answer questions \u2192 closing\n- **Closing line pattern**: \u201cBest regards, Wilson Xing | Sales Consultant\u201d \u2014 signature phrase used verbatim\n- **Paragraph count and spacing**: 1\u20132 paragraphs per idea; friendly spacing between sections\n- **Lists**: None \u2014 no bullet points; uses clear sentence structure\n\n### Style\n- **Tone and formality**: Warm, respectful, consultative \u2014 \u201cI understand\u201d and \u201cyou want to ensure\u2026\u201d\n- **Energy level**: Friendly, encouraging, low-pressure \u2014 \u201cyou\u2019re doing your research, we\u2019re here\u201d\n- **Vocabulary preferences**: \u201cInvesting in a new vehicle is a big decision,\u201d \u201cyou want to ensure,\u201d \u201cone of the strongest programs we\u2019ve seen\u201d\n- **Vehicle references**: \u201c2026 Jetta Comfortline\u201d \u2014 exact model, trim, year\n- **Emojis/punctuation quirks**: None; uses full stops and commas; no caps except for proper nouns\n- **Signature**: \u201cBest regards, Wilson Xing | Sales Consultant\u201d \u2014 exact phrase, never abbreviated\n\n### Operational Rules\n- **Goal**: Reconnect after test drive + offer timely, non-pushy incentive\n- **Personalization fields**: [FirstName], [Year Model] (e.g., \u201c2026 Jetta Comfortline\u201d), incentive details\n- **CTA standard**: \u201cJust let me know if you\u2019d like to compare numbers\u2026\u201d \u2014 open-ended, low-pressure\n- **Language guardrails**:  \n  - Avoid \u201cYou should\u2026\u201d \u2014 use \u201cI understand\u2026\u201d  \n  - Never say \u201cWe\u2019re offering this to help you decide\u201d \u2014 instead say \u201cIt\u2019s one of the strongest programs\u2026\u201d  \n  - No fabricated deals \u2014 only mention *current* finance rate\n- **Quality checklist (4\u20136 items)**:  \n  1. Is [FirstName], [Year Model] included?  \n  2. Is the incentive rate and term clearly stated (e.g., \u201c0.99% for 60 months\u201d)?  \n  3. Is \u201cI understand\u2026\u201d or \u201cyou\u2019re doing your research\u201d used?  \n  4. Is \u201cBest regards, Wilson Xing | Sales Consultant\u201d used?  \n  5. Is the CTA open-ended (\u201cjust let me know\u201d) and not pushy?  \n  6. Does it avoid pressure or urgency?"}}], "created": 1781369219, "model": "Qwen3VL-4B-Instruct-Q4_K_M.gguf", "system_fingerprint": "b9590-d2462f8f7", "object": "chat.completion", "usage": {"completion_tokens": 1439, "prompt_tokens": 1236, "total_tokens": 2675, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 1235}}, "id": "chatcmpl-a4xIRe9lNN1skT2E3w9zdkZTG0v7cZY9", "timings": {"cache_n": 1235, "prompt_n": 1, "prompt_ms": 82.85, "prompt_per_token_ms": 82.85, "prompt_per_second": 12.070006035003018, "predicted_n": 1439, "predicted_ms": 36844.408, "predicted_per_token_ms": 25.604175121612233, "predicted_per_second": 39.05613030883818}}', '2026-06-13 16:46:59.311502+00');
INSERT INTO public.llm_request_logs (id, url, model, input, output, created_at) VALUES (81, 'http://host.docker.internal:8080/v1/chat/completions', 'Qwen3VL-4B-Instruct-Q4_K_M.ggu', '{"model": "Qwen3VL-4B-Instruct-Q4_K_M.ggu", "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are an AI email-writing assistant for a car dealership sales representative.\nYour task is to compose a personalised outreach email to a specific customer.\n\nYou will receive:\n1. Email purpose (the reason for reaching out)\n2. Customer profile (name, note, vehicles they own/lease)\n3. Matching inventory vehicles that may be relevant to this customer\n4. The sales representative''s writing style guide (in Markdown)\n5. Customer''s full contact log (channel, date, summary of each prior interaction)\n\nRules:\n- Match the representative''s voice and style exactly as described in the style guide\n- Treat any \"Extra hard rules\" as mandatory requirements that override default phrasing\n- If the style guide includes a concrete format template, headings, or option-label pattern, follow it exactly\n- Make the email feel personal and relevant to this specific customer''s situation\n- Use the contact log to avoid repeating topics already covered, acknowledge the relationship naturally, and pick up where the last conversation left off\n- Reference their vehicle(s) naturally (e.g., lease end dates, age, type)\n- Mention 1-2 inventory options at most; do not list every car\n- Follow the word count and paragraph count specified in the style guide; if unspecified, target 180\u2013260 words\n- Always include a warm closing paragraph thanking the customer, a soft CTA (reply or call), and a professional sign-off with name and title\n- For lease/finance ending emails, prioritize a lease-end guidance format (upgrade vs buyout vs return) over inventory sales copy\n- Do NOT turn lease-end emails into price-led inventory advertisements unless explicitly requested by the user template/rules\n- Do NOT include a subject line in the body\n- Respond ONLY with a JSON object in the exact format:\n  {\"subject\": \"...\", \"body\": \"...\"}"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Email purpose: The customer''s lease or financing is ending soon. Write an email about upgrade options and next steps.\n\nCustomer: Brianna C Algee\n\nCustomer phone: (902) 225-9368\n\nNote: (none)\n\nCustomer vehicles:\n  \u2022 2022 VOLKSWAGEN TIGUAN (lease) lease ends 2026-09-16\n\nRelevant inventory:\n  (none)\n\nContact history (newest first):\n  (no prior contact logged)\n\nStyle guide:\nPrimary section to follow for this email type:\n## Lease Expiration\n\n### Subject Line\n- **Typical length**: 4\u20139 words (e.g., \u201cYour Lease Ends Soon\u201d or \u201cQuick Update: 2022 Tiguan\u201d)\n- **Tone and urgency**: Friendly but timely \u2014 implies \u201cthis is your window to act\u201d\n- **Personalisation**: Uses customer name + vehicle model/year (e.g., \u201cAndy, your 2022 VW Tiguan\u201d)\n- **Common openers**: \u201cCan you believe how quickly time flies?\u201d \u2014 light, conversational hook\n- **Capitalisation**: Title case for subject lines (e.g., \u201cYour Lease Ends Soon\u201d)\n- **Use of numbers**: Explicit dates or terms (e.g., \u201cJuly 31, 2026\u201d)\n- **Emojis/characters**: None used \u2014 clean, professional tone\n\n### Format\n- **Message length**: 6\u20138 paragraphs; concise but warm\n- **Opening line pattern**: Friendly opener (\u201cHi Andy\u2026\u201d) \u2192 soft transition into topic\n- **Body structure**: Hook \u2192 reminder \u2192 options list \u2192 CTA \u2192 appreciation\n- **Closing line pattern**: \u201cWarm regards, Wilson Xing | Sales Consultant\u201d \u2014 signature phrase used verbatim\n- **Paragraph count and spacing**: 1\u20132 paragraphs per section, with space between options and CTAs\n- **Lists**: Clear, numbered options (Option 1/2/3) \u2014 bold or simple bullet style\n\n### Style\n- **Tone and formality**: Warm, professional, consultative \u2014 avoids \u201csalesy\u201d language\n- **Energy level**: Calm, encouraging, reassuring \u2014 \u201cno-pressure chat\u201d is key\n- **Vocabulary preferences**: \u201cEnd-of-lease,\u201d \u201ctransition,\u201d \u201cnavigate,\u201d \u201cseamless,\u201d \u201cbest path forward\u201d\n- **Vehicle references**: \u201c2022 VW Tiguan\u201d \u2014 exact model + year used; trim optional\n- **Emojis/punctuation quirks**: None; uses full stops and commas; no caps except for proper nouns\n- **Signature**: \u201cWarm regards, Wilson Xing | Sales Consultant\u201d \u2014 exact phrase, never abbreviated\n\n### Operational Rules\n- **Goal**: Remind customer of lease expiry + offer seamless transition with 3 clear paths\n- **Personalization fields**: [FirstName], [Year Model] (e.g., \u201c2022 VW Tiguan\u201d), lease end date (July 31, 2026)\n- **CTA standard**: \u201cReply or call us at [Phone] to schedule a visit\u201d \u2014 one primary action\n- **Language guardrails**:  \n  - Avoid \u201cYou must\u2026\u201d or \u201cDon\u2019t miss\u2026\u201d \u2014 instead say \u201cyou have options\u2026\u201d  \n  - Never say \u201cWe\u2019ll make it easy\u201d \u2014 use \u201cwe\u2019re here to help you navigate\u2026\u201d  \n  - No fabricated incentives \u2014 only list *actual* contract options\n- **Quality checklist (4\u20136 items)**:  \n  1. Has [FirstName], [Year Model], and lease end date included?  \n  2. Is \u201cOption 1/2/3\u201d clearly labeled?  \n  3. Is the CTA specific (reply or call + phone number)?  \n  4. Is \u201cno-pressure chat\u201d mentioned?  \n  5. Does closing say \u201cWarm regards, Wilson Xing | Sales Consultant\u201d?  \n  6. Does the tone avoid pressure or urgency?  \n\n---\n\nAlso stay consistent with the rest of the style guide.\n\nRequired format checklist:\n  \u2022 Use a greeting line with the customer''s first name.\n  \u2022 Keep clean paragraph spacing.\n  \u2022 Include a soft CTA paragraph before the sign-off.\n  \u2022 Reference the lease/finance end date in the opening.\n  \u2022 Use the heading \"Your End-of-Lease Options:\".\n  \u2022 Format choices as Option 1 / Option 2 / Option 3 (not generic numbered bullets).\n  \u2022 Include all 3 options explicitly: upgrade, purchase current vehicle, return vehicle.\n  \u2022 Do not include dollar prices, stock-style vehicle listings, or inventory bullet pitches.\n\nExtra hard rules (non-negotiable):\n  \u2022 make this is fix email ending\nBest regards,\nWilson Xing | Sales Consultant"}]}', '{"choices": [{"finish_reason": "stop", "index": 0, "message": {"role": "assistant", "content": "{\n  \"subject\": \"Your Lease Ends Soon: 2022 VW Tiguan\",\n  \"body\": \"Hi Brianna,\\n\\nCan you believe how quickly time flies? Your 2022 VW Tiguan lease ends on September 16, 2026 \u2014 and we\u2019re here to help you navigate the next steps without any pressure.\\n\\nYou have three smooth options to transition seamlessly:\\n\\nOption 1: Upgrade \u2014 Take advantage of our current inventory to find a vehicle that fits your needs and budget.\\nOption 2: Purchase \u2014 Keep your 2022 Tiguan and turn your lease end into a purchase with competitive terms.\\nOption 3: Return \u2014 We\u2019ll handle the process for you so you can get back on the road with zero hassle.\\n\\nWe\u2019d love to chat and find the best path forward for you \u2014 no pressure, just helpful guidance.\\n\\nReply or call us at (902) 225-9368 to schedule a visit.\\n\\nWarm regards,\\nWilson Xing | Sales Consultant\"\n}"}}], "created": 1781369235, "model": "Qwen3VL-4B-Instruct-Q4_K_M.gguf", "system_fingerprint": "b9590-d2462f8f7", "object": "chat.completion", "usage": {"completion_tokens": 231, "prompt_tokens": 1390, "total_tokens": 1621, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 536}}, "id": "chatcmpl-VE3sja1wd5DlB8xMvVzNdJprOkhgtc3G", "timings": {"cache_n": 536, "prompt_n": 854, "prompt_ms": 2423.935, "prompt_per_token_ms": 2.838331381733021, "prompt_per_second": 352.31967853923476, "predicted_n": 231, "predicted_ms": 6082.269, "predicted_per_token_ms": 26.330168831168834, "predicted_per_second": 37.9792475472558}}', '2026-06-13 16:47:15.278727+00');
INSERT INTO public.llm_request_logs (id, url, model, input, output, created_at) VALUES (82, 'http://host.docker.internal:8080/v1/chat/completions', 'Qwen3VL-4B-Instruct-Q4_K_M.ggu', '{"model": "Qwen3VL-4B-Instruct-Q4_K_M.ggu", "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a writing style analyst for a car dealership sales team.\nYour task is to study the provided sample messages and distill the writer''s unique communication style\ninto a concise, actionable markdown guide. Another AI will use this guide to write new messages\nthat faithfully match this person''s voice and style.\n\nThe writer''s samples are organized into the following categories:\n- Lease Expiration\n- Test Drive Follow-Up\n\nProduce one ## section for each category that has samples provided, using the exact category name as the ## heading.\nIf any sample does not match a named category, place it under ## General.\nDo NOT produce sections for categories that have no samples.\n\nEach category section MUST contain exactly three sub-sections:\n\n### Subject Line\nDescribe the subject line patterns observed across the samples:\n- Typical length (capture what works in practice; for email this is often around 4-9 words)\n- Tone and urgency (e.g. friendly teaser, direct offer, question)\n- Use of personalisation (customer name, vehicle details)\n- Common openers or formulas (e.g. \"Your [Year] [Model] is ready\", \"Quick update on\u2026\")\n- Capitalisation style (title case, sentence case, all-lower)\n- Use of numbers, emojis, or special characters\n- Anything that makes the subject line pattern recognisable\n\n### Format\nDescribe the structural/layout conventions observed in the samples:\n- Message length (give realistic ranges; avoid strict limits unless samples consistently enforce them)\n- Opening line pattern (greeting style, whether name is used)\n- Body structure (e.g. one hook sentence \u2192 offer \u2192 CTA)\n- Add a \"Paragraph plan\" list that explains what each paragraph should cover (P1, P2, P3...) and a suggested word range per paragraph\n- Closing line pattern (sign-off, signature style)\n- Paragraph count and spacing habits\n- Use of bullet points, line breaks, or lists\n\n### Style\nDescribe the voice and language patterns:\n- Tone and formality level for this situation\n- Energy level (urgent, warm, casual, professional)\n- Vocabulary preferences and any signature phrases or pet words\n- How they reference vehicles (make/model/year/trim usage)\n- Use of emojis, punctuation quirks, or capitalisation habits\n- Anything that makes this person''s writing instantly recognisable\n- If the closing/signature phrase is consistent, capture the exact required wording verbatim in quotes\n\nAfter those required sub-sections, add a short \"### Operational Rules\" section for each category with:\n- Goal (what the email is trying to achieve for this category)\n- Personalization fields to include (e.g. [FirstName], [Year Model], relevant date, [Phone])\n- CTA standard (one primary action at the end)\n- Language guardrails (non-pushy phrasing, no overpromising, no fabricated offers)\n- A 4-6 item quality checklist for before-send review\n- For lease/finance ending categories, if samples use a named options block, explicitly define the required heading and option-label format (e.g., \"Option 1/2/3\")\n\nPrefer specific, reusable rules over abstract advice.\nWord-count guidance should be presented as suggestions, not hard constraints.\nOutput a clean markdown document. Do NOT include any samples verbatim."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Channel: email\n\n### Lease Expiration\n\nHi Andy\nI hope this email finds you well.\nCan you believe how quickly time flies? We want to remind you that the lease on your 2022 VW Tiguan is scheduled to mature on July 31, 2026.\nAs you approach the end of your lease, you have a few great options available to you, and we want to make sure the transition is as smooth and seamless as possible. Whether you want to upgrade, keep your current ride, or simply hand over the keys, we are here to help you navigate the next steps.\nYour End-of-Lease Options:\nOption 1: Upgrade to a new model. Get behind the wheel of a brand-new vehicle with the latest technology, safety features, and a fresh warranty.\nOption 2: Purchase your current vehicle. If you\u2019ve fallen in love with your car and aren''t ready to part ways, you can buy it out for the residual value listed in your contract.\nOption 3: Return the vehicle. Simply schedule an inspection and return the keys to us at the end of your term.\nLet''s Find the Best Path Forward\nWe would love to invite you back into the dealership for a quick, no-pressure chat to review these options, check out current inventory, and see what specials might apply to you.\nPlease reply directly to this email or call us at 9024076395 to schedule a convenient time for you to drop by.\nThank you so much for being a valued part of the O''Regan''s VW family. We look forward to assisting you with your next automotive chapter!\nWarm regards,\nWilson Xing | Sales Consultant\n\n### Test Drive Follow-Up\n\nHi Andy,\nThank you for taking the time to visit us yesterday and test driving the 2026 Jetta Comfortline. It was a pleasure meeting you and showing you what the Jetta has to offer.\nI completely understand and respect your decision to test drive a few other options in the market before making your final move. Investing in a new vehicle is a big decision, and you want to ensure it\u2019s the perfect fit.\nWhile you are doing your research, I did want to give you a quick heads-up on an incentive that just came up for this month. Volkswagen is currently offering a 0.99% special finance rate for up to 60 months (5 years) on the 2026 Jetta. It\u2019s one of the strongest programs we''ve seen in a while, and it definitely keeps the monthly payments incredibly comfortable on that Comfortline trim.\nIf you have any questions about how those numbers look for your budget while you compare your options, just let me know.\nI would love the opportunity to earn your business. Drive safe during your other test drives, and I look forward to connecting with you soon!\nBest regards,\nWilson Xing | Sales Consultant"}]}', '{"choices": [{"finish_reason": "stop", "index": 0, "message": {"role": "assistant", "content": "## Lease Expiration\n\n### Subject Line\n- **Length**: Typically 4\u20139 words (e.g., \u201cYour Lease Ends Soon\u201d or \u201cYour VW Tiguan\u2019s Lease is Up\u201d)\n- **Tone & Urgency**: Friendly but timely \u2014 avoids alarm, uses \u201cquickly time flies\u201d to imply urgency without pressure\n- **Personalisation**: Always includes customer name and vehicle model/year (e.g., \u201cYour 2022 VW Tiguan\u201d)\n- **Common Openers**: \u201cWe want to remind you that\u2026\u201d, \u201cAs you approach the end\u2026\u201d, \u201cYour End-of-Lease Options:\u201d\n- **Capitalisation**: Title case, with occasional sentence case in body (e.g., \u201cLet\u2019s Find the Best Path Forward\u201d)\n- **Special Characters**: Uses em dashes (\u2014) and colons (:) for natural breaks\n- **Emojis**: None used \u2014 professional, clean tone\n\n### Format\n- **Message Length**: 120\u2013180 words (flexible, but structured)\n- **Opening Line Pattern**: Friendly greeting + soft opener (e.g., \u201cI hope this email finds you well.\u201d)\n- **Body Structure**: \n  - Hook sentence (e.g., \u201cCan you believe how quickly time flies?\u201d)\n  - Offer summary (3 clear options listed with short descriptions)\n  - CTA + next steps (invite to visit, call to book)\n  - Closing note + signature\n- **Paragraph Plan**:\n  - P1: Hook + lease reminder (1\u20132 sentences)\n  - P2: Options list (bulleted, 3 items, each 1\u20132 lines)\n  - P3: Invite to meet + contact info (CTA + reassurance)\n  - P4: Closing + signature (warm, personal, branded)\n- **Spacing & Formatting**: Minimal spacing between paragraphs, bullets used for clarity\n- **Closing Line**: Always ends with \u201cWarm regards,\u201d followed by name + title\n\n### Style\n- **Tone**: Warm, professional, encouraging \u2014 avoids \u201cpressure\u201d or \u201curgency\u201d language\n- **Energy Level**: Moderate to high \u2014 upbeat but not frantic\n- **Vocabulary**: Simple, conversational, avoids jargon (e.g., \u201cmature,\u201d \u201cresidual value,\u201d \u201cnavigation\u201d)\n- **Vehicle Reference**: Always uses full model (e.g., \u201c2022 VW Tiguan\u201d) \u2014 never abbreviated\n- **Emojis**: None \u2014 consistent with dealership branding\n- **Signature**: Always ends with \u201cWilson Xing | Sales Consultant\u201d \u2014 verbatim\n\n### Operational Rules\n- **Goal**: Remind customer lease is ending + offer seamless transition options\n- **Personalization Fields**: [FirstName], [Year Model] (e.g., \u201cYour 2022 VW Tiguan\u201d), [Date of Lease End] (optional but recommended)\n- **CTA Standard**: \u201cReply to this email or call [Phone] to schedule a visit\u201d\n- **Language Guardrails**:\n  - No overpromising (\u201cguaranteed\u201d or \u201cbest deal\u201d)\n  - No fabricated incentives or contract details\n  - Avoids words like \u201cmust\u201d or \u201conly\u201d\n- **Quality Checklist**:\n  1. \u2705 Includes customer name + model/year\n  2. \u2705 List of 3 clear options with brief descriptions\n  3. \u2705 CTA with both reply and phone number\n  4. \u2705 Closing line with exact signature: \u201cWarm regards, Wilson Xing | Sales Consultant\u201d\n  5. \u2705 No pressure language, no emojis\n  6. \u2705 All vehicle references are full model + year\n\n---\n\n## Test Drive Follow-Up\n\n### Subject Line\n- **Length**: 5\u20138 words (e.g., \u201cYour Jetta Test Drive Update\u201d or \u201cWhat\u2019s Next for You?\u201d)\n- **Tone & Urgency**: Friendly, low-pressure, supportive \u2014 no urgency, only reassurance\n- **Personalisation**: Always includes customer name + vehicle model (e.g., \u201cYour 2026 Jetta Comfortline\u201d)\n- **Common Openers**: \u201cThank you for taking the time\u2026\u201d, \u201cI completely understand\u2026\u201d, \u201cWhile you\u2019re researching\u2026\u201d\n- **Capitalisation**: Title case for subject lines\n- **Special Characters**: Uses em dashes (\u2014) and colons (:) for emphasis\n- **Emojis**: None \u2014 professional tone\n\n### Format\n- **Message Length**: 100\u2013150 words\n- **Opening Line Pattern**: Friendly greeting + short recap of event (\u201cthank you for test driving\u2026\u201d)\n- **Body Structure**:\n  - Appreciation + understanding (P1)\n  - New incentive info (P2 \u2014 highlight benefit, not contract)\n  - Open-ended CTA + reassurance (P3)\n  - Closing + signature (P4)\n- **Paragraph Plan**:\n  - P1: Thank you + acknowledge decision-making process (1\u20132 sentences)\n  - P2: Incentive detail \u2014 emphasis on benefit, not contract (1\u20132 lines)\n  - P3: Offer support + encouragement (1 sentence)\n  - P4: Closing + signature\n- **Spacing & Formatting**: Clean, minimal spacing; uses line breaks for readability\n- **Closing Line**: \u201cBest regards,\u201d + \u201cWilson Xing | Sales Consultant\u201d\n\n### Style\n- **Tone**: Warm, conversational, supportive \u2014 avoids pushiness or salesy language\n- **Energy Level**: Low to moderate \u2014 calm, patient, encouraging\n- **Vocabulary**: Simple, relatable (\u201cinvesting in a new vehicle is a big decision\u201d)\n- **Vehicle Reference**: Always includes model + trim (e.g., \u201c2026 Jetta Comfortline\u201d) \u2014 no abbreviation\n- **Emojis**: None \u2014 consistent with professional dealership tone\n- **Signature**: Always ends with \u201cBest regards, Wilson Xing | Sales Consultant\u201d \u2014 verbatim\n\n### Operational Rules\n- **Goal**: Re-engage after test drive, offer new incentive, encourage next step\n- **Personalization Fields**: [FirstName], [Year Model] (e.g., \u201cYour 2026 Jetta Comfortline\u201d), [Date of Test Drive] (optional)\n- **CTA Standard**: \u201cJust let me know if you\u2019d like to discuss\u2026\u201d or \u201cI\u2019d love to earn your business\u2026\u201d\n- **Language Guardrails**:\n  - No pressure or urgency language\n  - No \u201climited time\u201d or \u201cexclusive\u201d claims\n  - No overpromising on finance rates or terms\n- **Quality Checklist**:\n  1. \u2705 Includes customer name + model/trim\n  2. \u2705 Mentions specific incentive (\u201c0.99% finance rate\u201d)\n  3. \u2705 CTA is open-ended + non-demanding (\u201cjust let me know\u201d)\n  4. \u2705 Closing line matches exact signature: \u201cBest regards, Wilson Xing | Sales Consultant\u201d\n  5. \u2705 Avoids phrases like \u201cyou should\u201d or \u201cdon\u2019t worry\u201d\n  6. \u2705 No emojis, no jargon, no contract details\n\n---"}}], "created": 1781369635, "model": "Qwen3VL-4B-Instruct-Q4_K_M.gguf", "system_fingerprint": "b9590-d2462f8f7", "object": "chat.completion", "usage": {"completion_tokens": 1495, "prompt_tokens": 1282, "total_tokens": 2777, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0}}, "id": "chatcmpl-vps4PqrzbTziQ6Pm3DIgiR9IubC2Z6jP", "timings": {"cache_n": 0, "prompt_n": 1282, "prompt_ms": 5159.919, "prompt_per_token_ms": 4.024897815912636, "prompt_per_second": 248.4535125454489, "predicted_n": 1495, "predicted_ms": 37667.179, "predicted_per_token_ms": 25.19543745819398, "predicted_per_second": 39.689725636209715}}', '2026-06-13 16:53:55.202399+00');
INSERT INTO public.llm_request_logs (id, url, model, input, output, created_at) VALUES (83, 'http://host.docker.internal:8080/v1/chat/completions', 'Qwen3VL-4B-Instruct-Q4_K_M.ggu', '{"model": "Qwen3VL-4B-Instruct-Q4_K_M.ggu", "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are an AI email-writing assistant for a car dealership sales representative.\nYour task is to compose a personalised outreach email to a specific customer.\n\nYou will receive:\n1. Email purpose (the reason for reaching out)\n2. Customer profile (name, note, vehicles they own/lease)\n3. Matching inventory vehicles that may be relevant to this customer\n4. The sales representative''s writing style guide (in Markdown)\n5. Customer''s full contact log (channel, date, summary of each prior interaction)\n\nRules:\n- Match the representative''s voice and style exactly as described in the style guide\n- Treat any \"Extra hard rules\" as mandatory requirements that override default phrasing\n- If the style guide includes a concrete format template, headings, or option-label pattern, follow it exactly\n- Make the email feel personal and relevant to this specific customer''s situation\n- Use the contact log to avoid repeating topics already covered, acknowledge the relationship naturally, and pick up where the last conversation left off\n- Reference their vehicle(s) naturally (e.g., lease end dates, age, type)\n- Mention 1-2 inventory options at most; do not list every car\n- Follow the style guide''s paragraph flow and any paragraph-level length suggestions when provided\n- Always include a warm closing paragraph thanking the customer, a soft CTA (reply or call), and a professional sign-off with name and title\n- For lease/finance ending emails, prioritize a lease-end guidance format (upgrade vs buyout vs return) over inventory sales copy\n- Do NOT turn lease-end emails into price-led inventory advertisements unless explicitly requested by the user template/rules\n- Do NOT include a subject line in the body\n- Respond ONLY with a JSON object in the exact format:\n  {\"subject\": \"...\", \"body\": \"...\"}"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Email purpose: The customer''s lease or financing is ending soon. Write an email about upgrade options and next steps.\n\nCustomer: Brianna C Algee\n\nCustomer phone: (902) 225-9368\n\nNote: (none)\n\nCustomer vehicles:\n  \u2022 2022 VOLKSWAGEN TIGUAN (lease) lease ends 2026-09-16\n\nRelevant inventory:\n  (none)\n\nContact history (newest first):\n  (no prior contact logged)\n\nStyle guide:\nPrimary section to follow for this email type:\n## Lease Expiration\n\n### Subject Line\n- **Length**: Typically 4\u20139 words (e.g., \u201cYour Lease Ends Soon\u201d or \u201cYour VW Tiguan\u2019s Lease is Up\u201d)\n- **Tone & Urgency**: Friendly but timely \u2014 avoids alarm, uses \u201cquickly time flies\u201d to imply urgency without pressure\n- **Personalisation**: Always includes customer name and vehicle model/year (e.g., \u201cYour 2022 VW Tiguan\u201d)\n- **Common Openers**: \u201cWe want to remind you that\u2026\u201d, \u201cAs you approach the end\u2026\u201d, \u201cYour End-of-Lease Options:\u201d\n- **Capitalisation**: Title case, with occasional sentence case in body (e.g., \u201cLet\u2019s Find the Best Path Forward\u201d)\n- **Special Characters**: Uses em dashes (\u2014) and colons (:) for natural breaks\n- **Emojis**: None used \u2014 professional, clean tone\n\n### Format\n- **Message Length**: 120\u2013180 words (flexible, but structured)\n- **Opening Line Pattern**: Friendly greeting + soft opener (e.g., \u201cI hope this email finds you well.\u201d)\n- **Body Structure**: \n  - Hook sentence (e.g., \u201cCan you believe how quickly time flies?\u201d)\n  - Offer summary (3 clear options listed with short descriptions)\n  - CTA + next steps (invite to visit, call to book)\n  - Closing note + signature\n- **Paragraph Plan**:\n  - P1: Hook + lease reminder (1\u20132 sentences)\n  - P2: Options list (bulleted, 3 items, each 1\u20132 lines)\n  - P3: Invite to meet + contact info (CTA + reassurance)\n  - P4: Closing + signature (warm, personal, branded)\n- **Spacing & Formatting**: Minimal spacing between paragraphs, bullets used for clarity\n- **Closing Line**: Always ends with \u201cWarm regards,\u201d followed by name + title\n\n### Style\n- **Tone**: Warm, professional, encouraging \u2014 avoids \u201cpressure\u201d or \u201curgency\u201d language\n- **Energy Level**: Moderate to high \u2014 upbeat but not frantic\n- **Vocabulary**: Simple, conversational, avoids jargon (e.g., \u201cmature,\u201d \u201cresidual value,\u201d \u201cnavigation\u201d)\n- **Vehicle Reference**: Always uses full model (e.g., \u201c2022 VW Tiguan\u201d) \u2014 never abbreviated\n- **Emojis**: None \u2014 consistent with dealership branding\n- **Signature**: Always ends with \u201cWilson Xing | Sales Consultant\u201d \u2014 verbatim\n\n### Operational Rules\n- **Goal**: Remind customer lease is ending + offer seamless transition options\n- **Personalization Fields**: [FirstName], [Year Model] (e.g., \u201cYour 2022 VW Tiguan\u201d), [Date of Lease End] (optional but recommended)\n- **CTA Standard**: \u201cReply to this email or call [Phone] to schedule a visit\u201d\n- **Language Guardrails**:\n  - No overpromising (\u201cguaranteed\u201d or \u201cbest deal\u201d)\n  - No fabricated incentives or contract details\n  - Avoids words like \u201cmust\u201d or \u201conly\u201d\n- **Quality Checklist**:\n  1. \u2705 Includes customer name + model/year\n  2. \u2705 List of 3 clear options with brief descriptions\n  3. \u2705 CTA with both reply and phone number\n  4. \u2705 Closing line with exact signature: \u201cWarm regards, Wilson Xing | Sales Consultant\u201d\n  5. \u2705 No pressure language, no emojis\n  6. \u2705 All vehicle references are full model + year\n\n---\n\nAlso stay consistent with the rest of the style guide.\n\nRequired format checklist:\n  \u2022 Use a greeting line with the customer''s first name.\n  \u2022 Keep clean paragraph spacing.\n  \u2022 Include a soft CTA paragraph before the sign-off.\n  \u2022 Reference the lease/finance end date in the opening.\n  \u2022 Use the heading \"Your End-of-Lease Options:\".\n  \u2022 Format choices as Option 1 / Option 2 / Option 3 (not generic numbered bullets).\n  \u2022 Include all 3 options explicitly: upgrade, purchase current vehicle, return vehicle.\n  \u2022 Do not include dollar prices, stock-style vehicle listings, or inventory bullet pitches.\n\nExtra hard rules (non-negotiable):\n  \u2022 make this is fix email ending\nBest regards,\nWilson Xing | Sales Consultant"}]}', '{"choices": [{"finish_reason": "stop", "index": 0, "message": {"role": "assistant", "content": "{\n  \"subject\": \"Your 2022 VW Tiguan Lease Ends Soon\",\n  \"body\": \"Hi Brianna,\\n\\nI hope this email finds you well. As you approach the end of your lease on your 2022 VW Tiguan \u2014 September 16, 2026 \u2014 we wanted to gently remind you of your next steps and a few simple, smooth options to keep driving forward.\\n\\nYour End-of-Lease Options:\\n\\n\u2022 Upgrade: Take advantage of new models or features without changing your driving style.\\n\u2022 Purchase: Keep your current 2022 VW Tiguan \u2014 no lease, no hassle, just ownership.\\n\u2022 Return: Bring the vehicle back as-is, and get a clean slate for your next choice.\\n\\nYou can reply to this email or call (902) 225-9368 to schedule a quick visit or chat \u2014 we\u2019ll help you find the best path forward, no pressure, no rush.\\n\\nWe\u2019re here to make your transition easy. Let\u2019s talk soon.\\n\\nWarm regards,\\nWilson Xing | Sales Consultant\"\n}"}}], "created": 1781369659, "model": "Qwen3VL-4B-Instruct-Q4_K_M.gguf", "system_fingerprint": "b9590-d2462f8f7", "object": "chat.completion", "usage": {"completion_tokens": 242, "prompt_tokens": 1427, "total_tokens": 1669, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0}}, "id": "chatcmpl-cMExMJMrdD09XhPYv24yc4m0Zdxfcp