 "prompt_ms": 96.605, "prompt_per_token_ms": 96.605, "prompt_per_second": 10.35143108534755, "predicted_n": 223, "predicted_ms": 5732.717, "predicted_per_token_ms": 25.707251121076233, "predicted_per_second": 38.899530536742006}}', '2026-06-13 16:56:36.200849+00');
INSERT INTO public.llm_request_logs (id, url, model, input, output, created_at) VALUES (85, 'http://host.docker.internal:8080/v1/chat/completions', 'Qwen3VL-4B-Instruct-Q4_K_M.ggu', '{"model": "Qwen3VL-4B-Instruct-Q4_K_M.ggu", "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a writing style analyst for a car dealership sales team.\nYour task is to study the provided sample messages and distill the writer''s unique communication style\ninto a concise, actionable markdown guide. Another AI will use this guide to write new messages\nthat faithfully match this person''s voice and style.\n\nThe writer''s samples are organized into the following categories:\n- Lease Expiration\n- Test Drive Follow-Up\n\nProduce one ## section for each category that has samples provided, using the exact category name as the ## heading.\nIf any sample does not match a named category, place it under ## General.\nDo NOT produce sections for categories that have no samples.\n\nEach category section MUST contain exactly three sub-sections:\n\n### Subject Line\nDescribe the subject line patterns observed across the samples:\n- Typical length (capture what works in practice; for email this is often around 4-9 words)\n- Tone and urgency (e.g. friendly teaser, direct offer, question)\n- Use of personalisation (customer name, vehicle details)\n- Common openers or formulas (e.g. \"Your [Year] [Model] is ready\", \"Quick update on\u2026\")\n- Capitalisation style (title case, sentence case, all-lower)\n- Use of numbers, emojis, or special characters\n- Anything that makes the subject line pattern recognisable\n\n### Format\nDescribe the structural/layout conventions observed in the samples:\n- Message length (give realistic ranges; avoid strict limits unless samples consistently enforce them)\n- Opening line pattern (greeting style, whether name is used)\n- Body structure (e.g. one hook sentence \u2192 offer \u2192 CTA)\n- Add a \"Paragraph plan\" list that explains what each paragraph should cover (P1, P2, P3...) and a suggested word range per paragraph\n- Closing line pattern (sign-off, signature style)\n- Paragraph count and spacing habits\n- Use of bullet points, line breaks, or lists\n\n### Style\nDescribe the voice and language patterns:\n- Tone and formality level for this situation\n- Energy level (urgent, warm, casual, professional)\n- Vocabulary preferences and any signature phrases or pet words\n- How they reference vehicles (make/model/year/trim usage)\n- Use of emojis, punctuation quirks, or capitalisation habits\n- Anything that makes this person''s writing instantly recognisable\n- If the closing/signature phrase is consistent, capture the exact required wording verbatim in quotes\n\nAfter those required sub-sections, add a short \"### Operational Rules\" section for each category with:\n- Goal (what the email is trying to achieve for this category)\n- Personalization fields to include (e.g. [FirstName], [Year Model], relevant date, [Phone])\n- CTA standard (one primary action at the end)\n- Language guardrails (non-pushy phrasing, no overpromising, no fabricated offers)\n- A 4-6 item quality checklist for before-send review\n- For lease/finance ending categories, if samples use a named options block, explicitly define the required heading and option-label format (e.g., \"Option 1/2/3\")\n\nPrefer specific, reusable rules over abstract advice.\nWord-count guidance should be presented as suggestions, not hard constraints.\nOutput a clean markdown document. Do NOT include any samples verbatim."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Channel: email\n\n### Lease Expiration\n\nHi Andy\nI hope this email finds you well.\nCan you believe how quickly time flies? We want to remind you that the lease on your 2022 VW Tiguan is scheduled to mature on July 31, 2026.\nAs you approach the end of your lease, you have a few great options available to you, and we want to make sure the transition is as smooth and seamless as possible. Whether you want to upgrade, keep your current ride, or simply hand over the keys, we are here to help you navigate the next steps.\nYour End-of-Lease Options:\nOption 1: Upgrade to a new model. Get behind the wheel of a brand-new vehicle with the latest technology, safety features, and a fresh warranty.\nOption 2: Purchase your current vehicle. If you\u2019ve fallen in love with your car and aren''t ready to part ways, you can buy it out for the residual value listed in your contract.\nOption 3: Return the vehicle. Simply schedule an inspection and return the keys to us at the end of your term.\nLet''s Find the Best Path Forward\nWe would love to invite you back into the dealership for a quick, no-pressure chat to review these options, check out current inventory, and see what specials might apply to you.\nPlease reply directly to this email or call us at 9024076395 to schedule a convenient time for you to drop by.\nThank you so much for being a valued part of the O''Regan''s VW family. We look forward to assisting you with your next automotive chapter!\nWarm regards,\nWilson Xing | Sales Consultant\n\n### Test Drive Follow-Up\n\nHi Andy,\nThank you for taking the time to visit us yesterday and test driving the 2026 Jetta Comfortline. It was a pleasure meeting you and showing you what the Jetta has to offer.\nI completely understand and respect your decision to test drive a few other options in the market before making your final move. Investing in a new vehicle is a big decision, and you want to ensure it\u2019s the perfect fit.\nWhile you are doing your research, I did want to give you a quick heads-up on an incentive that just came up for this month. Volkswagen is currently offering a 0.99% special finance rate for up to 60 months (5 years) on the 2026 Jetta. It\u2019s one of the strongest programs we''ve seen in a while, and it definitely keeps the monthly payments incredibly comfortable on that Comfortline trim.\nIf you have any questions about how those numbers look for your budget while you compare your options, just let me know.\nI would love the opportunity to earn your business. Drive safe during your other test drives, and I look forward to connecting with you soon!\nBest regards,\nWilson Xing | Sales Consultant"}]}', '{"choices": [{"finish_reason": "stop", "index": 0, "message": {"role": "assistant", "content": "## Lease Expiration\n\n### Subject Line\n- **Length**: 4\u20139 words (often 6\u20138 words for maximum impact)\n- **Tone**: Friendly, slightly urgent, with a touch of warmth\n- **Personalisation**: Uses customer\u2019s name and vehicle details (e.g., \u201cyour 2022 VW Tiguan\u201d)\n- **Openers**: \u201cCan you believe how quickly time flies?\u201d or \u201cWe want to remind you\u2026\u201d \u2014 casual, conversational, relatable\n- **Capitalisation**: Title case for most subject lines (e.g., \u201cYour Lease is Upcoming!\u201d)\n- **Emojis/Numbers**: Rarely used; numbers are used sparingly for dates (e.g., \u201cJuly 31, 2026\u201d)\n- **Pattern Recognition**: Uses \u201cend-of-lease\u201d or \u201clease maturing\u201d as a hook, often followed by a warm, helpful tone\n\n### Format\n- **Length**: 5\u20137 paragraphs (average 150\u2013250 words)\n- **Opening Line**: Friendly, personalized greeting + casual opener (e.g., \u201cHi Andy, I hope this email finds you well.\u201d)\n- **Body Structure**:\n  - P1: Hook with time-sensitive reminder + vehicle reference\n  - P2: Transition to options + reassurance of support\n  - P3: List of 3 clear, numbered options (Option 1/2/3)\n  - P4: Soft CTA with \u201cno-pressure\u201d framing\n  - P5: Closing with appreciation + signature\n- **Paragraph Plan**:\n  - P1: Reminder + vehicle reference + gentle urgency\n  - P2: Reassurance + \u201cwe\u2019re here to help\u201d framing\n  - P3: 3 bullet-point options (clear, action-oriented, with benefit highlights)\n  - P4: CTA to schedule a visit or call (no pressure, flexible)\n  - P5: Warm closing + dealership loyalty line\n- **Closing Line**: \u201cWarm regards,\u201d + full name/title verbatim (e.g., \u201cWilson Xing | Sales Consultant\u201d)\n- **Spacing**: Minimal spacing between paragraphs, tight and professional\n\n### Style\n- **Tone**: Warm, professional, conversational \u2014 avoids over-the-top sales pitch\n- **Energy Level**: Moderate urgency, high empathy \u2014 \u201cno-pressure\u201d is a key phrase\n- **Vocabulary**: Uses \u201cend-of-lease,\u201d \u201ctransition,\u201d \u201cnavigate,\u201d \u201cseamless,\u201d \u201cworthwhile\u201d \u2014 avoids jargon\n- **Vehicle Reference**: Always specifies model, year, and trim (e.g., \u201c2022 VW Tiguan\u201d)\n- **Emojis/Punctuation**: No emojis; uses dashes, colons, and commas for rhythm; minimal exclamation\n- **Signature Phrase**: \u201cWarm regards,\u201d + \u201cWilson Xing | Sales Consultant\u201d \u2014 consistent, unchanging\n\n---\n\n### Operational Rules\n\n- **Goal**: Remind customer of lease expiration, offer clear next steps, and invite a low-pressure consult.\n- **Personalization Fields**: `[FirstName]`, `[Year Model]`, `[Date]` (optional), `[Phone]`\n- **CTA Standard**: \u201cReply or call us at [Phone] to schedule a visit\u201d \u2014 no pressure, flexible\n- **Language Guardrails**:\n  - No overpromising or fabricated offers (e.g., \u201cbest deal in town\u201d \u2192 avoid)\n  - No guilt-tripping or pressure (e.g., \u201cdon\u2019t miss out\u201d \u2192 replace with \u201cwe\u2019re here to help\u201d)\n  - Avoid \u201curgent\u201d or \u201climited time\u201d unless explicitly stated (in samples, only \u201ctime flies\u201d is used)\n- **Quality Checklist (4\u20136 items)**:\n  1. Does the subject line include customer name + vehicle model?\n  2. Are all 3 options clearly labeled (Option 1/2/3) with simple, benefit-driven descriptions?\n  3. Is the CTA actionable and non-pushy (\u201creply or call\u201d not \u201cact now\u201d)?\n  4. Does the closing line contain exact signature phrase (e.g., \u201cWilson Xing | Sales Consultant\u201d)?\n  5. Is the tone warm, not salesy, and includes \u201cwe\u2019re here to help\u201d?\n  6. Are all vehicle details (model, year, trim) accurate and referenced?\n\n---\n\n## Test Drive Follow-Up\n\n### Subject Line\n- **Length**: 4\u20139 words (often 7\u20138 words)\n- **Tone**: Friendly, slightly encouraging, with a \u201cyou\u2019re doing good\u201d vibe\n- **Personalisation**: Uses customer\u2019s name + specific vehicle (e.g., \u201cyour 2026 Jetta Comfortline\u201d)\n- **Openers**: \u201cHi Andy,\u201d or \u201cThank you for taking the time\u2026\u201d \u2014 warm, conversational\n- **Capitalisation**: Title case (e.g., \u201cThank You for Testing Drive!\u201d)\n- **Emojis/Numbers**: Occasionally uses \u201c0.99%\u201d for rate, but no emojis\n- **Pattern Recognition**: Uses \u201ctest drive\u201d as a reference point + \u201cwe\u2019re here to help\u201d framing\n\n### Format\n- **Length**: 4\u20136 paragraphs (average 120\u2013200 words)\n- **Opening Line**: Personalised greeting + acknowledgment of visit\n- **Body Structure**:\n  - P1: Thank you + warm intro (\u201cIt was a pleasure\u2026\u201d)\n  - P2: Acknowledge customer\u2019s research + show respect for their decision\n  - P3: Introduce incentive (with numbers + benefit)\n  - P4: Soft CTA + \u201cno rush\u201d framing\n  - P5: Closing + \u201clook forward to connecting\u201d\n- **Paragraph Plan**:\n  - P1: Thank you + warm intro + reference to visit\n  - P2: Validate customer\u2019s decision + show understanding\n  - P3: Introduce incentive (with specific rate, term, trim)\n  - P4: Offer to answer questions + no pressure\n  - P5: Closing + \u201clook forward to connecting\u201d\n- **Closing Line**: \u201cBest regards,\u201d + full name/title verbatim (e.g., \u201cWilson Xing | Sales Consultant\u201d)\n- **Spacing**: Tight, conversational, no formal spacing\n\n### Style\n- **Tone**: Warm, professional, slightly conversational \u2014 \u201cI completely understand\u2026\u201d\n- **Energy Level**: Low pressure, high empathy \u2014 \u201cno rush,\u201d \u201cinvesting in a new vehicle is a big decision\u201d\n- **Vocabulary**: Uses \u201cyou\u2019re doing your research,\u201d \u201cperfect fit,\u201d \u201ccomfortable on that trim\u201d \u2014 avoids salesy terms\n- **Vehicle Reference**: Always includes model, year, trim (e.g., \u201c2026 Jetta Comfortline\u201d)\n- **Emojis/Punctuation**: No emojis; uses dashes, colons, and commas for rhythm; minimal exclamation\n- **Signature Phrase**: \u201cBest regards,\u201d + \u201cWilson Xing | Sales Consultant\u201d \u2014 consistent, unchanging\n\n---\n\n### Operational Rules\n\n- **Goal**: Follow up after test drive, offer incentive, and invite further contact without pressure\n- **Personalization Fields**: `[FirstName]`, `[Year Model]`, `[Trim]`, `[Phone]`\n- **CTA Standard**: \u201cJust let me know\u201d or \u201cI\u2019d love to earn your business\u201d \u2014 low-pressure, open-ended\n- **Language Guardrails**:\n  - No pressure language (e.g., \u201cact now\u201d \u2192 replace with \u201clet me know\u201d)\n  - No overpromising (e.g., \u201cbest deal\u201d \u2192 avoid)\n  - No fabricated offers (e.g., \u201cexclusive rate\u201d \u2192 only use if confirmed)\n- **Quality Checklist (4\u20136 items)**:\n  1. Does the subject line include customer name + vehicle model?\n  2. Is the incentive clearly stated with numbers (e.g., \u201c0.99% for 60 months\u201d)?\n  3. Is the CTA open-ended and low-pressure (\u201cjust let me know\u201d vs. \u201cact now\u201d)?\n  4. Does the closing line contain exact signature phrase (e.g., \u201cWilson Xing | Sales Consultant\u201d)?\n  5. Is the tone warm, not salesy, and includes \u201cyou\u2019re doing good\u201d framing?\n  6. Are all vehicle details (model, year, trim) accurate and referenced?"}}], "created": 1781370589, "model": "Qwen3VL-4B-Instruct-Q4_K_M.gguf", "system_fingerprint": "b9590-d2462f8f7", "object": "chat.completion", "usage": {"completion_tokens": 1764, "prompt_tokens": 1282, "total_tokens": 3046, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 1281}}, "id": "chatcmpl-Bh5zf51B72n7FnsSYdZiB7UpWu1MRDNt", "timings": {"cache_n": 1281, "prompt_n": 1, "prompt_ms": 1480.471, "prompt_per_token_ms": 1480.471, "prompt_per_second": 0.675460714867093, "predicted_n": 1764, "predicted_ms": 47098.552, "predicted_per_token_ms": 26.69985941043084, "predicted_per_second": 37.453380732384296}}', '2026-06-13 17:09:49.255787+00');
INSERT INTO public.llm_request_logs (id, url, model, input, output, created_at) VALUES (86, 'http://host.docker.internal:8080/v1/chat/completions', 'Qwen3VL-4B-Instruct-Q4_K_M.ggu', '{"model": "Qwen3VL-4B-Instruct-Q4_K_M.ggu", "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are an AI email-writing assistant for a car dealership sales representative.\nYour task is to compose a personalised outreach email to a specific customer.\n\nYou will receive:\n1. Email purpose (the reason for reaching out)\n2. Customer profile (name, note, vehicles they own/lease)\n3. Matching inventory vehicles that may be relevant to this customer\n4. The sales representative''s writing style guide (in Markdown)\n5. Customer''s full contact log (channel, date, summary of each prior interaction)\n\nRules:\n- Match the representative''s voice and style exactly as described in the style guide\n- Treat any \"Extra hard rules\" as mandatory requirements that override default phrasing\n- If the style guide includes a concrete format template, headings, or option-label pattern, follow it exactly\n- Make the email feel personal and relevant to this specific customer''s situation\n- Use the contact log to avoid repeating topics already covered, acknowledge the relationship naturally, and pick up where the last conversation left off\n- Reference their vehicle(s) naturally (e.g., lease end dates, age, type)\n- Mention 1-2 inventory options at most; do not list every car\n- Follow the style guide''s paragraph flow and any paragraph-level length suggestions when provided\n- Always include a warm closing paragraph thanking the customer, a soft CTA (reply or call), and a professional sign-off with name and title\n- For lease/finance ending emails, prioritize a lease-end guidance format (upgrade vs buyout vs return) over inventory sales copy\n- Do NOT turn lease-end emails into price-led inventory advertisements unless explicitly requested by the user template/rules\n- Do NOT include a subject line in the body\n- Respond ONLY with a JSON object in the exact format:\n  {\"subject\": \"...\", \"body\": \"...\"}"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Email purpose: The customer''s lease or financing is ending soon. Write an email about upgrade options and next steps.\n\nCustomer: Brianna C Algee\n\nCustomer phone: (902) 225-9368\n\nNote: (none)\n\nCustomer vehicles:\n  \u2022 2022 VOLKSWAGEN TIGUAN (lease) lease ends 2026-09-16\n\nRelevant inventory:\n  (none)\n\nContact history (newest first):\n  (no prior contact logged)\n\nStyle guide:\nPrimary section to follow for this email type:\n## Lease Expiration\n\n### Subject Line\n- **Length**: 4\u20139 words (often 6\u20138 words for maximum impact)\n- **Tone**: Friendly, slightly urgent, with a touch of warmth\n- **Personalisation**: Uses customer\u2019s name and vehicle details (e.g., \u201cyour 2022 VW Tiguan\u201d)\n- **Openers**: \u201cCan you believe how quickly time flies?\u201d or \u201cWe want to remind you\u2026\u201d \u2014 casual, conversational, relatable\n- **Capitalisation**: Title case for most subject lines (e.g., \u201cYour Lease is Upcoming!\u201d)\n- **Emojis/Numbers**: Rarely used; numbers are used sparingly for dates (e.g., \u201cJuly 31, 2026\u201d)\n- **Pattern Recognition**: Uses \u201cend-of-lease\u201d or \u201clease maturing\u201d as a hook, often followed by a warm, helpful tone\n\n### Format\n- **Length**: 5\u20137 paragraphs (average 150\u2013250 words)\n- **Opening Line**: Friendly, personalized greeting + casual opener (e.g., \u201cHi Andy, I hope this email finds you well.\u201d)\n- **Body Structure**:\n  - P1: Hook with time-sensitive reminder + vehicle reference\n  - P2: Transition to options + reassurance of support\n  - P3: List of 3 clear, numbered options (Option 1/2/3)\n  - P4: Soft CTA with \u201cno-pressure\u201d framing\n  - P5: Closing with appreciation + signature\n- **Paragraph Plan**:\n  - P1: Reminder + vehicle reference + gentle urgency\n  - P2: Reassurance + \u201cwe\u2019re here to help\u201d framing\n  - P3: 3 bullet-point options (clear, action-oriented, with benefit highlights)\n  - P4: CTA to schedule a visit or call (no pressure, flexible)\n  - P5: Warm closing + dealership loyalty line\n- **Closing Line**: \u201cWarm regards,\u201d + full name/title verbatim (e.g., \u201cWilson Xing | Sales Consultant\u201d)\n- **Spacing**: Minimal spacing between paragraphs, tight and professional\n\n### Style\n- **Tone**: Warm, professional, conversational \u2014 avoids over-the-top sales pitch\n- **Energy Level**: Moderate urgency, high empathy \u2014 \u201cno-pressure\u201d is a key phrase\n- **Vocabulary**: Uses \u201cend-of-lease,\u201d \u201ctransition,\u201d \u201cnavigate,\u201d \u201cseamless,\u201d \u201cworthwhile\u201d \u2014 avoids jargon\n- **Vehicle Reference**: Always specifies model, year, and trim (e.g., \u201c2022 VW Tiguan\u201d)\n- **Emojis/Punctuation**: No emojis; uses dashes, colons, and commas for rhythm; minimal exclamation\n- **Signature Phrase**: \u201cWarm regards,\u201d + \u201cWilson Xing | Sales Consultant\u201d \u2014 consistent, unchanging\n\n---\n\n### Operational Rules\n\n- **Goal**: Remind customer of lease expiration, offer clear next steps, and invite a low-pressure consult.\n- **Personalization Fields**: `[FirstName]`, `[Year Model]`, `[Date]` (optional), `[Phone]`\n- **CTA Standard**: \u201cReply or call us at [Phone] to schedule a visit\u201d \u2014 no pressure, flexible\n- **Language Guardrails**:\n  - No overpromising or fabricated offers (e.g., \u201cbest deal in town\u201d \u2192 avoid)\n  - No guilt-tripping or pressure (e.g., \u201cdon\u2019t miss out\u201d \u2192 replace with \u201cwe\u2019re here to help\u201d)\n  - Avoid \u201curgent\u201d or \u201climited time\u201d unless explicitly stated (in samples, only \u201ctime flies\u201d is used)\n- **Quality Checklist (4\u20136 items)**:\n  1. Does the subject line include customer name + vehicle model?\n  2. Are all 3 options clearly labeled (Option 1/2/3) with simple, benefit-driven descriptions?\n  3. Is the CTA actionable and non-pushy (\u201creply or call\u201d not \u201cact now\u201d)?\n  4. Does the closing line contain exact signature phrase (e.g., \u201cWilson Xing | Sales Consultant\u201d)?\n  5. Is the tone warm, not salesy, and includes \u201cwe\u2019re here to help\u201d?\n  6. Are all vehicle details (model, year, trim) accurate and referenced?\n\n---\n\nAlso stay consistent with the rest of the style guide.\n\nRequired format checklist:\n  \u2022 Use a greeting line with the customer''s first name.\n  \u2022 Keep clean paragraph spacing.\n  \u2022 Include a soft CTA paragraph before the sign-off.\n  \u2022 Reference the lease/finance end date in the opening.\n  \u2022 Use the heading \"Your End-of-Lease Options:\".\n  \u2022 Format choices as Option 1 / Option 2 / Option 3 (not generic numbered bullets).\n  \u2022 Include all 3 options explicitly: upgrade, purchase current vehicle, return vehicle.\n  \u2022 Do not include dollar prices, stock-style vehicle listings, or inventory bullet pitches.\n\nExtra hard rules (non-negotiable):\n  \u2022 make this is fix email ending\nBest regards,\nWilson Xing | Sales Consultant"}]}', '{"choices": [{"finish_reason": "stop", "index": 0, "message": {"role": "assistant", "content": "{\n  \"subject\": \"Your 2022 VW Tiguan Lease Ends Sept 16\",\n  \"body\": \"Hi Brianna,\\n\\nCan you believe how quickly time flies? Your 2022 VW Tiguan lease ends on September 16 \u2014 and we\u2019re here to help you make the next move feel smooth, not stressful.\\n\\nWe know you\u2019ve got a lot going on, and we\u2019re ready to walk you through your options without any pressure. Whether you\u2019re looking to upgrade, keep your ride, or return it \u2014 we\u2019ve got you covered.\\n\\nYour End-of-Lease Options:\\n\\nOption 1: Upgrade Your Ride \u2014 Take advantage of our new inventory to explore a vehicle that fits your lifestyle, budget, and preferences. We\u2019ll show you how to transition seamlessly into a new model.\\n\\nOption 2: Purchase Your Current Vehicle \u2014 If you want to keep your 2022 VW Tiguan, we\u2019ll help you navigate the best purchase price and terms based on its current condition and market value.\\n\\nOption 3: Return Your Vehicle \u2014 We\u2019ll make sure your return is hassle-free and we\u2019ll guide you through the process so you can get back on the road with no surprises.\\n\\nNo need to rush \u2014 just reply or call us at (902) 225-9368 to schedule a visit or chat. We\u2019re here to help you decide what\u2019s right for you, no matter which path you choose.\\n\\nWarm regards,\\nWilson Xing | Sales Consultant\"\n}"}}], "created": 1781370745, "model": "Qwen3VL-4B-Instruct-Q4_K_M.gguf", "system_fingerprint": "b9590-d2462f8f7", "object": "chat.completion", "usage": {"completion_tokens": 328, "prompt_tokens": 1579, "total_tokens": 1907, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 511}}, "id": "chatcmpl-0t7nqw0MLz5gqFFAXZ18uGWYzwmzDEAO", "timings": {"cache_n": 511, "prompt_n": 1068, "prompt_ms": 3054.143, "prompt_per_token_ms": 2.859684456928839, "prompt_per_second": 349.688930740964, "predicted_n": 328, "predicted_ms": 8604.306, "predicted_per_token_ms": 26.23264024390244, "predicted_per_second": 38.12044806402748}}', '2026-06-13 17:12:25.925901+00');
INSERT INTO public.llm_request_logs (id, url, model, input, output, created_at) VALUES (87, 'http://host.docker.internal:8080/v1/chat/completions', 'Qwen3VL-4B-Instruct-Q4_K_M.ggu', '{"model": "Qwen3VL-4B-Instruct-Q4_K_M.ggu", "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "if customer had/interested in Tiguan or other USV, remind them rav4 wait time is 4 month long\n\nYou MUST respond with ONLY a JSON object in exactly this format (no extra text, no markdown fences):\n{\"triggered\": true/false, \"alert\": \"...\", \"suggestion\": \"...\"}\nSet \"triggered\" to true only when the check genuinely applies to this customer. If triggered is false, \"alert\" and \"suggestion\" may be empty strings."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Knowledge base:\ntoyota rav 4 wait time 4 month\n\nCustomer deal history:\n{\"customer_name\": \"Brianna C Algee\", \"phone\": \"(902) 225-9368\", \"email\": \"briallgee@gmail.com\", \"note\": null, \"deals\": [{\"deal_type\": \"lease\", \"contract_date\": \"2022-09-16\", \"make\": \"VOLKSWAGEN\", \"model\": \"TIGUAN\", \"model_year\": 2022, \"trim\": \"COMFORTLINE\", \"trim_package\": \"R-LINE BLACK EDITION\", \"selling_price\": \"42340.00\", \"rate_pct\": \"5.99\", \"term\": 48, \"payment_frequency\": \"biweekly\", \"payment_amount\": \"253.29\", \"cash_down\": \"8781.75\"}]}"}], "max_tokens": 400}', '{"choices": [{"finish_reason": "stop", "index": 0, "message": {"role": "assistant", "content": "{\"triggered\": true, \"alert\": \"Customer previously leased a Volkswagen Tiguan, so they may be interested in other USVs.\", \"suggestion\": \"Note that the Toyota RAV4 wait time is currently 4 months.\"}"}}], "created": 1781619815, "model": "Qwen3VL-4B-Instruct-Q4_K_M.gguf", "system_fingerprint": "b9590-d2462f8f7", "object": "chat.completion", "usage": {"completion_tokens": 50, "prompt_tokens": 319, "total_tokens": 369, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0}}, "id": "chatcmpl-AvUHWPq7IlP90QzTO6yQnPeeSnBHwdkt", "timings": {"cache_n": 0, "prompt_n